["constant","When sent by a client, this method changes the description of the session. <literal>ANNOUNCE<\/literal> acts like an HTTP PUT or POST just like <constant>CURL_RTSPREQ_SET_PARAMETER<\/constant>. Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Used to get the low level description of a stream. The application should note what formats it understands in the <literal>Accept:<\/literal> header. Unless set manually, libcurl automatically adds in <literal>Accept: application\/sdp<\/literal>. Time-condition headers are added to DESCRIBE requests if the <constant>CURLOPT_TIMECONDITION<\/constant> option is used. Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Retrieve a parameter from the server. By default, libcurl adds a <literal>Content-Type: text\/parameters<\/literal> header on all non-empty requests unless a custom one is set. <literal>GET_PARAMETER<\/literal> acts just like an HTTP PUT or POST. Applications wishing to send a heartbeat message should use an empty <literal>GET_PARAMETER<\/literal> request. Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Used to retrieve the available methods of the server. Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Send a <literal>PAUSE<\/literal> command to the server. Use the <constant>CURLOPT_RANGE<\/constant> option with a single value to indicate when the stream should be halted (e.g. npt=25). Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Send a <literal>PLAY<\/literal> command to the server. Use the <constant>CURLOPT_RANGE<\/constant> option to modify the playback time (e.g. npt=10-15). Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Set the RTSP request type to this value to receive interleaved RTP data. Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
["constant","Used to tell the server to record a session. Use the <constant>CURLOPT_RANGE<\/constant> option to modify the record time. Available as of cURL 7.20.0."]
