["function","Return time zone relative to given DateTime\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturn time zone relative to given DateTime.",[["$object","DateTimeInterface","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>"]],["DateTimeZone|false","Returns a <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>DateTime::setTimezone<\/function>"]]
["function","Alters the timestamp\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nAlter the timestamp of a DateTime object by incrementing or decrementing in a format accepted by <function>DateTimeImmutable::__construct<\/function>.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$modifier","string","A date\/time string. Valid formats are explained in Date and Time Formats."]],["DateTime","Returns <classname>DateTime<\/classname> on success. Procedural style returns <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>strtotime<\/function>","<function>DateTimeImmutable::modify<\/function>","<function>DateTime::add<\/function>","<function>DateTime::sub<\/function>","<function>DateTime::setDate<\/function>","<function>DateTime::setISODate<\/function>","<function>DateTime::setTime<\/function>","<function>DateTime::setTimestamp<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the date\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nResets the current date of the DateTime object to a different date.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::setDate but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>, and changes the existing object.\n\nThe procedural version takes the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object as its first argument.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$year","int","Year of the date."],["$month","int","Month of the date."],["$day","int","Day of the date."]],["DateTime","Returns the modified <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining."],["<function>DateTimeImmutable::setDate<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the ISO date\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSet a date according to the ISO 8601 standard - using weeks and day offsets rather than specific dates.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::setISODate but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>.\n\nThe procedural version takes the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object as its first argument.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$year","int","Year of the date."],["$week","int","Week of the date."],["$dayOfWeek","int","Offset from the first day of the week."]],["DateTime","Returns the modified <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining."],["<function>DateTimeImmutable::setISODate<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets microsecond part of the time\n\nSets microsecond part of the time.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::setMicrosecond but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>.",[["$microsecond","int","The microsecond value to set (<literal>0<\/literal> to <literal>999999<\/literal>)."]],["static","Returns the modified <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining."],["DateTimeInterface::getMicrosecond"]]
["function","Sets the time\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nResets the current time of the DateTime object to a different time.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::setTime but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>.\n\nThe procedural version takes the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object as its first argument.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$hour","int","Hour of the time."],["$minute","int","Minute of the time."],["$second","int","Second of the time."],["$microsecond","int","Microsecond of the time."]],["DateTime","Returns the modified <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining."],["<function>DateTimeImmutable::setTime<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the date and time based on an Unix timestamp\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSets the date and time based on an Unix timestamp.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::setTimestamp but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>.\n\nThe procedural version takes the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object as its first argument.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$timestamp","int","Unix timestamp representing the date. Setting timestamps outside the range of <type>int<\/type> is possible by using DateTimeImmutable::modify with the <literal>@<\/literal> format."]],["DateTime","Returns the modified <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining."],["<function>DateTimeImmutable::setTimestamp<\/function>","<function>DateTime::setMicrosecond<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the time zone for the DateTime object\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSets a new timezone for a <classname>DateTime<\/classname> <type>object<\/type>.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::setTimezone but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>.\n\nThe procedural version takes the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object as its first argument.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$timezone","DateTimeZone","A <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object representing the desired time zone."]],["DateTime","Returns the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining. The underlying point-in-time is not changed when calling this method."],["<function>DateTimeImmutable::setTimezone<\/function>","<function>DateTime::getTimezone<\/function>","<function>DateTimeZone::__construct<\/function>"]]
["function","Subtracts an amount of days, months, years, hours, minutes and seconds from\n   a DateTime object\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nModifies the specified DateTime object, by subtracting the specified <classname>DateInterval<\/classname> object.\n\nLike DateTimeImmutable::sub but works with <classname>DateTime<\/classname>.\n\nThe procedural version takes the <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object as its first argument.",[["$object","DateTime","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object returned by <function>date_create<\/function>. The function modifies this object."],["$interval","DateInterval","A <classname>DateInterval<\/classname> object"]],["DateTime","Returns the modified <classname>DateTime<\/classname> object for method chaining."],["<function>DateTimeImmutable::sub<\/function>"]]
["class","Representation of date and time.\n\nThis class behaves the same as <classname>DateTime<\/classname> except new objects are returned when modification methods such as <function>DateTime::modify<\/function> are called."]
["function","Returns new DateTimeImmutable object\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns new a DateTimeImmutable object.",[["$datetime","string","A date\/time string. Valid formats are explained in Date and Time Formats.\n\nEnter <literal>\"now\"<\/literal> here to obtain the current time when using the <parameter>timezone<\/parameter> parameter."],["$timezone","DateTimeZone|null","A <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object representing the timezone of <parameter>datetime<\/parameter>.\n\nIf <parameter>timezone<\/parameter> is omitted or <type>null<\/type>, the current timezone will be used.\n\nThe <parameter>timezone<\/parameter> parameter and the current timezone are ignored when the <parameter>datetime<\/parameter> parameter either is a UNIX timestamp (e.g. <literal>@946684800<\/literal>) or specifies a timezone (e.g. <literal>2010-01-28T15:00:00+02:00<\/literal>, or <literal>2010-07-05T06:00:00Z<\/literal>)."]],["DateTimeImmutable|false","Returns a new DateTimeImmutable instance."]]
