["function","Creates new DateTimeZone object\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nCreates a new DateTimeZone object.\n\nA DateTimeZone object provides access to three different types of timezone rules: UTC offset (type <literal>1<\/literal>), timezone abbreviation (type <literal>2<\/literal>), and timezone identifiers as published in the IANA timezone database (type <literal>3<\/literal>).\n\nThe DateTimeZone object can be attached to <classname>DateTime<\/classname> and <classname>DateTimeImmutable<\/classname> objects to be able to render the timezone encapsulated by these objects in a local timezone.",[["$timezone","string","One of the supported timezone names, an offset value (+0200), or a timezone abbreviation (BST)."]],["DateTimeZone|false","Returns <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> on success. Procedural style returns <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Returns location information for a timezone\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns location information for a timezone, including country code, latitude\/longitude and comments.",[["$object","DateTimeZone","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object returned by <function>timezone_open<\/function>"]],["array|false","Array containing location information about timezone or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>DateTimeZone::listIdentifiers<\/function> to get a full or\n   partial list of all supported timezone identifiers"]]
["function","Returns the name of the timezone\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns the name of the timezone.",[["$object","DateTimeZone","The <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> for which to get a name."]],["string","Depending on zone type, UTC offset (type 1), timezone abbreviation (type 2), and timezone identifiers as published in the IANA timezone database (type 3), the descriptor string to create a new <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object with the same offset and\/or rules. For example <literal>02:00<\/literal>, <literal>CEST<\/literal>, or one of the timezone names in the list of timezones."]]
["function","Returns the timezone offset from GMT\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nThis function returns the offset to GMT for the date\/time specified in the <parameter>datetime<\/parameter> parameter. The GMT offset is calculated with the timezone information contained in the DateTimeZone object being used.",[["$object","DateTimeZone","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object returned by <function>timezone_open<\/function>"],["$datetime","DateTimeInterface","DateTime that contains the date\/time to compute the offset from."]],["int","Returns time zone offset in seconds."]]
["function","Returns all transitions for the timezone\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style",[["$object","DateTimeZone","Procedural style only: A <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> object returned by <function>timezone_open<\/function>"],["$timestampBegin","int","Begin timestamp."],["$timestampEnd","int","End timestamp."]],["array|false",["Returns a numerically indexed array of transition arrays on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure. DateTimeZone objects wrapping type 1 (UTC offsets) and type 2 (abbreviations) do not contain any transitions, and calling this method on them will return <type>false<\/type>.","If <parameter>timestampBegin<\/parameter> is given, the first entry in the returned array will contain a transition element at the time of <parameter>timestampBegin<\/parameter>.",{"type":"table","title":"Transition Array Structure","headers":["Key","Type","Description"],"rows":[["<literal>ts<\/literal>","<type>int<\/type>","Unix timestamp"],["<literal>time<\/literal>","<type>string<\/type>","<constant>DateTimeInterface::ISO8601_EXPANDED<\/constant> (PHP 8.2 and later), or <constant>DateTimeInterface::ISO8601<\/constant> (PHP 8.1 and lower) time string"],["<literal>offset<\/literal>","<type>int<\/type>","Offset to UTC in seconds"],["<literal>isdst<\/literal>","<type>bool<\/type>","Whether daylight saving time is active"],["<literal>abbr<\/literal>","<type>string<\/type>","Timezone abbreviation"]]}]]]
["function","Returns associative array containing dst, offset and the timezone name\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nThe returned list of abbreviations includes all historical use of abbreviations, which can lead to correct, but confusing entries. There are also conflicts, as <literal>PST<\/literal> is used both in the US and in the Philippines.\n\nThe list that this function returns is therefore not suitable for building an array with options to present a choice of timezone to users.\n\nThe data for this function are precompiled for performance reasons, and are not updated when using a newer timezonedb.",null,["array","Returns the array of timezone abbreviations."],["<function>timezone_identifiers_list<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns a numerically indexed array containing all defined timezone identifiers\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturn the list of IANA Time Zone identifiers.\n\nIt's possible to detect the client (browser) timezone with JavaScript using Intl.DateTimeFormat or Temporal.ZonedDateTime.",[["$timezoneGroup","int","One of the <classname>DateTimeZone<\/classname> class constants (or a combination)."],["$countryCode","string|null","A two-letter (uppercase) ISO 3166-1 compatible country code.\n\nThis option is only used when <parameter>timezoneGroup<\/parameter> is set to <constant>DateTimeZone::PER_COUNTRY<\/constant>."]],["array","Returns the array of timezone identifiers. Only non-outdated items are returned. To get all, including outdated timezone identifiers, use the <constant>DateTimeZone::ALL_WITH_BC<\/constant> as value for <parameter>timezoneGroup<\/parameter>."],["<function>timezone_abbreviations_list<\/function>"]]
