["function","Replaces a token in the list with another one\n\nReplaces a token in the list with another one.",[["$token","string","The token to replace."],["$newToken","string","The new token."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if <parameter>token<\/parameter> was in the list, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Returns whether the given token is supported\n\nReturns whether <parameter>token<\/parameter> is in the associated attribute's supported tokens.",[["$token","string","The token."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Toggles the presence of a token in the list\n\nToggles the presence of <parameter>token<\/parameter> in the list.",[["$token","string","The token to toggle."],["$force","bool|null","If <parameter>force<\/parameter> is provided, setting it to <type>true<\/type> will add the token, and setting it to <type>false<\/type> will remove the token."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the token is in the list after the call, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["class","Represents an XML document."]
["class","Allows to use XPath 1.0 queries on HTML or XML documents.\n\nThis is the modern, spec-compliant equivalent of <classname>DOMXPath<\/classname>."]
["function","Gets a Dom\\Attr or Dom\\Element object from a\n   SimpleXMLElement object\n\nThis function takes the given attribute or element <parameter>node<\/parameter> (a <classname>SimpleXMLElement<\/classname> instance) and creates a <classname>Dom\\Attr<\/classname> or <classname>Dom\\Element<\/classname> node, respectively. The new <classname>Dom\\Node<\/classname> refers to the same underlying XML node as the <classname>SimpleXMLElement<\/classname>.",[["$node","object","The attribute or element node to import (a <classname>SimpleXMLElement<\/classname> instance)."]],["Dom\\Attr|Dom\\Element","The <classname>Dom\\Attr<\/classname> or <classname>Dom\\Element<\/classname>."],["<function>simplexml_import_dom<\/function>"]]
["class","Exception thrown if a value does not adhere to a defined valid data domain."]
["class","<classname>Collection<\/classname> is the base interface which covers functionality common to all the data structures in this library. It guarantees that all structures are traversable, countable, and can be converted to json using <function>json_encode<\/function>."]
["function","Removes all values\n\nRemoves all values from the collection.",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a shallow copy of the collection\n\nReturns a shallow copy of the collection.",null,["Ds\\Collection","Returns a shallow copy of the collection."]]
["function","Returns whether the collection is empty\n\nReturns whether the collection is empty.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the collection is empty, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Converts the collection to an array\n\nConverts the collection to an <type>array<\/type>.\n\nCasting to an <type>array<\/type> is not supported yet.",null,["array","An <type>array<\/type> containing all the values in the same order as the collection."]]
["class","A Deque (pronounced “deck”) is a sequence of values in a contiguous buffer that grows and shrinks automatically. The name is a common abbreviation of “double-ended queue” and is used internally by <classname>Ds\\Queue<\/classname>.\n\nTwo pointers are used to keep track of a head and a tail. The pointers can “wrap around” the end of the buffer, which avoids the need to move other values around to make room. This makes shift and unshift very fast —  something a <classname>Ds\\Vector<\/classname> can’t compete with.\n\nAccessing a value by index requires a translation between the index and its corresponding position in the buffer: ((head + position) % capacity)."]
["function","Creates a new instance\n\nCreates a new instance, using either a <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or an <type>array<\/type> for the initial <parameter>values<\/parameter>.",[["$values","mixed","A traversable object or an <type>array<\/type> to use for the initial values."]]]
["function","Allocates enough memory for a required capacity\n\nEnsures that enough memory is allocated for a required capacity. This removes the need to reallocate the internal buffer as values are added.",[["$capacity","int","The number of values for which capacity should be allocated.\n\nCapacity will stay the same if this value is less than or equal to the current capacity.\n\nCapacity will always be rounded up to the nearest power of 2."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Updates all values by applying a callback function to each value\n\nUpdates all values by applying a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> function to each value in the deque.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>\n\nA <type>callable<\/type> to apply to each value in the deque.\n\nThe callback should return what the value should be replaced by."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns the current capacity\n\nReturns the current capacity.",null,["int","The current capacity."]]
["function","Removes all values from the deque\n\nRemoves all values from the deque.",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Determines if the deque contains given values\n\nDetermines if the deque contains all values.",[["$values","mixed","Values to check."]],["bool","<type>false<\/type> if any of the provided <parameter>values<\/parameter> are not in the deque, <type>true<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Returns a shallow copy of the deque\n\nReturns a shallow copy of the deque.",null,["Ds\\Deque","A shallow copy of the deque."]]
["function","Returns the number of values in the collection\n\nSee <function>Countable::count<\/function>"]
["function","Creates a new deque using a callable to\n    determine which values to include\n\nCreates a new deque using a <type>callable<\/type> to determine which values to include.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>bool<\/type>\n\nOptional <type>callable<\/type> which returns <type>true<\/type> if the value should be included, <type>false<\/type> otherwise.\n\nIf a callback is not provided, only values which are <type>true<\/type> (see converting to boolean) will be included."]],["Ds\\Deque","A new deque containing all the values for which either the <parameter>callback<\/parameter> returned <type>true<\/type>, or all values that convert to <type>true<\/type> if a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> was not provided."]]
["function","Attempts to find a value's index\n\nReturns the index of the <parameter>value<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> if not found.",[["$value","mixed","The value to find."]],["mixed","The index of the value, or <type>false<\/type> if not found.\n\nValues will be compared by value and by type."]]
["function","Returns the first value in the deque\n\nReturns the first value in the deque.",null,["mixed","The first value in the deque."]]
["function","Returns the value at a given index\n\nReturns the value at a given index.",[["$index","int","The index to access, starting at 0."]],["mixed","The value at the requested index."]]
["function","Inserts values at a given index\n\nInserts values into the deque at a given index.",[["$index","int","The index at which to insert. 0 <= index <= count\n\nYou can insert at the index equal to the number of values."],["$values","mixed","The value or values to insert."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns whether the deque is empty\n\nReturns whether the deque is empty.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the deque is empty, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Joins all values together as a string\n\nJoins all values together as a string using an optional separator between each value.",[["$glue","string","An optional string to separate each value."]],["string","All values of the deque joined together as a string."]]
["function","Returns a representation that can be converted to JSON\n\nSee <function>JsonSerializable::jsonSerialize<\/function>\n\nYou should never need to call this directly."]
["function","Returns the last value\n\nReturns the last value in the deque.",null,["mixed","The last value in the deque."]]
["function","Returns the result of applying a callback to each value\n\nReturns the result of applying a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> function to each value in the deque.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>\n\nA <type>callable<\/type> to apply to each value in the deque.\n\nThe callable should return what the new value will be in the new deque."]],["Ds\\Deque","The result of applying a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> to each value in the deque.\n\nThe values of the current instance won't be affected."]]
["function","Returns the result of adding all given values to the deque\n\nReturns the result of adding all given values to the deque.",[["$values","mixed","A <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or an <type>array<\/type>."]],["Ds\\Deque","The result of adding all given values to the deque, effectively the same as adding the values to a copy, then returning that copy.\n\nThe current instance won't be affected."]]
["function","Removes and returns the last value\n\nRemoves and returns the last value.",null,["mixed","The removed last value."]]
["function","Adds values to the end of the deque\n\nAdds values to the end of the deque.",[["$values","mixed","The values to add."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Reduces the deque to a single value using a callback function\n\nReduces the deque to a single value using a callback function.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>carry<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>\n\n<parameter>carry<\/parameter> — The return value of the previous callback, or <parameter>initial<\/parameter> if it's the first iteration.\n\n<parameter>value<\/parameter> — The value of the current iteration."],["$initial","mixed","The initial value of the carry value. Can be <type>null<\/type>."]],["mixed","The return value of the final callback."]]
["function","Removes and returns a value by index\n\nRemoves and returns a value by index.",[["$index","int","The index of the value to remove."]],["mixed","The value that was removed."]]
["function","Reverses the deque in-place\n\nReverses the deque in-place.",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a reversed copy\n\nReturns a reversed copy of the deque.",null,["Ds\\Deque","A reversed copy of the deque.  The current instance is not affected. "]]
["function","Rotates the deque by a given number of rotations\n\nRotates the deque by a given number of rotations, which is equivalent to successively calling $deque->push($deque->shift()) if the number of rotations is positive, or $deque->unshift($deque->pop()) if negative.",[["$rotations","int","The number of times the deque should be rotated."]],["void","No value is returned.. The deque of the current instance will be rotated."]]
["function","Updates a value at a given index\n\nUpdates a value at a given index.",[["$index","int","The index of the value to update."],["$value","mixed","The new value."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Removes and returns the first value\n\nRemoves and returns the first value.",null,["mixed","The first value, which was removed."]]
["function","Returns a sub-deque of a given range\n\nCreates a sub-deque of a given range.",[["$index","int","The index at which the sub-deque starts.\n\nIf positive, the deque will start at that index in the deque. If negative, the deque will start that far from the end."],["$length","int","If a length is given and is positive, the resulting deque will have up to that many values in it. If the length results in an overflow, only values up to the end of the deque will be included. If a length is given and is negative, the deque will stop that many values from the end. If a length is not provided, the resulting deque will contain all values between the index and the end of the deque."]],["Ds\\Deque","A sub-deque of the given range."]]
["function","Sorts the deque in-place\n\nSorts the deque in-place, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a sorted copy\n\nReturns a sorted copy, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["Ds\\Deque","Returns a sorted copy of the deque."]]
["function","Returns the sum of all values in the deque\n\nReturns the sum of all values in the deque.\n\nArrays and objects are considered equal to zero when calculating the sum.",null,["int|float","The sum of all the values in the deque as either a <type>float<\/type> or <type>int<\/type> depending on the values in the deque."]]
["function","Converts the deque to an array\n\nConverts the deque to an <type>array<\/type>.\n\nCasting to an <type>array<\/type> is not supported yet.",null,["array","An <type>array<\/type> containing all the values in the same order as the deque."]]
["function","Adds values to the front of the deque\n\nAdds values to the front of the deque, moving all the current values forward to make room for the new values.",[["$values","mixed","The values to add to the front of the deque.  Multiple values will be added in the same order that they are passed. \n\nMultiple values will be added in the same order that they are passed."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["class","Hashable is an interface which allows objects to be used as keys. It’s an alternative to <function>spl_object_hash<\/function>, which determines an object’s hash based on its handle: this means that two objects that are considered equal by an implicit definition would not be treated as equal because they are not the same instance.\n\n<function>hash<\/function> is used to return a scalar value to be used as the object's hash value, which determines where it goes in the hash table. While this value does not have to be unique, objects which are equal must have the same hash value.\n\n<function>equals<\/function> is used to determine if two objects are equal. It's guaranteed that the comparing object will be an instance of the same class as the subject."]
["function","Determines whether an object is equal to the current instance\n\nDetermines whether another object is equal to the current instance.\n\nThis method allows objects to be used as keys in structures such as <classname>Ds\\Map<\/classname> and <classname>Ds\\Set<\/classname>, or any other lookup structure that honors this interface.\n\nIt's guaranteed that <parameter>obj<\/parameter> is an instance of the same class.\n\nIt's important that objects which are equal also have the same hash value. See <function>Ds\\Hashable::hash<\/function>.",[["$obj","object","The object to compare the current instance to, which is always an instance of the same class."]],["bool","<type>true<\/type> if equal, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Returns a scalar value to be used as a hash value\n\nReturns a scalar value to be used as the hash value of the objects.\n\nWhile the hash value does not define equality, all objects that are equal according to <function>Ds\\Hashable::equals<\/function> must have the same hash value. Hash values of equal objects don't have to be unique, for example you could just return <type>true<\/type> for all objects and nothing would break - the only implication would be that hash tables then turn into linked lists because all your objects will be hashed to the same bucket. It's therefore very important that you pick a good hash value, such as an ID or email address.\n\nThis method allows objects to be used as keys in structures such as <classname>Ds\\Map<\/classname> and <classname>Ds\\Set<\/classname>, or any other lookup structure that honors this interface.\n\nDo not pick a value that might change within the object, such as a public property. Hash table lookups would fail because the hash has changed.\n\nAll objects that are equal must have the same hash value.",null,["mixed","A scalar value to be used as this object's hash value."]]
["class","A Map is a sequential collection of key-value pairs, almost identical to an <type>array<\/type> used in a similar context. Keys can be any type, but must be unique. Values are replaced if added to the map using the same key."]
["function","Creates a new instance\n\nCreates a new instance, using either a <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or an <type>array<\/type> for the initial <parameter>values<\/parameter>.",[["$values","mixed","A traversable object or an <type>array<\/type> to use for the initial values."]]]
["function","Allocates enough memory for a required capacity\n\nAllocates enough memory for a required capacity.",[["$capacity","int","The number of values for which capacity should be allocated.\n\nCapacity will stay the same if this value is less than or equal to the current capacity.\n\nCapacity will always be rounded up to the nearest power of 2."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Updates all values by applying a callback function to each value\n\nUpdates all values by applying a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> function to each value in the map.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>key<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>\n\nA <type>callable<\/type> to apply to each value in the map.\n\nThe callback should return what the value should be replaced by."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns the current capacity\n\nReturns the current capacity.",null,["int","The current capacity."]]
["function","Removes all values\n\nRemoves all values from the map.",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a shallow copy of the map\n\nReturns a shallow copy of the map.",null,["Ds\\Map","Returns a shallow copy of the map."]]
["function","Returns the number of values in the map\n\nSee <function>Countable::count<\/function>"]
["function","Creates a new map using keys that aren't in another map\n\nReturns the result of removing all keys from the current instance that are present in a given <parameter>map<\/parameter>.\n\nA \\ B = {x ∈ A | x ∉ B}",[["$map","Ds\\Map","The map containing the keys to exclude in the resulting map."]],["Ds\\Map","The result of removing all keys from the current instance that are present in a given <parameter>map<\/parameter>."],["Complement on Wikipedia"]]
["function","Creates a new map using a callable to determine which pairs to include\n\nCreates a new map using a <type>callable<\/type> to determine which pairs to include.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>key<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>bool<\/type>\n\nOptional <type>callable<\/type> which returns <type>true<\/type> if the pair should be included, <type>false<\/type> otherwise.\n\nIf a callback is not provided, only values which are <type>true<\/type> (see converting to boolean) will be included."]],["Ds\\Map","A new map containing all the pairs for which either the <parameter>callback<\/parameter> returned <type>true<\/type>, or all values that convert to <type>true<\/type> if a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> was not provided."]]
["function","Returns the first pair in the map\n\nReturns the first pair in the map.",null,["Ds\\Pair","The first pair in the map."]]
["function","Returns the value for a given key\n\nReturns the value for a given key, or an optional default value if the key could not be found.\n\nKeys of type <type>object<\/type> are supported. If an object implements <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, equality will be determined by the object's equals function. If an object does not implement <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, objects must be references to the same instance to be considered equal.\n\nYou can also use array syntax to access values by key, eg. $map[\"key\"].\n\nBe careful when using array syntax. Scalar keys will be coerced to integers by the engine. For example, $map[\"1\"] will attempt to access int(1), while $map->get(\"1\") will correctly look up the string key.\n\nSee Arrays.",[["$key","mixed","The key to look up."],["$default","mixed","The optional default value, returned if the key could not be found."]],["mixed","The value mapped to the given <parameter>key<\/parameter>, or the <parameter>default<\/parameter> value if provided and the key could not be found in the map."]]
["function","Determines whether the map contains a given key\n\nDetermines whether the map contains a given key.",[["$key","mixed","The key to look for."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the key could be found, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Determines whether the map contains a given value\n\nDetermines whether the map contains a given value.",[["$value","mixed","The value to look for."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the value could be found, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Creates a new map by intersecting keys with another map\n\nCreates a new map containing the pairs of the current instance whose keys are also present in the given <parameter>map<\/parameter>. In other words, returns a copy of the current instance with all keys removed that are not also in the other <parameter>map<\/parameter>.\n\nA ∩ B = {x : x ∈ A ∧ x ∈ B}\n\nValues from the current instance will be kept.",[["$map","Ds\\Map","The other map, containing the keys to intersect with."]],["Ds\\Map","The key intersection of the current instance and another <parameter>map<\/parameter>."],["Intersection on Wikipedia"]]
["function","Returns whether the map is empty\n\nReturns whether the map is empty.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the map is empty, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Returns a representation that can be converted to JSON\n\nSee <function>JsonSerializable::jsonSerialize<\/function>\n\nYou should never need to call this directly."]
["function","Returns a set of the map's keys\n\nReturns a set containing all the keys of the map, in the same order.",null,["Ds\\Set","A <classname>Ds\\Set<\/classname> containing all the keys of the map."]]
["function","Sorts the map in-place by key\n\nSorts the map in-place by key, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a copy, sorted by key\n\nReturns a copy sorted by key, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["Ds\\Map","Returns a copy of the map, sorted by key."]]
["function","Returns the last pair of the map\n\nReturns the last pair of the map.",null,["Ds\\Pair","The last pair of the map."]]
["function","Returns the result of applying a callback to each value\n\nReturns the result of applying a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> function to each value of the map.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>key<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>\n\nA <type>callable<\/type> to apply to each value in the map.\n\nThe callable should return what the key will be mapped to in the resulting map."]],["Ds\\Map","The result of applying a <parameter>callback<\/parameter> to each value in the map.\n\nThe keys and values of the current instance won't be affected."]]
["function","Returns the result of adding all given associations\n\nReturns the result of associating all keys of a given <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or <type>array<\/type> with their corresponding values, combined with the current instance.\n\nValues of the current instance will be overwritten by those provided where keys are equal.",[["$values","mixed","A <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or an <type>array<\/type>."]],["Ds\\Map","The result of associating all keys of a given <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or <type>array<\/type> with their corresponding values, combined with the current instance.\n\nThe current instance won't be affected."]]
["function","Returns a sequence containing all the pairs of the map\n\nReturns a <classname>Ds\\Sequence<\/classname> containing all the pairs of the map.",null,["Ds\\Sequence","<classname>Ds\\Sequence<\/classname> containing all the pairs of the map."]]
["function","Associates a key with a value\n\nAssociates a <parameter>key<\/parameter> with a <parameter>value<\/parameter>, overwriting a previous association if one exists.\n\nKeys of type <type>object<\/type> are supported. If an object implements <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, equality will be determined by the object's equals function. If an object does not implement <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, objects must be references to the same instance to be considered equal.\n\nYou can also use array syntax to associate values by key, eg. $map[\"key\"] = $value.\n\nBe careful when using array syntax. Scalar keys will be coerced to integers by the engine. For example, $map[\"1\"] will attempt to access int(1), while $map->get(\"1\") will correctly look up the string key.\n\nSee Arrays.",[["$key","mixed","The key to associate the value with."],["$value","mixed","The value to be associated with the key."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Associates all key-value pairs of a traversable object or array\n\nAssociates all key-value <parameter>pairs<\/parameter> of a <classname>traversable<\/classname> object or <type>array<\/type>.\n\nKeys of type <type>object<\/type> are supported. If an object implements <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, equality will be determined by the object's equals function. If an object does not implement <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, objects must be references to the same instance to be considered equal.",[["$pairs","mixed","<classname>traversable<\/classname> object or <type>array<\/type>."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Reduces the map to a single value using a callback function\n\nReduces the map to a single value using a callback function.",[["$callback","callable","callback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>carry<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>key<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>value<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>\n\n<parameter>carry<\/parameter> — The return value of the previous callback, or <parameter>initial<\/parameter> if it's the first iteration.\n\n<parameter>key<\/parameter> — The key of the current iteration.\n\n<parameter>value<\/parameter> — The value of the current iteration."],["$initial","mixed","The initial value of the carry value. Can be <type>null<\/type>."]],["mixed","The return value of the final callback."]]
["function","Removes and returns a value by key\n\nRemoves and returns a value by key, or return an optional default value if the key could not be found.\n\nKeys of type <type>object<\/type> are supported. If an object implements <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, equality will be determined by the object's equals function. If an object does not implement <classname>Ds\\Hashable<\/classname>, objects must be references to the same instance to be considered equal.\n\nYou can also use array syntax to access values by key, eg. $map[\"key\"].\n\nBe careful when using array syntax. Scalar keys will be coerced to integers by the engine. For example, $map[\"1\"] will attempt to access int(1), while $map->get(\"1\") will correctly look up the string key.\n\nSee Arrays.",[["$key","mixed","The key to remove."],["$default","mixed","The optional default value, returned if the key could not be found."]],["mixed","The value that was removed, or the <parameter>default<\/parameter> value if provided and the <parameter>key<\/parameter> could not be found in the map."]]
["function","Reverses the map in-place\n\nReverses the map in-place.",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a reversed copy\n\nReturns a reversed copy of the map.",null,["Ds\\Map","A reversed copy of the map.  The current instance is not affected. "]]
["function","Returns the pair at a given positional index\n\nReturns the pair at a given zero-based <parameter>position<\/parameter>.",[["$position","int","The zero-based positional index to return."]],["Ds\\Pair","Returns the <classname>Ds\\Pair<\/classname> at the given <parameter>position<\/parameter>."]]
["function","Returns a subset of the map defined by a starting index and length\n\nReturns a subset of the map defined by a starting <parameter>index<\/parameter> and <parameter>length<\/parameter>.",[["$index","int","The index at which the range starts.\n\nIf positive, the range will start at that index in the map. If negative, the range will start that far from the end."],["$length","int","If a length is given and is positive, the resulting map will have up to that many pairs in it. If a length is given and is negative, the range will stop that many pairs from the end. If the length results in an overflow, only pairs up to the end of the map will be included. If a length is not provided, the resulting map will contain all pairs between the index and the end of the map."]],["Ds\\Map","A subset of the map defined by a starting index and length."]]
["function","Sorts the map in-place by value\n\nSorts the map in-place by value, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a copy, sorted by value\n\nReturns a copy, sorted by value using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["Ds\\Map","Returns a copy of the map, sorted by value."]]
["function","Returns the sum of all values in the map\n\nReturns the sum of all values in the map.\n\nArrays and objects are considered equal to zero when calculating the sum.",null,["int|float","The sum of all the values in the map as either a <type>float<\/type> or <type>int<\/type> depending on the values in the map."]]
["function","Converts the map to an array\n\nConverts the map to an <type>array<\/type>.\n\nMaps with non-scalar keys can't be converted to an <type>array<\/type>.\n\nAn <type>array<\/type> will treat all numeric keys as integers, eg. \"1\" and 1 as keys in the map will only result in 1 being included in the array.\n\nCasting to an <type>array<\/type> is not supported yet.",null,["array","An <type>array<\/type> containing all the values in the same order as the map."]]
["function","Creates a new map using values from the current instance and another map\n\nCreates a new map that contains the pairs of the current instance as well as the pairs of another <parameter>map<\/parameter>.\n\nA ∪ B = {x: x ∈ A ∨ x ∈ B}\n\nValues of the current instance will be overwritten by those provided where keys are equal.",[["$map","Ds\\Map","The other map, to combine with the current instance."]],["Ds\\Map","A new map containing all the pairs of the current instance as well as another <parameter>map<\/parameter>."],["Union on Wikipedia"]]
["function","Returns a sequence of the map's values\n\nReturns a sequence containing all the values of the map, in the same order.",null,["Ds\\Sequence","A <classname>Ds\\Sequence<\/classname> containing all the values of the map."]]
["function","Creates a new map using keys of either the current instance or of another map, but not of both\n\nCreates a new map containing keys of the current instance as well as another <parameter>map<\/parameter>, but not of both.\n\nA ⊖ B = {x : x ∈ (A \\ B) ∪ (B \\ A)}",[["$map","Ds\\Map","The other map."]],["Ds\\Map","A new map containing keys in the current instance as well as another <parameter>map<\/parameter>, but not in both."],["Symmetric Difference on Wikipedia"]]
["class","A pair is used by <classname>Ds\\Map<\/classname> to pair keys with values."]
["function","Creates a new instance\n\nCreates a new instance using a given <parameter>key<\/parameter> and <parameter>value<\/parameter>.",[["$key","mixed","The key."],["$value","mixed","The value."]]]
["function","Removes all values\n\nRemoves all values from the pair.",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
