["function","Returns whether the pair is empty\n\nReturns whether the pair is empty.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the pair is empty, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Returns a representation that can be converted to JSON\n\nSee <function>JsonSerializable::jsonSerialize<\/function>\n\nYou should never need to call this directly."]
["function","Converts the pair to an array\n\nConverts the pair to an <type>array<\/type>.\n\nCasting to an <type>array<\/type> is not supported yet.",null,["array","An <type>array<\/type> containing all the values in the same order as the pair."]]
["class","A PriorityQueue is very similar to a Queue. Values are pushed into the queue with an assigned priority, and the value with the highest priority will always be at the front of the queue.\n\nImplemented using a max heap.\n\n\"First in, first out\" ordering is preserved for values with the same priority.\n\nIterating over a PriorityQueue is destructive, equivalent to successive pop operations until the queue is empty."]
