["function","Sorts the set in-place\n\nSorts the set in-place, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Returns a sorted copy\n\nReturns a sorted copy, using an optional <parameter>comparator<\/parameter> function.",[["$comparator","callable","The comparison function must return an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if the first argument is considered to be respectively less than, equal to, or greater than the second.\n\ncallback(<type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>a<\/parameter>, <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>b<\/parameter>): <type>int<\/type>\n\nReturning non-integer values from the comparison function, such as <type>float<\/type>, will result in an internal cast to <type>int<\/type> of the callback's return value. So values such as <literal>0.99<\/literal> and <literal>0.1<\/literal> will both be cast to an integer value of <literal>0<\/literal>, which will compare such values as equal."]],["Ds\\Set","Returns a sorted copy of the set."]]
