["function","Prevents priority inversion\n\nPrevents priority inversion by limiting how many low-priority event callbacks can be invoked before checking for more high-priority events.\n\nAvailable since <literal>libevent 2.1.0-alpha<\/literal>.",[["$max_interval","int","An interval after which Libevent should stop running callbacks and check for more events, or <literal>0<\/literal>, if there should be no such interval."],["$max_callbacks","int","A number of callbacks after which Libevent should stop running callbacks and check for more events, or <constant>-1<\/constant>, if there should be no such limit."],["$min_priority","int","A priority below which <parameter>max_interval<\/parameter> and <parameter>max_callbacks<\/parameter> should not be enforced. If this is set to <literal>0<\/literal>, they are enforced for events of every priority; if it's set to <literal>1<\/literal>, they're enforced for events of priority <literal>1<\/literal> and above, and so on."]],["void","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["class","Represents Libevent's DNS base structure. Used to resolve DNS asynchronously, parse configuration files like resolv.conf etc."]
