["function","Creates new connection listener associated with an event base\n\nCreates new connection listener associated with an event base.",[["$base","EventBase","Associated event base."],["$cb","callable","A <type>callable<\/type> that will be invoked when new connection received."],["$data","mixed","Custom user data attached to <parameter>cb<\/parameter>."],["$flags","int","Bit mask of <literal>EventListener::OPT_*<\/literal> constants. See EventListener constants."],["$backlog","int","Controls the maximum number of pending connections that the network stack should allow to wait in a not-yet-accepted state at any time; see documentation for your system’s <literal>listen<\/literal> function for more details. If <parameter>backlog<\/parameter> is negative, Libevent tries to pick a good value for the <parameter>backlog<\/parameter> ; if it is zero, Event assumes that <literal>listen<\/literal> is already called on the socket (<parameter>target<\/parameter>)."],["$target","mixed","May be string, socket resource, or a stream associated with a socket. In case if <parameter>target<\/parameter> is a string, the string will be parsed as network address. It will be interpreted as a UNIX domain socket path, if prefixed with <literal>'unix:'<\/literal>, e.g. <literal>'unix:\/tmp\/my.sock'<\/literal>."]]]
