["function","Clips along the first path from the 8BIM profile\n\nClips along the first path from the 8BIM profile, if present.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Clips along the named paths from the 8BIM profile, if present\n\nClips along the named paths from the 8BIM profile, if present. Later operations take effect inside the path. Id may be a number if preceded with #, to work on a numbered path, e.g., \"#1\" to use the first path.\n\nThis function is currently not documented; only its argument list is available.",[["$pathname","string",""],["$inside","string",""]],["void",""]]
["function","Clips along the named paths from the 8BIM profile\n\nClips along the named paths from the 8BIM profile, if present. Later operations take effect inside the path. It may be a number if preceded with #, to work on a numbered path, e.g., \"#1\" to use the first path.",[["$pathname","string","The name of the path"],["$inside","bool","If <type>true<\/type> later operations take effect inside clipping path. Otherwise later operations take effect outside clipping path."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Makes an exact copy of the Imagick object\n\nMakes an exact copy of the Imagick object.\n\nThis function has been DEPRECATED as of imagick 3.1.0 in favour of using the clone keyword.",null,["Imagick","A copy of the Imagick object is returned."]]
["function","Replaces colors in the image\n\nReplaces colors in the image from a color lookup table. Optional second parameter to replace colors in a specific channel. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.3.6 or newer.",[["$lookup_table","Imagick","Imagick object containing the color lookup table"],["$channel","int","The Channeltype constant. When not supplied, default channels are replaced."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::adaptiveBlurImage<\/function>","<function>Imagick::motionBlurImage<\/function>","<function>Imagick::radialBlurImage<\/function>"]]
["function","Composites a set of images\n\nComposites a set of images while respecting any page offsets and disposal methods. GIF, MIFF, and MNG animation sequences typically start with an image background and each subsequent image varies in size and offset. Returns a new Imagick object where each image in the sequence is the same size as the first and composited with the next image in the sequence.",null,["Imagick","Returns a new Imagick object on success."]]
["function","Changes the color value of any pixel that matches target\n\nChanges the color value of any pixel that matches target and is an immediate neighbor.",[["$fill","mixed","ImagickPixel object containing the fill color"],["$fuzz","float","The amount of fuzz. For example, set fuzz to 10 and the color red at intensities of 100 and 102 respectively are now interpreted as the same color for the purposes of the floodfill."],["$bordercolor","mixed","ImagickPixel object containing the border color"],["$x","int","X start position of the floodfill"],["$y","int","Y start position of the floodfill"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Apply color transformation to an image\n\nApply color transformation to an image. The method permits saturation changes, hue rotation, luminance to alpha, and various other effects. Although variable-sized transformation matrices can be used, typically one uses a 5x5 matrix for an RGBA image and a 6x6 for CMYKA (or RGBA with offsets). The matrix is similar to those used by Adobe Flash except offsets are in column 6 rather than 5 (in support of CMYKA images) and offsets are normalized (divide Flash offset by 255)",[["$color_matrix","array",""]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Blends the fill color with the image\n\nBlends the fill color with each pixel in the image.",[["$colorize","mixed","ImagickPixel object or a string containing the colorize color"],["$opacity","mixed","ImagickPixel object or an float containing the opacity value. 1.0 is fully opaque and 0.0 is fully transparent."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Combines one or more images into a single image\n\nCombines one or more images into a single image. The grayscale value of the pixels of each image in the sequence is assigned in order to the specified channels of the combined image. The typical ordering would be image 1 => Red, 2 => Green, 3 => Blue, etc.",[["$channelType","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["Imagick","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Adds a comment to your image\n\nAdds a comment to your image.",[["$comment","string","The comment to add"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Returns the difference in one or more images\n\nCompares one or more images and returns the difference image.",[["$image","Imagick","Imagick object containing the image to compare."],["$channelType","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."],["$metricType","int","One of the metric type constants."]],["array","Array consisting of <literal>new_wand<\/literal> and <literal>distortion<\/literal>."]]
["function","Returns the maximum bounding region between images\n\nCompares each image with the next in a sequence and returns the maximum bounding region of any pixel differences it discovers. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.2.9 or newer.",[["$method","int","One of the layer method constants."]],["Imagick","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::optimizeImageLayers<\/function>","<function>Imagick::writeImages<\/function>","<function>Imagick::writeImage<\/function>"]]
["function","Compares an image to a reconstructed image\n\nReturns an array containing a reconstructed image and the difference between images.",[["$compare","Imagick","An image to compare to."],["$metric","int","Provide a valid metric type constant. Refer to this list of metric constants."]],["array","Returns an array containing a reconstructed image and the difference between images."]]
["function","Composite one image onto another\n\nComposite one image onto another at the specified offset. Any extra arguments needed for the compose algorithm should passed to setImageArtifact with 'compose:args' as the first parameter and the data as the second parameter.",[["$composite_object","Imagick","Imagick object which holds the composite image"],["$compose","mixed","Composite operator. See Composite Operator Constants"],["$x","int","The column offset of the composited image"],["$y","int","The row offset of the composited image"],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::setImageArtifact<\/function>"]]
["function","Change the contrast of the image\n\nEnhances the intensity differences between the lighter and darker elements of the image. Set sharpen to a value other than 0 to increase the image contrast otherwise the contrast is reduced.",[["$sharpen","bool","The sharpen value"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Enhances the contrast of a color image\n\nEnhances the contrast of a color image by adjusting the pixels color to span the entire range of colors available. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.2.9 or newer.",[["$black_point","float","The black point."],["$white_point","float","The white point."],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. <constant>Imagick::CHANNEL_ALL<\/constant>. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Applies a custom convolution kernel to the image\n\nApplies a custom convolution kernel to the image.",[["$kernel","array","The convolution kernel"],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Get the number of images\n\nReturns the number of images.",[["$mode","int","An unused argument. Currently there is a non-particularly well defined feature in PHP where calling count() on a countable object might (or might not) require this method to accept a parameter. This parameter is here to be conformant with the interface of countable, even though the param is not used."]],["int","Returns the number of images."]]
["function","Extracts a region of the image\n\nExtracts a region of the image.",[["$width","int","The width of the crop"],["$height","int","The height of the crop"],["$x","int","The X coordinate of the cropped region's top left corner"],["$y","int","The Y coordinate of the cropped region's top left corner"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Creates a crop thumbnail\n\nCreates a fixed size thumbnail by first scaling the image up or down and cropping a specified area from the center.",[["$width","int","The width of the thumbnail"],["$height","int","The Height of the thumbnail"],["$legacy","bool","Optional <type>bool<\/type> parameter. If set to true, the calculations are done with the small rounding bug that existed in Imagick before 3.4.0. If set to false, the calculations should produce the same results as the ImageMagick command-line tools."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Returns a reference to the current Imagick object\n\nReturns reference to the current imagick object with image pointer at the correct sequence.",null,["Imagick","Returns self on success."]]
["function","Displaces an image's colormap\n\nDisplaces an image's colormap by a given number of positions. If you cycle the colormap a number of times you can produce a psychedelic effect.",[["$displace","int","The amount to displace the colormap."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Deciphers an image\n\nDeciphers image that has been enciphered before. The image must be enciphered using <function>Imagick::encipherImage<\/function>. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.3.9 or newer.",[["$passphrase","string","The passphrase"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::encipherImage<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns certain pixel differences between images\n\nCompares each image with the next in a sequence and returns the maximum bounding region of any pixel differences it discovers.",null,["Imagick","Returns a new Imagick object on success."]]
["function","Delete image artifact\n\nDeletes an artifact associated with the image. The difference between image properties and image artifacts is that properties are public and artifacts are private. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.5.7 or newer.",[["$artifact","string","The name of the artifact to delete"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::setImageArtifact<\/function>","<function>Imagick::getImageArtifact<\/function>"]]
["function","Deletes an image property\n\nDeletes an image property.",[["$name","string","The name of the property to delete."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Removes skew from the image\n\nThis method can be used to remove skew from for example scanned images where the paper was not properly placed on the scanning surface. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.4.5 or newer.",[["$threshold","float","Deskew threshold"]],["bool",""]]
["function","Reduces the speckle noise in an image\n\nReduces the speckle noise in an image while preserving the edges of the original image.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Destroys the Imagick object\n\nDestroys the Imagick object and frees all resources associated with it. This method is deprecated in favour of Imagick::clear.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Displays an image\n\nThis method displays an image on a X server.",[["$servername","string","The X server name"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Displays an image or image sequence\n\nDisplays an image or image sequence on a X server.",[["$servername","string","The X server name"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Distorts an image using various distortion methods\n\nDistorts an image using various distortion methods, by mapping color lookups of the source image to a new destination image usually of the same size as the source image, unless 'bestfit' is set to <type>true<\/type>.\n\nIf 'bestfit' is enabled, and distortion allows it, the destination image is adjusted to ensure the whole source 'image' will just fit within the final destination image, which will be sized and offset accordingly. Also in many cases the virtual offset of the source image will be taken into account in the mapping.\n\nThis method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.3.6 or newer.",[["$method","int","The method of image distortion. See distortion constants"],["$arguments","array","The arguments for this distortion method"],["$bestfit","bool","Attempt to resize destination to fit distorted source"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::blurImage<\/function>","<function>Imagick::motionBlurImage<\/function>","<function>Imagick::radialBlurImage<\/function>"]]
["function","Renders the ImagickDraw object on the current image\n\nRenders the ImagickDraw object on the current image.",[["$draw","ImagickDraw","The drawing operations to render on the image."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Enhance edges within the image\n\nEnhance edges within the image with a convolution filter of the given radius. Use radius 0 and it will be auto-selected.",[["$radius","float","The radius of the operation."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Returns a grayscale image with a three-dimensional effect\n\nReturns a grayscale image with a three-dimensional effect. We convolve the image with a Gaussian operator of the given radius and standard deviation (sigma). For reasonable results, radius should be larger than sigma. Use a radius of 0 and it will choose a suitable radius for you.",[["$radius","float","The radius of the effect"],["$sigma","float","The sigma of the effect"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Enciphers an image\n\nConverts plain pixels to enciphered pixels. The image is not readable until it has been deciphered using <function>Imagick::decipherImage<\/function> This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.3.9 or newer.",[["$passphrase","string","The passphrase"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::decipherImage<\/function>"]]
["function","Improves the quality of a noisy image\n\nApplies a digital filter that improves the quality of a noisy image.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Equalizes the image histogram\n\nEqualizes the image histogram.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Applies an expression to an image\n\nApplies an arithmetic, relational, or logical expression to an image. Use these operators to lighten or darken an image, to increase or decrease contrast in an image, or to produce the \"negative\" of an image.",[["$op","int","The evaluation operator"],["$constant","float","The value of the operator"],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Exports raw image pixels\n\nExports image pixels into an array. The map defines the ordering of the exported pixels. The size of the returned array is <literal>width * height * strlen(map)<\/literal>. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.4.7 or newer.",[["$x","int","X-coordinate of the exported area"],["$y","int","Y-coordinate of the exported area"],["$width","int","Width of the exported aread"],["$height","int","Height of the exported area"],["$map","string","Ordering of the exported pixels. For example <literal>\"RGB\"<\/literal>. Valid characters for the map are R, G, B, A, O, C, Y, M, K, I and P."],["$STORAGE","int","Refer to this list of pixel type constants"]],["array","Returns an array containing the pixels values."]]
["function","Set image size\n\nComfortability method for setting image size. The method sets the image size and allows setting x,y coordinates where the new area begins. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.3.1 or newer.\n\nPrior to ImageMagick 6.5.7-8 (1623), $x was positive when shifting to the left and negative when shifting to the right, and $y was positive when shifting an image up and negative when shifting an image down. Somewhere between ImageMagick 6.3.7 (1591) and ImageMagick 6.5.7-8 (1623), the axes of $x and $y were flipped, so that $x was negative when shifting to the left and positive when shifting to the right, and $y was negative when shifting an image up and positive when shifting an image down. Somewhere between ImageMagick 6.5.7-8 (1623) and ImageMagick 6.6.9-7 (1641), the axes of $x and $y were flipped back to pre-ImageMagick 6.5.7-8 (1623) functionality.",[["$width","int","The new width"],["$height","int","The new height"],["$x","int","X position for the new size"],["$y","int","Y position for the new size"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::resizeImage<\/function>","<function>Imagick::thumbnailImage<\/function>","<function>Imagick::cropImage<\/function>"]]
["function","Applies a custom convolution kernel to the image\n\nApplies a custom convolution kernel to the image.",[["$ImagickKernel","ImagickKernel","An instance of ImagickKernel that represents either a single kernel or a linked series of kernels."],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channel constants using bitwise operators. Defaults to <constant>Imagick::CHANNEL_DEFAULT<\/constant>. Refer to this list of channel constants"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Merges a sequence of images\n\nMerges a sequence of images. This is useful for combining Photoshop layers into a single image.",null,["Imagick","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Creates a vertical mirror image\n\nCreates a vertical mirror image by reflecting the pixels around the central x-axis.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::flopimage<\/function>"]]
["function","Changes the color value of any pixel that matches target\n\nChanges the color value of any pixel that matches target and is an immediate neighbor. This method is a replacement for deprecated <function>Imagick::paintFloodFillImage<\/function>. This method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.3.8 or newer.",[["$fill","mixed","ImagickPixel object or a string containing the fill color"],["$fuzz","float","The amount of fuzz. For example, set fuzz to 10 and the color red at intensities of 100 and 102 respectively are now interpreted as the same color."],["$target","mixed","ImagickPixel object or a string containing the target color to paint"],["$x","int","X start position of the floodfill"],["$y","int","Y start position of the floodfill"],["$invert","bool","If <type>true<\/type> paints any pixel that does not match the target color."],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channel constants using bitwise operators. Defaults to <constant>Imagick::CHANNEL_DEFAULT<\/constant>. Refer to this list of channel constants"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Creates a horizontal mirror image\n\nCreates a horizontal mirror image by reflecting the pixels around the central y-axis.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."],["<function>Imagick::flipimage<\/function>"]]
["function","Implements the discrete Fourier transform (DFT)\n\nImplements the discrete Fourier transform (DFT) of the image either as a magnitude \/ phase or real \/ imaginary image pair.",[["$magnitude","bool","If true, return as magnitude \/ phase pair otherwise a real \/ imaginary image pair."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Adds a simulated three-dimensional border\n\nAdds a simulated three-dimensional border around the image. The width and height specify the border width of the vertical and horizontal sides of the frame. The inner and outer bevels indicate the width of the inner and outer shadows of the frame.",[["$matte_color","mixed","ImagickPixel object or a string representing the matte color"],["$width","int","The width of the border"],["$height","int","The height of the border"],["$inner_bevel","int","The inner bevel width"],["$outer_bevel","int","The outer bevel width"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Applies a function on the image\n\nApplies an arithmetic, relational, or logical expression to a pseudo image.\n\nSee also ImageMagick v6 Examples - Image Transformations — Function, Multi-Argument Evaluate\n\nThis method is available if Imagick has been compiled against ImageMagick version 6.4.9 or newer.",[["$function","int","Refer to this list of function constants"],["$arguments","array","Array of arguments to pass to this function."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Evaluate expression for each pixel in the image\n\nEvaluate expression for each pixel in the image. Consult The Fx Special Effects Image Operator for more information.",[["$expression","string","The expression."],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["Imagick","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Gamma-corrects an image\n\nGamma-corrects an image. The same image viewed on different devices will have perceptual differences in the way the image's intensities are represented on the screen. Specify individual gamma levels for the red, green, and blue channels, or adjust all three with the gamma parameter. Values typically range from 0.8 to 2.3.",[["$gamma","float","The amount of gamma-correction."],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Blurs an image\n\nBlurs an image. We convolve the image with a Gaussian operator of the given radius and standard deviation (sigma). For reasonable results, the radius should be larger than sigma. Use a radius of 0 and selects a suitable radius for you.",[["$radius","float","The radius of the Gaussian, in pixels, not counting the center pixel."],["$sigma","float","The standard deviation of the Gaussian, in pixels."],["$channel","int","Provide any channel constant that is valid for your channel mode. To apply to more than one channel, combine channeltype constants using bitwise operators. Refer to this list of channel constants."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
