["function","Check the distance between this color and another\n\nChecks the distance between the color described by this ImagickPixel object and that of the provided object, by plotting their RGB values on the color cube. If the distance between the two points is less than the fuzz value given, the colors are similar. This method replaces ImagickPixel::isSimilar() and correctly normalises the fuzz value to ImageMagick QuantumRange.",[["$color","ImagickPixel","The ImagickPixel object to compare this object against."],["$fuzz","float","The maximum distance within which to consider these colors as similar. The theoretical maximum for this value is the square root of three (1.732)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
["function","Returns whether two colors differ by less than the specified distance\n\nReturns true if the distance between two colors is less than the specified distance. The fuzz value should be in the range 0-QuantumRange. The maximum value represents the longest possible distance in the colorspace. e.g. from RGB(0, 0, 0) to RGB(255, 255, 255) for the RGB colorspace",[["$color","string",""],["$fuzz","string",""]],["bool",""]]
["function","Check the distance between this color and another\n\nThis function is currently not documented; only its argument list is available.\n\nChecks the distance between the color described by this ImagickPixel object and that of the provided object, by plotting their RGB values on the color cube. If the distance between the two points is less than the fuzz value given, the colors are similar. Deprecated in favour of ImagickPixel::isPixelSimilar().",[["$color","ImagickPixel","The ImagickPixel object to compare this object against."],["$fuzz","float","The maximum distance within which to consider these colors as similar. The theoretical maximum for this value is the square root of three (1.732)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success."]]
