["function","Check whether a locale uses a right-to-left writing system\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nDetermines whether a locale uses a right-to-left writing system.\n\nThis method relies on the ICU library and evaluates the dominant script associated with the locale.",[["$locale","string","The locale identifier. If empty, the default locale is used."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the locale uses a right-to-left writing system, or <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Searches the language tag list for the best match to the language\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSearches the items in <parameter>languageTag<\/parameter> for the best match to the language range specified in <parameter>locale<\/parameter> according to RFC 4647's lookup algorithm.",[["$languageTag","array","An <type>array<\/type> containing a list of language tags to compare to <parameter>locale<\/parameter>. Maximum 100 items allowed."],["$locale","string","The locale to use as the language range when matching."],["$canonicalize","bool","If true, the arguments will be converted to canonical form before matching."],["$defaultLocale","string|null","The locale to use if no match is found."]],["string|null","The closest matching language tag or default value.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_filter_matches<\/function>"]]
["function","Remove likely subtags from a locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nMinimizes a locale tag by removing subtags that can be inferred using the ICU likely subtag data. For example, <literal>en_Latn_US<\/literal> becomes <literal>en<\/literal>.",[["$locale","string","The locale to minimize."]],["string|false","Returns the locale with likely subtags removed, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["Locale::addLikelySubtags","Locale::canonicalize"]]
["function","Returns a key-value array of locale ID subtag elements\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns a key-value array of locale ID subtag elements.",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the subtag array from. Note: The 'variant' and 'private' subtags can take maximum 15 values whereas 'extlang' can take maximum 3 values. If an empty string is passed, the value returned by <function>locale_get_default<\/function> is used instead."]],["array|null","Returns an array containing a list of key-value pairs, where the keys identify the particular locale ID subtags, and the values are the associated subtag values. The array will be ordered as the locale id subtags e.g. in the locale id if variants are <literal>-varX-varY-varZ<\/literal> then the returned array will have <literal>variant0=>varX<\/literal>, <literal>variant1=>varY<\/literal>, <literal>variant2=>varZ<\/literal>.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_compose<\/function>","<function>locale_get_default<\/function>","<function>locale_set_default<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the default runtime locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSets the default runtime locale to <parameter>locale<\/parameter>. This changes the value of INTL global 'default_locale' locale identifier. UAX #35 extensions are accepted.",[["$locale","string","Is a BCP 47 compliant language tag."]],["true","Returns <type>true<\/type>."],["<function>locale_get_default<\/function>"]]
