["class","BSON type for binary data (i.e. array of bytes). Binary values also have a subtype, which is used to indicate what kind of data is in the byte array. Subtypes from zero to 127 are predefined or reserved. Subtypes from 128-255 are user-defined."]
["constant","Column data. This subtype is used for time-series collections."]
["constant","Encrypted value. This subtype is used for client-side encryption."]
["constant","Function."]
["constant","Generic binary data."]
["constant","MD5 hash. When using this type, the Binary's data should be 16 bytes in length."]
["constant","Generic binary data (deprecated in favor of <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::TYPE_GENERIC<\/constant>)."]
["constant","Universally unique identifier (deprecated in favor of <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::TYPE_UUID<\/constant>). When using this type, the Binary's data should be 16 bytes in length.\n\nHistorically, other drivers encoded values with this type based on their language conventions (e.g. varying endianness), which makes it non-portable. The PHP extension applies no special handling for encoding or decoding data with this type."]
["constant","Sensitive data. This subtype is used for sensitive data that should be excluded from server-side logging when possible."]
["constant","User-defined type. While types between 0 and 127 are predefined or reserved, types between 128 and 255 are user-defined and may be used for anything."]
["constant","Universally unique identifier. When using this type, the Binary's data should be 16 bytes in length and encoded according to RFC 4122."]
["constant","Vector data. This subtype is used to efficiently store vector data for use with MongoDB's vector search."]
["function","Construct a new Binary",[["$data","string","Binary data."],["$type","int","Unsigned 8-bit integer denoting the data's type. Defaults to <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::TYPE_GENERIC<\/constant> if not specified."]],null,["BSON Types"]]
["function","Returns the Binary's data\n\nThis method is an alias of: MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::getData.",null,["string","Returns the Binary's data."],["MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::getData","BSON Types"]]
["function","Creates a new binary with subtype MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::SUBTYPE_VECTOR from the given array and vector type",[["$vector","array","An array of values representing the vector data. The type of each value must match the type indicated by the <parameter>vectorType<\/parameter> parameter: for <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType::Float32<\/constant>, each value must be a <type>float<\/type>for <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType::Int8<\/constant>, each value must be an 8-bit <type>int<\/type>, i.e. from <literal>-127<\/literal> to <literal>128<\/literal>for <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType::PackedBit<\/constant>, each value must be a <type>bool<\/type> or 1-bit <type>int<\/type>, i.e. <literal>0<\/literal> or <literal>1<\/literal>\n\nfor <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType::Float32<\/constant>, each value must be a <type>float<\/type>\n\nfor <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType::Int8<\/constant>, each value must be an 8-bit <type>int<\/type>, i.e. from <literal>-127<\/literal> to <literal>128<\/literal>\n\nfor <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType::PackedBit<\/constant>, each value must be a <type>bool<\/type> or 1-bit <type>int<\/type>, i.e. <literal>0<\/literal> or <literal>1<\/literal>"],["$vectorType","MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType","The vector data type."]],["MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary","Returns a new Binary with subtype <constant>MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::SUBTYPE_VECTOR<\/constant>."],["MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::toArray","MongoDB\\BSON\\Binary::getVectorType","MongoDB\\BSON\\VectorType","BSON Types"]]
["function","Returns the Binary's data",null,["string","Returns the Binary's data."],["BSON Types"]]
