["function","Returns the command reply document\n\nThe reply document will be converted from BSON to PHP using the default deserialization rules (e.g. BSON documents will be converted to <type>stdClass<\/type>).",null,["object","Returns the command reply document as a <classname>stdClass<\/classname> object."],["",""]]
["function","Returns the command's request ID\n\nThe request ID is generated by the extension and may be used to associate this <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\CommandSucceededEvent<\/classname> with a previous <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\CommandStartedEvent<\/classname>.",null,["string","Returns the command's request ID."],["MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\CommandStartedEvent::getRequestId",""]]
["function","Returns the Server on which the command was executed\n\nReturns the <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Server<\/classname> on which the command was executed.",null,["MongoDB\\Driver\\Server","Returns the <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Server<\/classname> on which the command was executed."],["MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\CommandStartedEvent::getServer","MongoDB\\Driver\\Cursor::getServer","MongoDB\\Driver\\WriteResult::getServer",""]]
["function","Returns the server connection ID for the command\n\nReturns the server connection ID for the command. The server connection ID is distinct from server (i.e. <function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\CommandSucceededEvent::getServer<\/function>) and is returned in the \"connectionId\" field of a <literal>hello<\/literal> command response MongoDB 4.2+.",null,["int|null","Returns the server connection ID, or <type>null<\/type> if it is not available."]]
["function","Returns the load balancer service ID for the command\n\nWhen the driver is connected to a MongoDB cluster through a load balancer, the service ID corresponds to the <literal>serviceId<\/literal> field in the <literal>hello<\/literal> command response.",null,["MongoDB\\BSON\\ObjectId|null","Returns the load balancer service ID, or <type>null<\/type> if the driver is not connected to a load balancer."]]
["class","Classes implementing this interface may be registered as a subscriber and receive log messages from the extension. This is similar to stream-based debug logging (i.e. mongodb.debug) except that trace-level log messages are not received.\n\nAs with stream-based logging, it is only possible to register a logger globally using <function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>. The extension is not able to distinguish log messages for individual <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager<\/classname> objects."]
["constant","Critical log level. An error condition with slightly less severity. This constant exists for consistency with libmongoc; however, the extension is unlikely to use it in practice."]
["constant","Debug log level. Detailed information that may be helpful when debugging an application."]
["constant","Error log level. An error condition that the extension is unable to report through its API. This is the most severe log level in the extension."]
["constant","Info log level. High-level information about normal driver behavior."]
["constant","Message or notice log level. Indicates an event that is unusual but not problematic."]
["constant","Warning log level. Indicates a situation where undesirable application behavior may occur."]
["function","Notification method for a log message\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called for each logged message.",[["$level","int","The severity level. This will be one of the interface constants."],["$domain","string","The name of the driver component that emitted the log message."],["$message","string","The log message."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["class","Classes may implement this interface to register an event subscriber that is notified for various SDAM events. See the Server Discovery and Monitoring and SDAM Monitoring specifications for additional information."]
["function","Notification method for a server description change\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when a server's description changes. For example, a server's type changing from secondary to primary would cause its server description to change.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerChangedEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the changed server description."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerChangedEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for closing a server\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when an existing server is removed from the topology.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerClosedEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the closed server."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerClosedEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for a failed server heartbeat\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when a server heartbeat (i.e. hello command issued through server monitoring) fails.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerHeartbeatFailedEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the failed server heartbeat."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerHeartbeatFailedEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for a started server heartbeat\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when a server heartbeat (i.e. hello command issued through server monitoring) is sent to the server.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerHeartbeatStartedEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the started server heartbeat."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerHeartbeatStartedEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for a successful server heartbeat\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when a server heartbeat (i.e. hello command issued through server monitoring) succeeds.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerHeartbeatSucceededEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the successful server heartbeat."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerHeartbeatSucceededEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for opening a server\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when a new server is added to the topology.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerOpeningEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the opened server."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\ServerOpeningEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for a topology description change\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when the topology's description changes. For example, a topology discovering a new replica set primary would cause its topology description to change.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\TopologyChangedEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the changed topology description."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\TopologyChangedEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for closing the topology\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when the topology is closed.\n\nDue to the driver's connection handling and persistence behavior, this event can only be observed when a <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager<\/classname> is created with the <literal>\"disableClientPersistence\"<\/literal> driver option and freed before request shutdown (RSHUTDOWN).",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\TopologyClosedEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the closed topology."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\TopologyClosedEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
["function","Notification method for opening the topology\n\nIf the subscriber is registered, this method is called when the topology is opened.\n\nDue to the driver's connection handling and persistence behavior, this event may not be observed if a <classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager<\/classname> uses a previously persisted libmongoc client.",[["$event","MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\TopologyOpeningEvent","An event object encapsulating information about the opened topology."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<classname>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\TopologyOpeningEvent<\/classname>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Monitoring\\addSubscriber<\/function>","<function>MongoDB\\Driver\\Manager::addSubscriber<\/function>"]]
