["function","Creates SNMP instance representing session to remote SNMP agent\n\nCreates SNMP instance representing session to remote SNMP agent.",[["$version","mixed","SNMP protocol version: <constant>SNMP::VERSION_1<\/constant>, <constant>SNMP::VERSION_2C<\/constant>, <constant>SNMP::VERSION_3<\/constant>."],["$hostname","mixed",["The SNMP agent. <parameter>hostname<\/parameter> may be suffixed with optional SNMP agent port after colon. IPv6 addresses must be enclosed in square brackets if used with port. If FQDN is used for <parameter>hostname<\/parameter> it will be resolved by PHP SNMP extension, not by Net-SNMP engine. Usage of IPv6 addresses when specifying FQDN may be forced by enclosing FQDN into square brackets. Here are some examples:",{"type":"table","title":"","headers":[],"rows":[["IPv4 with default port","127.0.0.1"],["IPv6 with default port","::1 or [::1]"],["IPv4 with specific port","127.0.0.1:1161"],["IPv6 with specific port","[::1]:1161"],["FQDN with default port","host.domain"],["FQDN with specific port","host.domain:1161"],["FQDN with default port, force usage of IPv6 address","[host.domain]"],["FQDN with specific port, force usage of IPv6 address","[host.domain]:1161"]]}]],["$community","mixed","The community string, or, for <constant>SNMP::VERSION_3<\/constant>, the security name. The purpose of the <parameter>community<\/parameter> access string is SNMP version specific:\n\nSNMPv3 requires to configure security-related session parameters with the SNMP::setSecurity method."],["$timeout","mixed","The number of microseconds until the first timeout."],["$retries","mixed","The number of retries in case timeout occurs."]],null,["SNMP::close"]]
["function","Close SNMP session\n\nFrees previously allocated SNMP session object.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SNMP::__construct"]]
["function","Fetch an SNMP object\n\nFetch an SNMP object specified in <parameter>objectId<\/parameter> using GET query.",[["$objectId","array|string","The SNMP object (OID) or objects"],["$preserveKeys","bool","When <parameter>objectId<\/parameter> is an array and <parameter>preserveKeys<\/parameter> set to <type>true<\/type> keys in results will be taken exactly as in <parameter>objectId<\/parameter>, otherwise SNMP::oid_output_format property is used to determinate the form of keys."]],["mixed","Returns SNMP objects requested as string or array depending on <parameter>objectId<\/parameter> type or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["SNMP::getErrno","SNMP::getError"]]
["function","Get last error code\n\nReturns error code from last SNMP request.",null,["int","Returns one of SNMP error code values described in constants chapter."],["SNMP::getError"]]
["function","Get last error message\n\nReturns string with error from last SNMP request.",null,["string","String describing error from last SNMP request."],["SNMP::getErrno"]]
["function","Fetch an SNMP object which\n  follows the given object id\n\nFetch an SNMP object that follows specified <parameter>objectId<\/parameter>.",[["$objectId","array|string","The SNMP object (OID) or objects"]],["mixed","Returns SNMP objects requested as string or array depending on <parameter>objectId<\/parameter> type or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["SNMP::getErrno","SNMP::getError"]]
["function","Set the value of an SNMP object\n\nRequests remote SNMP agent setting the value of one or more SNMP objects specified by the <parameter>objectId<\/parameter>.",[["$objectId","array|string","The SNMP object id\n\nWhen count of OIDs in object_id array is greater than max_oids object property set method will have to use multiple queries to perform requested value updates. In this case type and value checks are made per-chunk so second or subsequent requests may fail due to wrong type or value for OID requested. To mark this a warning is raised when count of OIDs in object_id array is greater than max_oids."],["$type","array|string","The MIB defines the type of each object id. It has to be specified as a single character from the below list.\n\nIf <constant>OPAQUE_SPECIAL_TYPES<\/constant> was defined while compiling the SNMP library, the following are also valid:\n\nMost of these will use the obvious corresponding ASN.1 type. 's', 'x', 'd' and 'b' are all different ways of specifying an OCTET STRING value, and the 'u' unsigned type is also used for handling Gauge32 values.\n\nIf the MIB-Files are loaded into the MIB Tree with \"snmp_read_mib\" or by specifying it in the libsnmp config, '=' may be used as the <parameter>type<\/parameter> parameter for all object ids as the type can then be automatically read from the MIB.\n\nNote that there are two ways to set a variable of the type BITS like e.g. \"SYNTAX BITS {telnet(0), ftp(1), http(2), icmp(3), snmp(4), ssh(5), https(6)}\":\n\nUsing type \"b\" and a list of bit numbers. This method is not recommended since GET query for the same OID would return e.g. 0xF8.\n\nUsing type \"x\" and a hex number but without(!) the usual \"0x\" prefix.\n\nSee examples section for more details."],["$value","array|string","The new value."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SNMP::get"]]
["function","Configures security-related SNMPv3 session parameters\n\nsetSecurity configures security-related session parameters used in SNMP protocol version 3",[["$securityLevel","string","The security level: <literal>\"noAuthNoPriv\"<\/literal>, <literal>\"authNoPriv\"<\/literal>, or <literal>\"authPriv\"<\/literal>."],["$authProtocol","string","The authentication protocol: <literal>\"MD5\"<\/literal>, <literal>\"SHA\"<\/literal>, <literal>\"SHA256\"<\/literal>, or <literal>\"SHA512\"<\/literal>."],["$authPassphrase","string","The authentication passphrase."],["$privacyProtocol","string","The privacy protocol: <literal>\"DES\"<\/literal>, or <literal>\"AES\"<\/literal>, also accepted as <literal>\"AES128\"<\/literal>. <literal>\"AES192\"<\/literal>, <literal>\"AES192C\"<\/literal>, <literal>\"AES256\"<\/literal>, and <literal>\"AES256C\"<\/literal> are accepted when supported by the Net-SNMP library."],["$privacyPassphrase","string","The privacy passphrase."],["$contextName","string","the context name"],["$contextEngineId","string","the context EngineID"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SNMP::__construct"]]
["function","Fetch SNMP object subtree\n\nSNMP::walk is used to read SNMP subtree rooted at specified <parameter>objectId<\/parameter>.",[["$objectId","array|string","Root of subtree to be fetched"],["$suffixAsKey","bool","By default full OID notation is used for keys in output array. If set to <type>true<\/type> subtree prefix will be removed from keys leaving only suffix of object_id."],["$nonRepeaters","int","This specifies the number of supplied variables that should not be iterated over. The default is to use this value from SNMP object."],["$maxRepetitions","int","This specifies the maximum number of iterations over the repeating variables. The default is to use this value from SNMP object."]],["array|false","Returns an associative array of the SNMP object ids and their values on success or <type>false<\/type> on error. When a SNMP error occurs SNMP::getErrno and SNMP::getError can be used for retrieving error number (specific to SNMP extension, see class constants) and error message respectively."],["SNMP::getErrno","SNMP::getError"]]
