["function","Record alert log information\n\nRecord alert log information.  \"ALERT\" - Action must be taken immediately. Immediate attention should be given to relevant personnel for emergency repairs. \n\n\"ALERT\" - Action must be taken immediately. Immediate attention should be given to relevant personnel for emergency repairs.",[["$message","string","The log message."],["$content","array","The `message` contain placeholders which implementors replace with values from content array. Sush as `message` is `log info from {NAME}` and `content` is `array('NAME' => neeke)`, the log information will `log info from neeke`."],["$logger","string","The `logger` cased by the third param would be used right this right now, like a temp logger, when the function SeasLog::setLogger() called in pre content. If `logger` NULL or \"\", SeasLog will use lastest logger setted by SeasLog::setLogger."]],["bool","Return TRUE on record log information success, FALSE on failure."],["seaslog.default_template","SeasLog::debug","SeasLog::info","SeasLog::notice","SeasLog::warning","SeasLog::error","SeasLog::critical","SeasLog::emergency","SeasLog::log"]]
["function","Get log count by level, log_path and key_word\n\n`SeasLog` get count value of `grep -ai '{level}' | grep -aic '{key_word}'` use system pipe and return to PHP (array or int).",[["$level","string","String. The log information level."],["$log_path","string","String. The log information path."],["$key_word","string","String. The search key word for log information."]],["mixed","If `level` is SEASLOG_ALL or Empty, return all levels count as `array`. If `level` is SEASLOG_INFO or the other level, return count as `int`."],["SeasLog::analyzerDetail"]]
["function","Get log detail by level, log_path, key_word, start, limit, order\n\n`SeasLog` get results of `grep -ai '{level}' | grep -ai '{key_word}' | sed -n '{start},{limit}'p` use system pipe and return array to PHP.",[["$level","string","String. The log information level."],["$log_path","string","String. The log information path."],["$key_word","string","String. The search key word for log information."],["$start","int","Int. Default is `1`."],["$limit","int","Int. Default is `20`."],["$order","int","Int. Default is SEASLOG_DETAIL_ORDER_ASC. See also: SEASLOG_DETAIL_ORDER_ASCSEASLOG_DETAIL_ORDER_DESC"]],["mixed","Return results as array.  When `start`,`limit` is not NULL and in Windows, SeasLog will threw exception with message 'Param start and limit don't support Windows'. "],["SeasLog::analyzerCount"]]
["function","Manually release stream flow from logger\n\nManually release stream flow from logger. SeasLog caches the stream handle opened by the log logger to save the overhead of creating a stream. The handle will be automatically released at the end of the request. If in CLI mode, the process will also automatically release when it exits. Or you can use the following functions to manually release(manually release function needs to update SeasLog 1.8.6 or updated version).",[["$model","int","Constant int. SEASLOG_CLOSE_LOGGER_STREAM_MOD_ALLSEASLOG_CLOSE_LOGGER_STREAM_MOD_ASSIGN"],["$logger","string","The logger name."]],["bool","Return TRUE on released stream flow success, FALSE on failure."],["SeasLog::setLogger","SeasLog::getLastLogger"]]
