["function","Gets an SplFileObject object for the file\n\nCreates an <classname>SplFileObject<\/classname> <type>object<\/type> of the file. This is useful because <classname>SplFileObject<\/classname> contains additional methods for manipulating the file whereas <classname>SplFileInfo<\/classname> is only useful for gaining information, like whether the file is writable.",[["$mode","string","The mode for opening the file. See the <function>fopen<\/function> documentation for descriptions of possible modes. The default is read only."],["$useIncludePath","bool","When set to <type>true<\/type>, the filename is also searched for within the include_path"],["$context","resource|null","Refer to the context section of the manual for a description of <literal>contexts<\/literal>."]],["SplFileObject","The opened file as an <classname>SplFileObject<\/classname> <type>object<\/type>."],["<classname>SplFileObject<\/classname>","<function>stream_context_create<\/function>","<function>fopen<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the class used with SplFileInfo::openFile\n\nUse this method to set a custom class which will be used when SplFileInfo::openFile is called. The class name passed to this method must be <classname>SplFileObject<\/classname> or a class derived from <classname>SplFileObject<\/classname>.",[["$class","string","The class name to use when SplFileInfo::openFile is called."]],["void","No value is returned."],["SplFileInfo::openFile"]]
