["function","Check if the current row is valid.",null,["bool",""]]
["class",["Millisecond precision timer. The underlying implementation is based on epoll_wait and setitimer, using a min-heap data structure that supports adding a large number of timers.","In synchronous I\/O processes, such as the Manager and TaskWorker processes, it is implemented using setitimer and signals.","In asynchronous I\/O processes, it is implemented using the timeout of epoll_wait\/kevent\/poll\/select.","The underlying system does not support timers with a delay of <literal>0<\/literal>; values below <literal>1<\/literal> millisecond emit an <constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> and the call fails. This differs from languages such as Node.js. Swoole\\Event::defer may be used to achieve similar functionality.",{"type":"code","text":"<?php\nSwoole\\Event::defer(function () {\n  echo \"hello\\n\";\n});\n?>","role":"php"},"Timer Correction: The execution time of the timer callback function does not affect the timing of the next timer execution. For example, setting a tick timer of 10ms after 0.002s, the first callback will be executed at 0.012s, if the callback function takes 5ms to execute, the next timer will still trigger at 0.022s, not at 0.027s.","However, if the execution time of the timer callback function is too long, even covering the time of the next timer execution, the underlying system will perform time correction, discarding the expired behavior and triggering the timer callback at the next available time. For example, if the callback function at 0.012s takes 15ms to execute, causing the timer at 0.022s to be delayed, the timer callback will be triggered again at 0.032s.","By default, when a timer is triggered, a coroutine is automatically created to execute the callback function. This can be disabled with <function>swoole_async_set<\/function>.","Timer only works within the current process space.","Timer is purely asynchronous and incompatible with synchronous I\/O functions.","Timer execution may experience minor timing deviations."]]
["function","Execute a function after a specified time\n\nCreates a one-shot timer, which is destroyed once its callback has run. Unlike <function>sleep<\/function>, it does not block the current process.",[["$ms","int","The delay in milliseconds. Must be greater than or equal to <literal>1<\/literal>; a lower value emits an <constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> and the call fails."],["$callback","callable","The function to execute once the delay has elapsed. It is called as <literal>callback(mixed ...$params)<\/literal>. Unlike Swoole\\Timer::tick, the timer ID is not passed to the callback."],["$params","mixed","Additional values passed to <parameter>callback<\/parameter>."]],["int|false","Returns the timer ID, which can be passed to Swoole\\Timer::clear to cancel the timer before it fires. Returns <type>false<\/type> if the timer could not be created, in particular when <parameter>ms<\/parameter> is less than <literal>1<\/literal>."]]
["function","Delete a timer by ID\n\nDeletes the timer with the given ID. Only timers created by the current process can be removed; timers belonging to other processes are not visible here.",[["$timer_id","int","The timer ID returned by Swoole\\Timer::tick or Swoole\\Timer::after."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure. <type>false<\/type> is returned when no timer with this ID exists in the current process, or when the ID refers to an internal timer."]]
["function","Clear all timers in the current process.\n\nClear all timers in the current process. As of Swoole 4.4.0.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure. <type>false<\/type> is returned when no timer has been created in this process yet. Only timers created from PHP are removed; internal timers are left in place."]]
["function","Check if a timer is existed.\n\nChecks whether a timer with the given ID exists in the current process.",[["$timer_id","int","The timer ID returned by Swoole\\Timer::tick or Swoole\\Timer::after."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if a timer with this ID exists in the current process, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Get information about a timer.\n\nGet information about a timer. As of Swoole 4.4.0.",[["$timer_id","int","The timer ID returned by Swoole\\Timer::tick or Swoole\\Timer::after."]],["array|null","Returns an array describing the timer, or <type>null<\/type> if no timer with this ID exists in the current process. The array contains the following keys:\n\n<literal>exec_msec<\/literal> — The time of the next execution, in milliseconds, counted from the moment the timer subsystem was started. It is not a duration.\n\n<literal>exec_count<\/literal> — The number of times the callback has been executed. Available as of Swoole 4.8.0.\n\n<literal>interval<\/literal> — The interval of the timer, in milliseconds.\n\n<literal>round<\/literal> — The number of the timer loop round in which the timer was created.\n\n<literal>removed<\/literal> — Whether the timer has been removed."]]
["function","Get an iterator over the timers of the current process\n\nReturns an iterator over the IDs of the timers created from PHP in the current process. Timers created internally by Swoole are not listed. As of Swoole 4.4.0.",null,["Swoole\\Timer\\Iterator","Returns a <classname>Swoole\\Timer\\Iterator<\/classname> object, which extends <classname>ArrayIterator<\/classname> and yields the timer IDs as <type>int<\/type> values. The iterator is a snapshot taken when the method is called; it is empty when no timer exists."]]
["function","Set timer-related parameters\n\nSets the options used by the timers of the current process.\n\nThis method was deprecated in Swoole 4.6.0 and removed in Swoole 6.0.0. Use <function>swoole_async_set<\/function> instead.",[["$settings","array","An associative array of options. Only <literal>enable_coroutine<\/literal> is recognised: when set to <type>false<\/type>, the timer callbacks are executed directly instead of inside a newly created coroutine."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Get timer statistics.\n\nGet timer statistics. As of Swoole 4.4.0.",null,["array","Returns an array with the following keys:\n\n<literal>initialized<\/literal> — Whether the timer subsystem has been started. It is <type>false<\/type> until the first timer is created.\n\n<literal>num<\/literal> — The number of timers currently registered in the process.\n\n<literal>round<\/literal> — The current round of the timer loop."]]
["function","Set a repeating interval timer\n\nSets a timer that triggers every <parameter>ms<\/parameter> milliseconds. Unlike a timer created with Swoole\\Timer::after, it keeps triggering until it is removed with Swoole\\Timer::clear.",[["$ms","int","The interval in milliseconds. Must be greater than or equal to <literal>1<\/literal>; a lower value emits an <constant>E_WARNING<\/constant> and the call fails."],["$callback","callable","The function to execute on every tick. It is called as <literal>callback(int $timer_id, mixed ...$params)<\/literal>: the ID of the timer is passed as the first argument, followed by the values given in <parameter>params<\/parameter>."],["$params","mixed","Additional values passed to <parameter>callback<\/parameter> after the timer ID."]],["int|false","Returns the timer ID, which can be passed to Swoole\\Timer::clear. Returns <type>false<\/type> if the timer could not be created, in particular when <parameter>ms<\/parameter> is less than <literal>1<\/literal>."]]
