["class","A cross-platform, native implementation of named and unnamed event objects. Both automatic and manual event objects are supported.\n\nAn event object waits, without polling, for the object to be fired\/set. One instance waits on the event object while another instance fires\/sets the event. Event objects are useful wherever a long-running process would otherwise poll a resource (e.g. checking to see if uploaded data needs to be processed)."]
["function","Constructs a new SyncEvent object\n\nConstructs a named or unnamed event object.",[["$name","string","The name of the event if this is a named event object.\n\nIf the name already exists, it must be able to be opened by the current user that the process is running as or an exception will be thrown with a meaningless error message."],["$manual","bool","Specifies whether or not the event object must be reset manually.\n\nManual reset event objects allow all waiting processes through until the object is reset."],["$prefire","bool","Specifies whether or not to prefire (signal) the event object.\n\nOnly has impact if the calling process\/thread is the first to create the object."]],["mixed","The new <classname>SyncEvent<\/classname> object."],["SyncEvent::fire","SyncEvent::reset","SyncEvent::wait"]]
["function","Fires\/sets the event\n\nFires\/sets a <classname>SyncEvent<\/classname> object. Lets multiple threads through that are waiting if the event object was created with a manual value of <type>true<\/type>.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncEvent::reset","SyncEvent::wait"]]
["function","Resets a manual event\n\nResets a <classname>SyncEvent<\/classname> object that has been fired\/set. Only valid for manual event objects.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncEvent::fire","SyncEvent::reset","SyncEvent::wait"]]
["function","Waits for the event to be fired\/set\n\nWaits for the <classname>SyncEvent<\/classname> object to be fired.",[["$wait","int","The number of milliseconds to wait for the event to be fired. A value of -1 is infinite."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncEvent::fire"]]
["class","A cross-platform, native implementation of named and unnamed countable mutex objects.\n\nA mutex is a mutual exclusion object that restricts access to a shared resource (e.g. a file) to a single instance. Countable mutexes acquire the mutex a single time and internally track the number of times the mutex is locked. The mutex is unlocked as soon as it goes out of scope or is unlocked the same number of times that it was locked."]
["function","Constructs a new SyncMutex object\n\nConstructs a named or unnamed countable mutex.",[["$name","string","The name of the mutex if this is a named mutex object.\n\nIf the name already exists, it must be able to be opened by the current user that the process is running as or an exception will be thrown with a meaningless error message."]],["mixed","The new <classname>SyncMutex<\/classname> object."],["SyncMutex::lock","SyncMutex::unlock"]]
["function","Waits for an exclusive lock\n\nObtains an exclusive lock on a <classname>SyncMutex<\/classname> object. If the lock is already acquired, then this increments an internal counter.",[["$wait","int","The number of milliseconds to wait for the exclusive lock. A value of -1 is infinite."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncMutex::unlock"]]
["function","Unlocks the mutex\n\nDecreases the internal counter of a <classname>SyncMutex<\/classname> object. When the internal counter reaches zero, the actual lock on the object is released.",[["$all","bool","Specifies whether or not to set the internal counter to zero and therefore release the lock."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncMutex::lock"]]
["class","A cross-platform, native implementation of named and unnamed reader-writer objects.\n\nA reader-writer object allows many readers or one writer to access a resource. This is an efficient solution for managing resources where access will primarily be read-only but exclusive write access is occasionally necessary."]
["function","Constructs a new SyncReaderWriter object\n\nConstructs a named or unnamed reader-writer object.",[["$name","string","The name of the reader-writer if this is a named reader-writer object.\n\nIf the name already exists, it must be able to be opened by the current user that the process is running as or an exception will be thrown with a meaningless error message.\n\nOn Windows, <parameter>name<\/parameter> must not contain backslashes."],["$autounlock","int","Specifies whether or not to automatically unlock the reader-writer at the conclusion of the PHP script.\n\nIf an object is: A named reader-writer with an autounlock of FALSE, the object is locked for either reading or writing, and the PHP script concludes before the object is unlocked, then the underlying objects will end up in an inconsistent state."]],["mixed","The new <classname>SyncReaderWriter<\/classname> object."],["SyncReaderWriter::readlock","SyncReaderWriter::readunlock","SyncReaderWriter::writelock","SyncReaderWriter::writeunlock"]]
["function","Waits for a read lock\n\nObtains a read lock on a <classname>SyncReaderWriter<\/classname> object.",[["$wait","int","The number of milliseconds to wait for a lock. A value of -1 is infinite."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncReaderWriter::readunlock"]]
["function","Releases a read lock\n\nReleases a read lock on a <classname>SyncReaderWriter<\/classname> object.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncReaderWriter::readlock"]]
["function","Waits for an exclusive write lock\n\nObtains an exclusive write lock on a <classname>SyncReaderWriter<\/classname> object.",[["$wait","int","The number of milliseconds to wait for a lock. A value of -1 is infinite."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncReaderWriter::writeunlock"]]
["function","Releases a write lock\n\nReleases a write lock on a <classname>SyncReaderWriter<\/classname> object.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncReaderWriter::writelock"]]
["class","A cross-platform, native implementation of named and unnamed semaphore objects.\n\nA semaphore restricts access to a limited resource to a limited number of instances. Semaphores differ from mutexes in that they can allow more than one instance to access a resource at one time while a mutex only allows one instance at a time."]
["function","Constructs a new SyncSemaphore object\n\nConstructs a named or unnamed semaphore.",[["$name","string","The name of the semaphore if this is a named semaphore object.\n\nIf the name already exists, it must be able to be opened by the current user that the process is running as or an exception will be thrown with a meaningless error message."],["$initialval","int","The initial value of the semaphore. This is the number of locks that may be obtained."],["$autounlock","bool","Specifies whether or not to automatically unlock the semaphore at the conclusion of the PHP script.\n\nIf an object is: A named semaphore with an autounlock of <type>false<\/type>, the object is locked, and the PHP script concludes before the object is unlocked, then the underlying semaphore will end up in an inconsistent state."]],["mixed","The new <classname>SyncSemaphore<\/classname> object."],["SyncSemaphore::lock","SyncSemaphore::unlock"]]
["function","Decreases the count of the semaphore or waits\n\nDecreases the count of a <classname>SyncSemaphore<\/classname> object or waits until the semaphore becomes non-zero.",[["$wait","int","The number of milliseconds to wait for the semaphore. A value of -1 is infinite."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncSemaphore::unlock"]]
["function","Increases the count of the semaphore\n\nIncreases the count of a <classname>SyncSemaphore<\/classname> object.",[["$prevcount","int","Returns the previous count of the semaphore."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncSemaphore::lock"]]
["class","A cross-platform, native, consistent implementation of named shared memory objects.\n\nShared memory lets two separate processes communicate without the need for complex pipes or sockets. There are several integer-based shared memory implementations for PHP. Named shared memory is an alternative.\n\nSynchronization objects (e.g. SyncMutex) are still required to protect most uses of shared memory."]
["function","Constructs a new SyncSharedMemory object\n\nConstructs a named shared memory object.",[["$name","string","The name of the shared memory object.\n\nIf the name already exists, it must be able to be opened by the current user that the process is running as or an exception will be thrown with a meaningless error message."],["$size","int","The size, in bytes, of shared memory to reserve.\n\nThe amount of memory cannot be resized later. Request sufficient storage up front."]],["mixed","The new <classname>SyncSharedMemory<\/classname> object."],["SyncSharedMemory::first","SyncSharedMemory::size","SyncSharedMemory::write","SyncSharedMemory::read"]]
["function","Check to see if the object is the first instance system-wide of named shared memory\n\nRetrieves the system-wide first instance status of a <classname>SyncSharedMemory<\/classname> object.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["SyncSharedMemory::write","SyncSharedMemory::read"]]
["function","Copy data from named shared memory\n\nCopies data from named shared memory.",[["$start","int","The start\/offset, in bytes, to begin reading.\n\nIf the value is negative, the starting position will begin at the specified number of bytes from the end of the shared memory segment."],["$length","int","The number of bytes to read.\n\nIf unspecified, reading will stop at the end of the shared memory segment.\n\nIf the value is negative, reading will stop the specified number of bytes from the end of the shared memory segment."]],["mixed","A string containing the data read from shared memory."],["SyncSharedMemory::__construct","SyncSharedMemory::first","SyncSharedMemory::write","SyncSharedMemory::read"]]
["function","Returns the size of the named shared memory\n\nRetrieves the shared memory size of a <classname>SyncSharedMemory<\/classname> object.",null,["int","An integer containing the size of the shared memory. This will be the same size that was passed to the constructor."],["SyncSharedMemory::__construct","SyncSharedMemory::write","SyncSharedMemory::read"]]
["function","Copy data to named shared memory\n\nCopies data to named shared memory.",[["$string","string","The data to write to shared memory.\n\nIf the size of the data exceeds the size of the shared memory, the number of bytes written returned will be less than the length of the input."],["$start","int","The start\/offset, in bytes, to begin writing.\n\nIf the value is negative, the starting position will begin at the specified number of bytes from the end of the shared memory segment."]],["mixed","An integer containing the number of bytes written to shared memory."],["SyncSharedMemory::__construct","SyncSharedMemory::first","SyncSharedMemory::write","SyncSharedMemory::read"]]
