["class","Weak references allow the programmer to retain a reference to an object without preventing the object from being destroyed. They are useful for implementing cache-like structures. If the original object has been destroyed, <type>null<\/type> will be returned when calling the WeakReference::get method. The original object will be destroyed when the refcount for it drops to zero; creating weak references does not increase the <literal>refcount<\/literal> of the object being referenced.\n\n<classname>WeakReference<\/classname>s cannot be serialized."]
