["class","<classname>Yaf_Config_Simple<\/classname> is a configuration adapter backed by a PHP array (or, optionally, an INI file). In contrast to <classname>Yaf_Config_Ini<\/classname> it is mutable by default: values can be changed at runtime, which makes it suitable both for programmatically built configuration and for configuration that needs to be adjusted during the request."]
["function","Constructor of Yaf_Config_Simple\n\nCreates a new <classname>Yaf_Config_Simple<\/classname> instance from an array of configuration values.",[["$values","mixed","An array of configuration values."],["$readonly","mixed","Whether the configuration should be read-only. Defaults to <type>false<\/type> (writable)."]],["mixed","No value is returned."],["Yaf_Config_Simple::get","Yaf_Config_Simple::set","Yaf_Config_Simple::readonly"]]
