["constant","Similar to SOCKET_SUB, except you can send subscriptions as messages. See SOCKET_XPUB for format."]
["constant","Set I\/O thread affinity (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","The SOCKOPT_BACKLOG option shall set the maximum length of the queue of outstanding peer connections for the specified socket; this only applies to connection-oriented transports. (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Set a CIDR string to match against incoming TCP connections. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["constant","The high water mark for inbound and outbound messages is a hard limit on the maximum number of outstanding messages ØMQ shall queue in memory for any single peer that the specified socket is communicating with. Setting this option on a socket will only affect connections made after the option has been set. On ZeroMQ 3.x this is a wrapper for setting both SNDHWM and RCVHWM. (Value: <type>int<\/type>)."]
["constant","Set socket identity (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["constant","Disable IPV6 support if 1. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Enable IPV6. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 4.0 or higher (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["constant","Retrieve the last connected endpoint - for use with * wildcard ports. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["constant","The linger value of the socket. Specifies how long the socket blocks trying flush messages after it has been closed (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Limits the maximum size of the inbound message. Value -1 means no limit. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Control multicast loopback (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","Set rate for multicast sockets (pgm) (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","Set kernel receive buffer size (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","The SOCKOPT_RCVHWM option shall set the high water mark for inbound messages on the specified socket. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>int<\/type>)."]
["constant","Receive multi-part messages (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Sets the timeout for receive operation on the socket. Value -1 means no limit. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Set the initial reconnection interval (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","Set the max reconnection interval (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","Set multicast recovery interval (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","Sets the raw mode on the ROUTER, when set to 1. In raw mode when using tcp:\/\/ transport the socket will read and write without ZeroMQ framing. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 4.0 or higher (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["constant","Set kernel transmit buffer size (Value: <type>int<\/type> >= 0)"]
["constant","The ZMQ_SNDHWM option shall set the high water mark for outbound messages on the specified socket. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>int<\/type>)."]
["constant","Sets the timeout for send operation on the socket. Value -1 means no limit. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Establish message filter. Valid for subscriber socket (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
