["constant","Get the socket type. Valid for getSockOpt (Value: <type>int<\/type>)"]
["constant","Remove message filter. Valid for subscriber socket (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["constant","Set the XPUB to receive an application message on each instance of a subscription. Available if compiled against ZeroMQ 3.x or higher (Value: <type>string<\/type>)"]
["function","ZMQ constructor\n\nPrivate constructor to prevent direct initialization. This class holds the constants for ZMQ extension."]
["function","Construct a new ZMQContext object\n\nConstructs a new ZMQ context. The context is used to initialize sockets. A persistent context is required to initialize persistent sockets.",[["$io_threads","int","Number of io-threads in the context."],["$is_persistent","bool","Whether the context is persistent. Persistent context is stored over multiple requests and is a requirement for persistent sockets."]]]
["function","Get context option\n\nReturns the value of a context option.",[["$key","string","An integer representing the option. See the <constant>ZMQ::CTXOPT_*<\/constant> constants."]],["mixed","Returns either a <type>string<\/type> or an <type>int<\/type> depending on <parameter>key<\/parameter>. Throws ZMQContextException on error."]]
["function","Create a new socket\n\nShortcut for creating new sockets from the context. If the context is not persistent the <parameter>persistent_id<\/parameter> parameter is ignored and the socket falls back to being non-persistent. The <parameter>on_new_socket<\/parameter> is called only when a new underlying socket structure is created.",[["$type","int","<constant>ZMQ::SOCKET_*<\/constant> constant to specify socket type."],["$persistent_id","string","If <parameter>persistent_id<\/parameter> is specified the socket will be persisted over multiple requests."],["$on_new_socket","callable","Callback function, which is executed when a new socket structure is created. This function does not get invoked if the underlying persistent connection is re-used. The callback takes ZMQSocket and persistent_id as two arguments."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns a <classname>ZMQSocket<\/classname> object."]]
["function","Whether the context is persistent\n\nWhether the context is persistent. Persistent context is needed for persistent connections as each socket is allocated from a context.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the context is persistent and <type>false<\/type> if the context is non-persistent."]]
["function","Set a socket option\n\nSets a ZMQ context option. The type of the <parameter>value<\/parameter> depends on the <parameter>key<\/parameter>. See ZMQ Constant Types for more information.",[["$key","int","One of the <constant>ZMQ::CTXOPT_*<\/constant> constants."],["$value","mixed","The value of the parameter."]],["ZMQContext","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQContextException on error."]]
["function","Construct a new device\n\n\"ØMQ devices can do intermediation of addresses, services, queues, or any other abstraction you care to define above the message and socket layers.\" -- zguide",[["$frontend","ZMQSocket","Frontend parameter for the devices. Usually where there messages are coming."],["$backend","ZMQSocket","Backend parameter for the devices. Usually where there messages going to."],["$listener","ZMQSocket","Listener socket, which receives a copy of all messages going both directions. The type of this socket should be SUB, PULL or DEALER."]],["mixed","Call to this method will prepare the device. Usually devices are very long running processes so running this method from interactive script is not recommended. This method throw ZMQDeviceException if the device cannot be started."]]
["function","Get the idle timeout\n\nGets the idle callback timeout value. Added in ZMQ extension version 1.1.0.",null,["ZMQDevice","This method returns the idle callback timeout value."]]
["function","Get the timer timeout\n\nGets the timer callback timeout value. Added in ZMQ extension version 1.1.0.",null,["ZMQDevice","This method returns the timer timeout value."]]
["function","Run the new device\n\nRuns the device.",null,["void","Call to this method will block until the device is running. It is not recommended that devices are used from interactive scripts. On failure this method will throw ZMQDeviceException."]]
["function","Set the idle callback function\n\nSets the idle callback function. If idle timeout is defined the idle callback function shall be called if the internal poll loop times out without events. If the callback function returns false or a value that evaluates to false the device is stopped. The callback function signature is callback (mixed $user_data).",[["$cb_func","callable","Callback function to invoke when the device is idle. Returning false or a value that evaluates to false from this function will cause the device to stop."],["$timeout","int","How often to invoke the idle callback in milliseconds. The idle callback is invoked periodically when there is no activity on the device. The timeout value guarantees that there is at least this amount of milliseconds between invocations of the callback function."],["$user_data","mixed","Additional data to pass to the callback function."]],["ZMQDevice","On success this method returns the current object."]]
["function","Set the idle timeout\n\nSets the idle callback timeout value. The idle callback is invoked periodically when the device is idle.",[["$timeout","int","The idle callback timeout value."]],["ZMQDevice","On success this method returns the current object."]]
["function","Set the timer callback function\n\nSets the timer callback function. The timer callback will be invoked after timeout has passed. The difference between idle and timer callbacks are that idle callback is invoked only when the device is idle. The callback function signature is callback (mixed $user_data). Added in ZMQ extension version 1.1.0.",[["$cb_func","callable","Callback function to invoke when the timer fires. Returning false or a value that evaluates to false from this function will cause the device to stop."],["$timeout","int","How often to invoke the timer callback in milliseconds. The timer callback is invoked periodically. The timeout value guarantees that there is at least this amount of milliseconds between invocations of the callback function."],["$user_data","mixed","Additional data to pass to the callback function."]],["ZMQDevice","On success this method returns the current object."]]
["function","Set the timer timeout\n\nSets the timer callback timeout value. The timer callback is invoked periodically if it's set. Added in ZMQ extension version 1.1.0.",[["$timeout","int","The timer callback timeout value."]],["ZMQDevice","On success this method returns the current object."]]
["function","Add item to the poll set\n\nAdds a new item to the poll set and returns the internal id of the added item. The item can be removed from the poll set using the returned string id.",[["$entry","mixed","ZMQSocket object or a PHP stream resource"],["$type","int","Defines what activity the socket is polled for. See <constant>ZMQ::POLL_IN<\/constant> and <constant>ZMQ::POLL_OUT<\/constant> constants."]],["string","Returns a string id of the added item which can be later used to remove the item. Throws ZMQPollException on error."]]
["function","Clear the poll set\n\nClears all elements from the poll set.",null,["ZMQPoll","Returns the current object."]]
["function","Count items in the poll set\n\nCount the items in the poll set.",null,["int","Returns an <type>int<\/type> representing the amount of items in the poll set."]]
["function","Get poll errors\n\nReturns the ids of the objects that had errors in the last poll.",null,["array","Returns an array containing ids for the items that had errors in the last poll. Empty array is returned if there were no errors."]]
["function","Poll the items\n\nPolls the items in the current poll set. The readable and writable items are returned in the <parameter>readable<\/parameter> and <parameter>writable<\/parameter> parameters. <function>ZMQPoll::getLastErrors<\/function> can be used to check if there were errors.",[["$readable","array","Array where readable ZMQSockets\/PHP streams are returned. The array will be cleared at the beginning of the operation."],["$writable","array","Array where writable ZMQSockets\/PHP streams are returned. The array will be cleared at the beginning of the operation."],["$timeout","int","Timeout for the operation. -1 means that poll waits until at least one item has activity. Please note that starting from version 1.0.0 the poll timeout is defined in milliseconds, rather than microseconds."]],["int","Returns an integer representing the amount of items with activity."]]
["function","Remove item from poll set\n\nRemove item from the poll set. The <parameter>item<\/parameter> parameter can be ZMQSocket object, a stream resource or the id returned from <function>ZMQPoll::add<\/function> method.",[["$item","mixed","The ZMQSocket object, PHP stream or <type>string<\/type> id of the item."]],["bool","Returns true if the item was removed and false if the object with given id does not exist in the poll set."]]
["function","Construct a new ZMQSocket\n\nConstructs a ZMQSocket object. <parameter>persistent_id<\/parameter> parameter can be used to allocated a persistent socket. A persistent socket has to be allocated from a persistent context and it stays connected over multiple requests. The <parameter>persistent_id<\/parameter> parameter can be used to recall the same socket over multiple requests. The <parameter>on_new_socket<\/parameter> is called only when a new underlying socket structure is created.",[["$context","ZMQContext","ZMQContext object."],["$type","int","The socket type. See <constant>ZMQ::SOCKET_*<\/constant> constants."],["$persistent_id","string","If <parameter>persistent_id<\/parameter> is specified the socket will be persisted over multiple requests. If <parameter>context<\/parameter> is not persistent the socket falls back to non-persistent mode."],["$on_new_socket","callable","Callback function, which is executed when a new socket structure is created. This function does not get invoked if the underlying persistent connection is re-used.\n\ncallback(<type>ZMQSocket<\/type> <parameter>socket<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>persistent_id<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type>"]]]
["function","Bind the socket\n\nBind the socket to an endpoint. The endpoint is defined in format <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal> where transport is one of the following: inproc, ipc, tcp, pgm or epgm.",[["$dsn","string","The bind dsn, for example <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal>."],["$force","bool","Tries to bind even if the socket has already been bound to the given endpoint."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQSocketException on error."]]
["function","Connect the socket\n\nConnect the socket to a remote endpoint. The endpoint is defined in format <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal> where transport is one of the following: inproc, ipc, tcp, pgm or epgm.",[["$dsn","string","The connect dsn, for example <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal>."],["$force","bool","Tries to connect even if the socket has already been connected to given endpoint."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object."]]
["function","Disconnect a socket\n\nDisconnect the socket from a previously connected remote endpoint. The endpoint is defined in format <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal> where transport is one of the following: inproc, ipc, tcp, pgm or epgm.",[["$dsn","string","The connect dsn, for example <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal>."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQSocketException on error."]]
["function","Get list of endpoints\n\nReturns a list of endpoints where the socket is connected or bound to.",null,["array","Returns an array containing elements 'bind' and 'connect'."]]
["function","Get the persistent id\n\nReturns the persistent id of the socket.",null,["string","Returns the persistent id string assigned of the object and <type>null<\/type> if socket is not persistent."]]
["function","Get socket option\n\nReturns the value of a socket option.",[["$key","string","An integer representing the option. See the <constant>ZMQ::SOCKOPT_*<\/constant> constants."]],["mixed","Returns either a <type>string<\/type> or an <type>int<\/type> depending on <parameter>key<\/parameter>. Throws ZMQSocketException on error."]]
["function","Get the socket type\n\nGets the socket type.",null,["int","Returns an integer representing the socket type. The integer can be compared against <constant>ZMQ::SOCKET_*<\/constant> constants."]]
["function","Whether the socket is persistent\n\nCheck whether the socket is persistent.",null,["bool","Returns a <type>bool<\/type> based on whether the socket is persistent or not."]]
["function","Receives a message\n\nReceive a message from a socket. By default receiving will block until a message is available unless <constant>ZMQ::MODE_DONTWAIT<\/constant> flag is used. <constant>ZMQ::SOCKOPT_RCVMORE<\/constant> socket option can be used for receiving multi-part messages. See <function>ZMQSocket::setSockOpt<\/function> for more information.",[["$mode","int","Pass mode flags to receive multipart messages or non-blocking operation. See <constant>ZMQ::MODE_*<\/constant> constants."]],["string","Returns the message. If <constant>ZMQ::MODE_DONTWAIT<\/constant> is used and the operation would block <type>false<\/type> shall be returned."]]
["function","Receives a multipart message\n\nReceive an array multipart message from a socket. By default receiving will block until a message is available unless <constant>ZMQ::MODE_NOBLOCK<\/constant> flag is used.",[["$mode","int","Pass mode flags to receive multipart messages or non-blocking operation. See <constant>ZMQ::MODE_*<\/constant> constants."]],["array","Returns the array of message parts. Throws ZMQSocketException in error. If <constant>ZMQ::MODE_NOBLOCK<\/constant> is used and the operation would block <type>bool<\/type> false shall be returned."]]
["function","Sends a message\n\nSend a message using the socket. The operation can block unless <constant>ZMQ::MODE_NOBLOCK<\/constant> is used.",[["$message","string","The message to send."],["$mode","int","Pass mode flags to receive multipart messages or non-blocking operation. See <constant>ZMQ::MODE_*<\/constant> constants."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQSocketException on error. If <constant>ZMQ::MODE_NOBLOCK<\/constant> is used and the operation would block <type>bool<\/type> false shall be returned."]]
["function","Sends a multipart message\n\nSend a multipart message using the socket. The operation can block unless <constant>ZMQ::MODE_NOBLOCK<\/constant> is used.",[["$message","array","The message to send - an array of strings"],["$mode","int","Pass mode flags to receive multipart messages or non-blocking operation. See <constant>ZMQ::MODE_*<\/constant> constants."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQSocketException on error. If <constant>ZMQ::MODE_NOBLOCK<\/constant> is used and the operation would block <type>bool<\/type> false shall be returned."]]
["function","Set a socket option\n\nSets a ZMQ socket option. The type of the <parameter>value<\/parameter> depends on the <parameter>key<\/parameter>. See ZMQ Constant Types for more information.",[["$key","int","One of the <constant>ZMQ::SOCKOPT_*<\/constant> constants."],["$value","mixed","The value of the parameter."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQSocketException on error."]]
["function","Unbind the socket\n\nUnbind the socket from an endpoint. The endpoint is defined in format <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal> where transport is one of the following: inproc, ipc, tcp, pgm or epgm.",[["$dsn","string","The previously bound dsn, for example <literal>transport:\/\/address<\/literal>."]],["ZMQSocket","Returns the current object. Throws ZMQSocketException on error."]]
