["function","Replace file in ZIP archive with a given path\n\nReplace file in ZIP archive with a given path.\n\nFor maximum portability, it is recommended to always use forward slashes (<literal>\/<\/literal>) as directory separator in ZIP filenames.",[["$filepath","string","The path to the file to add."],["$index","int","The index of the file to be replaced, its name is unchanged."],["$start","int","For partial copy, start position."],["$length","int","For partial copy, length to be copied, if <constant>ZipArchive::LENGTH_TO_END<\/constant> (0) the file size is used, if <constant>ZipArchive::LENGTH_UNCHECKED<\/constant> the whole file is used (starting from <parameter>start<\/parameter>)."],["$flags","int","Bitmask consisting of <constant>ZipArchive::FL_ENC_GUESS<\/constant>, <constant>ZipArchive::FL_ENC_UTF_8<\/constant>, <constant>ZipArchive::FL_ENC_CP437<\/constant>, <constant>ZipArchive::FL_OPEN_FILE_NOW<\/constant>. The behaviour of these constants is described on the ZIP constants page."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["ZipArchive::addFile"]]
