["constant","The name of the class in which it is written, including its namespace (e.g. <literal>Foo\\Bar<\/literal>). Inside a trait, the name of the class using the trait. For anonymous classes, a name generated by the engine. To get the name of the class a method was called on, use <literal>static::class<\/literal>."]
["constant","The directory of the file, equivalent to <literal>dirname(__FILE__)<\/literal>. It has no trailing slash unless it is the root directory."]
["constant","The full path and filename of the file in which it is written, with symlinks resolved."]
["constant","The name of the function in which it is written, including its namespace (e.g. <literal>Foo\\bar<\/literal>). Inside a method, only the method name. For anonymous functions, a name generated by the engine that includes where the closure was defined (as of PHP 8.4.0; previously <literal>{closure}<\/literal>)."]
["constant","The line number on which it is written."]
["constant","The class and method name of the method in which it is written (e.g. <literal>Foo\\Bar::baz<\/literal>). Inside a trait, the trait name is used instead of the class name. Outside of a method, the same as <constant>__FUNCTION__<\/constant>."]
["constant","The name of the current namespace."]
["class","Created by <function>unserialize<\/function> when trying to unserialize an undefined class or a class that is not listed in the <literal>allowed_classes<\/literal> of <function>unserialize<\/function>'s <parameter>options<\/parameter> array.\n\nPrior to PHP 7.2.0, using <function>is_object<\/function> on the <classname>__PHP_Incomplete_Class<\/classname> class would return <type>false<\/type>. As of PHP 7.2.0, <type>true<\/type> will be returned."]
["constant","The name of the property, when used inside a property hook. Available as of PHP 8.4.0."]
["constant","The trait name, including its namespace (e.g. <literal>Foo\\Bar<\/literal>)."]
