["function","Does nothing, except go through the whole request cycle\n\n<function>eio_nop<\/function> does nothing, except go through the whole request cycle. Could be useful in debugging.",[["$pri","int","The request priority: <constant>EIO_PRI_DEFAULT<\/constant>, <constant>EIO_PRI_MIN<\/constant>, <constant>EIO_PRI_MAX<\/constant>, or <type>null<\/type>. If <type>null<\/type> passed, <parameter>pri<\/parameter> internally is set to <constant>EIO_PRI_DEFAULT<\/constant>."],["$callback","callable",["<parameter>callback<\/parameter> function is called when the request is done. It should match the following prototype:",{"type":"code","text":"void callback(mixed $data, int $result[, resource $req]);","role":"php"},"<parameter>data<\/parameter> — is custom data passed to the request. <parameter>result<\/parameter> — request-specific result value; basically, the value returned by corresponding system call. <parameter>req<\/parameter> — is optional request resource which can be used with functions like <function>eio_get_last_error<\/function>.","is custom data passed to the request.","request-specific result value; basically, the value returned by corresponding system call.","is optional request resource which can be used with functions like <function>eio_get_last_error<\/function>."]],["$data","mixed","Arbitrary variable passed to <parameter>callback<\/parameter>."]],["resource","<function>eio_nop<\/function> returns request resource on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>eio_busy<\/function>"]]
