["function","Alias of\n   apache_response_headers\n\nThis function is an alias of: <function>apache_response_headers<\/function>."]
["function","Tries to find out best available locale based on HTTP \"Accept-Language\" header\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nTries to find locale that can satisfy the language list that is requested by the HTTP \"Accept-Language\" header.",[["$header","string","The string containing the \"Accept-Language\" header according to format in RFC 2616."]],["string|false","The corresponding locale identifier.\n\nReturns <type>false<\/type> when the length of <parameter>header<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_lookup<\/function>"]]
["function","Add likely subtags to a locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nExpands a locale tag by adding likely subtags based on the ICU locale data. For example, <literal>en<\/literal> becomes <literal>en_Latn_US<\/literal>.",[["$locale","string","The locale to expand."]],["string|false","Returns the locale with likely subtags added, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["Locale::minimizeSubtags","Locale::canonicalize"]]
["function","Canonicalize the locale string\n\nCanonicalizes the passed locale string to ICU format.\n\nThis does not necessarily indicate or return a valid locale. It is only a version of the input that has been canonicalized according to ICU rules.\n\nThe behavior of this function depends on the version of ICU PHP is using (<constant>INTL_ICU_VERSION<\/constant>).",[["$locale","string","Original locale string."]],["string|null","Canonicalized locale string.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."]]
["function","Returns a correctly ordered and delimited locale ID\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns a correctly ordered and delimited locale ID the keys identify the particular locale ID subtags, and the values are the associated subtag values.",[["$subtags","array","An <type>array<\/type> containing a list of key-value pairs, where the keys identify the particular locale ID subtags, and the values are the associated subtag values.  The <literal>'variant'<\/literal> and <literal>'private'<\/literal> subtags can take maximum 15 values whereas <literal>'extlang'<\/literal> can take maximum 3 values. For instance, variants are allowed with the suffix ranging from 0-14. Hence the keys for the input array can be <literal>variant0<\/literal>, <literal>variant1<\/literal>, …,<literal>variant14<\/literal>. In the returned locale id, the subtag is ordered by suffix resulting in <literal>variant0<\/literal> followed by <literal>variant1<\/literal> followed by <literal>variant2<\/literal> and so on.  Alternatively, the <literal>'variant'<\/literal>, <literal>'private'<\/literal> and <literal>'extlang'<\/literal> values can be specified as array under specific key (e.g. <literal>'variant'<\/literal>). In this case no limits on the number of recognized subtags apply. \n\nThe <literal>'variant'<\/literal> and <literal>'private'<\/literal> subtags can take maximum 15 values whereas <literal>'extlang'<\/literal> can take maximum 3 values. For instance, variants are allowed with the suffix ranging from 0-14. Hence the keys for the input array can be <literal>variant0<\/literal>, <literal>variant1<\/literal>, …,<literal>variant14<\/literal>. In the returned locale id, the subtag is ordered by suffix resulting in <literal>variant0<\/literal> followed by <literal>variant1<\/literal> followed by <literal>variant2<\/literal> and so on.\n\nAlternatively, the <literal>'variant'<\/literal>, <literal>'private'<\/literal> and <literal>'extlang'<\/literal> values can be specified as array under specific key (e.g. <literal>'variant'<\/literal>). In this case no limits on the number of recognized subtags apply."]],["string|false","The corresponding locale identifier, or <type>false<\/type> when <parameter>subtags<\/parameter> is empty."],["<function>locale_parse<\/function>"]]
["function","Checks if a language tag filter matches with locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nChecks if a <parameter>languageTag<\/parameter> filter matches with <parameter>locale<\/parameter> according to RFC 4647's basic filtering algorithm",[["$languageTag","string","The language tag to check"],["$locale","string","The language range to check against"],["$canonicalize","bool","If true, the arguments will be converted to canonical form before matching."]],["bool|null","<type>true<\/type> if <parameter>locale<\/parameter> matches <parameter>languageTag<\/parameter> <type>false<\/type> otherwise.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_lookup<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the variants for the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGets the variants for the input locale",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the variants from"]],["array|null","The <type>array<\/type> containing the list of all variants subtag for the locale or <type>null<\/type> if not present\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_get_primary_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_region<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the default locale value from the INTL global 'default_locale'\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGets the default locale value. At the PHP initialization this value is set to 'intl.default_locale' value from php.ini if that value exists or from ICU's function uloc_getDefault().",null,["string","The current runtime locale"],["<function>locale_set_default<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns an appropriately localized display name for language of the inputlocale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns an appropriately localized display name for language of the input locale. If is <type>null<\/type> then the default locale is used.",[["$locale","string","The locale to return a display language for"],["$displayLocale","string|null","Optional format locale to use to display the language name"]],["string|false","Display name of the language for the <parameter>locale<\/parameter> in the format appropriate for <parameter>displayLocale<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>locale_get_display_name<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_region<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_variant<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns an appropriately localized display name for the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns an appropriately localized display name for the input locale. If <parameter>locale<\/parameter> is <type>null<\/type> then the default locale is used.",[["$locale","string","The locale to return a display name for."],["$displayLocale","string|null","optional format locale"]],["string|false","Display name of the locale in the format appropriate for <parameter>displayLocale<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>locale_get_display_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_region<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_variant<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns an appropriately localized display name for region of the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns an appropriately localized display name for region of the input locale. If is <type>null<\/type> then the default locale is used.",[["$locale","string","The locale to return a display region for."],["$displayLocale","string|null","Optional format locale to use to display the region name"]],["string|false","Display name of the region for the <parameter>locale<\/parameter> in the format appropriate for <parameter>displayLocale<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>locale_get_display_name<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_variant<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns an appropriately localized display name for script of the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns an appropriately localized display name for script of the input locale. If is <type>null<\/type> then the default locale is used.",[["$locale","string","The locale to return a display script for"],["$displayLocale","string|null","Optional format locale to use to display the script name"]],["string|false","Display name of the script for the <parameter>locale<\/parameter> in the format appropriate for <parameter>displayLocale<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>locale_get_display_name<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_region<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_variant<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns an appropriately localized display name for variants of the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns an appropriately localized display name for variants of the input locale. If is <type>null<\/type> then the default locale is used.",[["$locale","string","The locale to return a display variant for"],["$displayLocale","string|null","Optional format locale to use to display the variant name"]],["string|false","Display name of the variant for the <parameter>locale<\/parameter> in the format appropriate for <parameter>displayLocale<\/parameter>, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>locale_get_display_name<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_display_region<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the keywords for the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGets the keywords for the input locale.",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the keywords from. If an empty string is passed, the value returned by <function>locale_get_default<\/function> is used instead."]],["array|false|null","Associative <type>array<\/type> containing the keyword-value pairs for this locale, <type>null<\/type> if the locale has no keywords, or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_get_all_variants<\/function>","<function>locale_get_default<\/function>","<function>locale_set_default<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the primary language for the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGets the primary language for the input locale",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the primary language code from"]],["string|null","The language code associated with the language.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_get_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_region<\/function>","<function>locale_get_all_variants<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the region for the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGets the region for the input locale.",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the region code from"]],["string|null","The region subtag for the locale or <type>null<\/type> if not present\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_get_primary_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_script<\/function>","<function>locale_get_all_variants<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the script for the input locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nGets the script for the input locale.",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the script code from"]],["string|null","The script subtag for the locale or <type>null<\/type> if not present"],["<function>locale_get_primary_language<\/function>","<function>locale_get_region<\/function>","<function>locale_get_all_variants<\/function>"]]
["function","Check whether a locale uses a right-to-left writing system\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nDetermines whether a locale uses a right-to-left writing system.\n\nThis method relies on the ICU library and evaluates the dominant script associated with the locale.",[["$locale","string","The locale identifier. If empty, the default locale is used."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the locale uses a right-to-left writing system, or <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Searches the language tag list for the best match to the language\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSearches the items in <parameter>languageTag<\/parameter> for the best match to the language range specified in <parameter>locale<\/parameter> according to RFC 4647's lookup algorithm.",[["$languageTag","array","An <type>array<\/type> containing a list of language tags to compare to <parameter>locale<\/parameter>. Maximum 100 items allowed."],["$locale","string","The locale to use as the language range when matching."],["$canonicalize","bool","If true, the arguments will be converted to canonical form before matching."],["$defaultLocale","string|null","The locale to use if no match is found."]],["string|null","The closest matching language tag or default value.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_filter_matches<\/function>"]]
["function","Remove likely subtags from a locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nMinimizes a locale tag by removing subtags that can be inferred using the ICU likely subtag data. For example, <literal>en_Latn_US<\/literal> becomes <literal>en<\/literal>.",[["$locale","string","The locale to minimize."]],["string|false","Returns the locale with likely subtags removed, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["Locale::addLikelySubtags","Locale::canonicalize"]]
["function","Returns a key-value array of locale ID subtag elements\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nReturns a key-value array of locale ID subtag elements.",[["$locale","string","The locale to extract the subtag array from. Note: The 'variant' and 'private' subtags can take maximum 15 values whereas 'extlang' can take maximum 3 values. If an empty string is passed, the value returned by <function>locale_get_default<\/function> is used instead."]],["array|null","Returns an array containing a list of key-value pairs, where the keys identify the particular locale ID subtags, and the values are the associated subtag values. The array will be ordered as the locale id subtags e.g. in the locale id if variants are <literal>-varX-varY-varZ<\/literal> then the returned array will have <literal>variant0=>varX<\/literal>, <literal>variant1=>varY<\/literal>, <literal>variant2=>varZ<\/literal>.\n\nReturns <type>null<\/type> when the length of <parameter>locale<\/parameter> exceeds <constant>INTL_MAX_LOCALE_LEN<\/constant>."],["<function>locale_compose<\/function>","<function>locale_get_default<\/function>","<function>locale_set_default<\/function>"]]
["function","Sets the default runtime locale\n\nObject-oriented style\n\nProcedural style\n\nSets the default runtime locale to <parameter>locale<\/parameter>. This changes the value of INTL global 'default_locale' locale identifier. UAX #35 extensions are accepted.",[["$locale","string","Is a BCP 47 compliant language tag."]],["true","Returns <type>true<\/type>."],["<function>locale_get_default<\/function>"]]
["function","Get numeric formatting information\n\nReturns an associative array containing localized numeric and monetary formatting information.",null,["array",["<function>localeconv<\/function> returns data based upon the current locale as set by <function>setlocale<\/function>. The associative array that is returned contains the following fields:",{"type":"table","title":"","headers":["Array element","Description"],"rows":[["decimal_point","Decimal point character"],["thousands_sep","Thousands separator"],["grouping","Array containing numeric groupings"],["int_curr_symbol","International currency symbol (i.e. USD)"],["currency_symbol","Local currency symbol (i.e. $)"],["mon_decimal_point","Monetary decimal point character"],["mon_thousands_sep","Monetary thousands separator"],["mon_grouping","Array containing monetary groupings"],["positive_sign","Sign for positive values"],["negative_sign","Sign for negative values"],["int_frac_digits","International fractional digits"],["frac_digits","Local fractional digits"],["p_cs_precedes","1 if currency_symbol precedes a positive value, 0 if it succeeds one"],["p_sep_by_space","1 if a space separates currency_symbol from a positive value, 0 otherwise"],["n_cs_precedes","1 if currency_symbol precedes a negative value, 0 if it succeeds one"],["n_sep_by_space","1 if a space separates currency_symbol from a negative value, 0 otherwise"],["p_sign_posn","0 - Parentheses surround the quantity and currency_symbol1 - The sign string precedes the quantity and currency_symbol2 - The sign string succeeds the quantity and currency_symbol3 - The sign string immediately precedes the currency_symbol4 - The sign string immediately succeeds the currency_symbol"],["n_sign_posn","0 - Parentheses surround the quantity and currency_symbol1 - The sign string precedes the quantity and currency_symbol2 - The sign string succeeds the quantity and currency_symbol3 - The sign string immediately precedes the currency_symbol4 - The sign string immediately succeeds the currency_symbol"]]},"The <literal>p_sign_posn<\/literal> and <literal>n_sign_posn<\/literal> contain a string of formatting options. Each number represents one of the above listed conditions.","The grouping fields contain arrays that define the way numbers should be grouped. For example, the monetary grouping field for the nl_NL locale (in UTF-8 mode with the euro sign), would contain a 2 item array with the values 3 and 3. The higher the index in the array, the farther left the grouping is. If an array element is equal to <constant>CHAR_MAX<\/constant>, no further grouping is done. If an array element is equal to 0, the previous element should be used."]],["<function>setlocale<\/function>"]]
["function","Get the local time\n\nThe <function>localtime<\/function> function returns an array identical to that of the structure returned by the C function call.",[["$timestamp","int|null","The optional <parameter>timestamp<\/parameter> parameter is an <type>int<\/type> Unix timestamp that defaults to the current local time if <parameter>timestamp<\/parameter> is omitted or <type>null<\/type>. In other words, it defaults to the value of <function>time<\/function>."],["$associative","bool","Determines whether the function should return a regular, numerically indexed array, or an associative one."]],["array","If <parameter>associative<\/parameter> is set to <type>false<\/type> or not supplied then the array is returned as a regular, numerically indexed array. If <parameter>associative<\/parameter> is set to <type>true<\/type> then <function>localtime<\/function> returns an associative array containing the elements of the structure returned by the C function call to localtime. The keys of the associative array are as follows:\n\n \"tm_sec\" - seconds, <literal>0<\/literal> to <literal>59<\/literal>  \"tm_min\" - minutes, <literal>0<\/literal> to <literal>59<\/literal>  \"tm_hour\" - hours, <literal>0<\/literal> to <literal>23<\/literal>  \"tm_mday\" - day of the month, <literal>1<\/literal> to <literal>31<\/literal>  \"tm_mon\" - month of the year, <literal>0<\/literal> (Jan) to <literal>11<\/literal> (Dec)  \"tm_year\" - years since 1900  \"tm_wday\" - day of the week, <literal>0<\/literal> (Sun) to <literal>6<\/literal> (Sat)  \"tm_yday\" - day of the year, <literal>0<\/literal> to <literal>365<\/literal>  \"tm_isdst\" - is daylight savings time in effect?  Positive if yes, <literal>0<\/literal> if not, negative if unknown. "],["<function>getdate<\/function>"]]
["function","Natural logarithm\n\nIf the optional <parameter>base<\/parameter> parameter is specified, <function>log<\/function> returns logbase <parameter>num<\/parameter>, otherwise <function>log<\/function> returns the natural logarithm of <parameter>num<\/parameter>.",[["$num","float","The value to calculate the logarithm for"],["$base","float","The optional logarithmic base to use (defaults to 'e' and so to the natural logarithm)."]],["float","The logarithm of <parameter>num<\/parameter> to <parameter>base<\/parameter>, if given, or the natural logarithm."],["<function>log10<\/function>","<function>exp<\/function>","<function>pow<\/function>","<function>error_log<\/function>"]]
["function","Base-10 logarithm\n\nReturns the base-10 logarithm of <parameter>num<\/parameter>.",[["$num","float","The argument to process"]],["float","The base-10 logarithm of <parameter>num<\/parameter>"],["<function>log<\/function>"]]
["function","Returns log(1 + number), computed in a way that is accurate even when\n   the value of number is close to zero\n\n<function>log1p<\/function> returns log(1 + <parameter>num<\/parameter>) computed in a way that is accurate even when the value of <parameter>num<\/parameter> is close to zero. <function>log<\/function> might only return log(1) in this case due to lack of precision.",[["$num","float","The argument to process"]],["float","log(1 + <parameter>num<\/parameter>)"],["<function>expm1<\/function>","<function>log<\/function>","<function>log10<\/function>"]]
["language",[{"type":"heading","text":"Logical Operators"},{"type":"table","title":"Logical Operators","headers":["Example","Name","Result"],"rows":[["$a and $b","And","<type>true<\/type> if both $a and $b are <type>true<\/type>."],["$a or $b","Or","<type>true<\/type> if either $a or $b is <type>true<\/type>."],["$a xor $b","Xor","<type>true<\/type> if either $a or $b is <type>true<\/type>, but not both."],["! $a","Not","<type>true<\/type> if $a is not <type>true<\/type>."],["$a && $b","And","<type>true<\/type> if both $a and $b are <type>true<\/type>."],["$a || $b","Or","<type>true<\/type> if either $a or $b is <type>true<\/type>."]]},"The reason for the two different variations of \"and\" and \"or\" operators is that they operate at different precedences. (See Operator Precedence.)",{"type":"code","text":"<?php\n\n\/\/ --------------------\n\/\/ foo() will never get called as those operators are short-circuit\n\n$a = (false && foo());\n$b = (true  || foo());\n$c = (false and foo());\n$d = (true  or  foo());\n\n\/\/ --------------------\n\/\/ \"||\" has a greater precedence than \"or\"\n\n\/\/ The result of the expression (false || true) is assigned to $e\n\/\/ Acts like: ($e = (false || true))\n$e = false || true;\n\n\/\/ The constant false is assigned to $f before the \"or\" operation occurs\n\/\/ Acts like: (($f = false) or true)\n$f = false or true;\n\nvar_dump($e, $f);\n\n\/\/ --------------------\n\/\/ \"&&\" has a greater precedence than \"and\"\n\n\/\/ The result of the expression (true && false) is assigned to $g\n\/\/ Acts like: ($g = (true && false))\n$g = true && false;\n\n\/\/ The constant true is assigned to $h before the \"and\" operation occurs\n\/\/ Acts like: (($h = true) and false)\n$h = true and false;\n\nvar_dump($g, $h);\n?>","role":"php"},"The above example will output something similar to:",{"type":"code","text":"bool(true)\nbool(false)\nbool(false)\nbool(true)","kind":"screen"}]]
["function","Converts a long integer address into a string in (IPv4) Internet standard dotted format\n\nThe function <function>long2ip<\/function> generates an Internet address in dotted format (i.e.: aaa.bbb.ccc.ddd) from the long integer representation.",[["$ip","int","A proper address representation in long integer."]],["string","Returns the Internet IP address as a <type>string<\/type>."],["<function>ip2long<\/function>"]]
["function","Gives information about a file or symbolic link\n\nGathers the statistics of the file or symbolic link named by <parameter>filename<\/parameter>.",[["$filename","string","Path to a file or a symbolic link."]],["array|false","See the manual page for <function>stat<\/function> for information on the structure of the array that <function>lstat<\/function> returns. This function is identical to the <function>stat<\/function> function except that if the <parameter>filename<\/parameter> parameter is a symbolic link, the status of the symbolic link is returned, not the status of the file pointed to by the symbolic link.\n\nOn failure, <type>false<\/type> is returned."],["<function>stat<\/function>"]]
["function","Strip whitespace (or other characters) from the beginning of a string\n\nStrip whitespace (or other characters) from the beginning of a string.\n\nWithout the second parameter, <function>ltrim<\/function> will strip these characters:\n\n<literal>\" \"<\/literal>: ASCIISP character <literal>0x20<\/literal>, an ordinary space.\n\n<literal>\"\\t\"<\/literal>: ASCIIHT character <literal>0x09<\/literal>, a tab.\n\n<literal>\"\\n\"<\/literal>: ASCIILF character <literal>0x0A<\/literal>, a new line (line feed).\n\n<literal>\"\\r\"<\/literal>: ASCIICR character <literal>0x0D<\/literal>, a carriage return.\n\n<literal>\"\\0\"<\/literal>: ASCIINUL character <literal>0x00<\/literal>, the NUL-byte.\n\n<literal>\"\\v\"<\/literal>: ASCIIVT character <literal>0x0B<\/literal>, a vertical tab.",[["$string","string","The input string."],["$characters","string","Optionally, the stripped characters can also be specified using the <parameter>characters<\/parameter> parameter. Simply list all characters that need to be stripped. With <literal>..<\/literal> it is possible to specify an incrementing range of characters."]],["string","This function returns a string with whitespace stripped from the beginning of <parameter>string<\/parameter>."],["<function>trim<\/function>","<function>rtrim<\/function>"]]
["function","LZF compression\n\n<function>lzf_compress<\/function> compresses the given <parameter>data<\/parameter> string using LZF encoding.",[["$data","string","The string to compress."]],["string","Returns the compressed data or <type>false<\/type> if an error occurred."],["<function>lzf_decompress<\/function>"]]
["function","LZF decompression\n\n<function>lzf_compress<\/function> decompresses the given <parameter>data<\/parameter> string containing lzf encoded data.",[["$data","string","The compressed string."]],["string","Returns the decompressed data or <type>false<\/type> if an error occurred."],["<function>lzf_compress<\/function>"]]
["function","Determines what LZF extension was optimized for\n\nDetermines what was LZF extension optimized for during compilation.",null,["int","Returns 1 if LZF was optimized for speed, 0 for compression."]]
["language",[{"type":"heading","text":"Magic constants"},"Magic constants are keywords that are replaced with information about their own location in the source code: their file and line, and the function, class, trait, namespace, or property hook enclosing them. Despite their name, they are not actual constants: <function>defined<\/function> and <function>constant<\/function> do not recognize them, and a constant of the same name created with <function>define<\/function> does not affect them. They are case-insensitive. When used outside of the relevant context (e.g. <constant>__CLASS__<\/constant> outside of a class), they are replaced with an empty string.",{"type":"table","title":"PHP's magic constants","headers":["Name","Description"],"rows":[["<constant>__LINE__<\/constant>","The line number on which it is written."],["<constant>__FILE__<\/constant>","The full path and filename of the file in which it is written, with symlinks resolved."],["<constant>__DIR__<\/constant>","The directory of the file, equivalent to <literal>dirname(__FILE__)<\/literal>. It has no trailing slash unless it is the root directory."],["<constant>__FUNCTION__<\/constant>","The name of the function in which it is written, including its namespace (e.g. <literal>Foo\\bar<\/literal>). Inside a method, only the method name. For anonymous functions, a name generated by the engine that includes where the closure was defined (as of PHP 8.4.0; previously <literal>{closure}<\/literal>)."],["<constant>__CLASS__<\/constant>","The name of the class in which it is written, including its namespace (e.g. <literal>Foo\\Bar<\/literal>). Inside a trait, the name of the class using the trait. For anonymous classes, a name generated by the engine. To get the name of the class a method was called on, use <literal>static::class<\/literal>."],["<constant>__TRAIT__<\/constant>","The trait name, including its namespace (e.g. <literal>Foo\\Bar<\/literal>)."],["<constant>__METHOD__<\/constant>","The class and method name of the method in which it is written (e.g. <literal>Foo\\Bar::baz<\/literal>). Inside a trait, the trait name is used instead of the class name. Outside of a method, the same as <constant>__FUNCTION__<\/constant>."],["<constant>__PROPERTY__<\/constant>","The name of the property, when used inside a property hook. Available as of PHP 8.4.0."],["<constant>__NAMESPACE__<\/constant>","The name of the current namespace."]]},{"type":"code","text":"<?php\nnamespace App;\n\nfunction helper()\n{\n    echo __FUNCTION__, \"\\n\";\n    echo __METHOD__, \"\\n\";\n}\n\ntrait Greets\n{\n    public function greet()\n    {\n        echo __CLASS__, \"\\n\";\n        echo __TRAIT__, \"\\n\";\n        echo __METHOD__, \"\\n\";\n        echo __FUNCTION__, \"\\n\";\n    }\n}\n\nclass Greeter\n{\n    use Greets;\n}\n\nhelper();\n(new Greeter)->greet();\necho __NAMESPACE__, \"\\n\";","role":"php"},"The above example will output:",{"type":"code","text":"App\\helper\nApp\\helper\nApp\\Greeter\nApp\\Greets\nApp\\Greets::greet\ngreet\nApp","kind":"screen"},{"type":"heading","text":"See Also"},"::class<function>get_class<\/function><function>get_called_class<\/function><function>dirname<\/function>"]]
["function","Send mail\n\nSends an email.",[["$to","string","Receiver, or receivers of the mail.\n\nThe formatting of this string must comply with RFC 2822. Some examples are: user@example.comuser@example.com, anotheruser@example.comUser <user@example.com>User <user@example.com>, Another User <anotheruser@example.com>"],["$subject","string","Subject of the email to be sent.\n\nSubject must satisfy RFC 2047."],["$message","string",["Message to be sent.","Each line should be separated with a CRLF (\\r\\n). Lines should not be larger than 70 characters.","(Windows only) When PHP is talking to a SMTP server directly, if a full stop is found on the start of a line, it is removed. To counter-act this, replace these occurrences with a double dot.",{"type":"code","text":"<?php\n$text = str_replace(\"\\n.\", \"\\n..\", $text);\n?>","role":"php"}]],["$additional_headers","array|string","<type>String<\/type> or <type>array<\/type> to be inserted at the end of the email header.\n\nThis is typically used to add extra headers (From, Cc, and Bcc). Multiple extra headers should be separated with a CRLF (\\r\\n). If outside data are used to compose this header, the data should be sanitized so that no unwanted headers could be injected.\n\nIf an <type>array<\/type> is passed, its keys are the header names and its values are the respective header values.\n\nWhen sending mail, the mail must contain a <literal>From<\/literal> header. This can be set with the <parameter>additional_headers<\/parameter> parameter, or a default can be set in php.ini.\n\nFailing to do this will result in an error message similar to <literal>Warning: mail(): \"sendmail_from\" not set in php.ini or custom \"From:\" header missing<\/literal>. The <literal>From<\/literal> header sets also <literal>Return-Path<\/literal> when sending directly via SMTP (Windows only).\n\nIf messages are not received, try using a LF (\\n) only. Some Unix mail transfer agents (most notably qmail) replace LF by CRLF automatically (which leads to doubling CR if CRLF is used). This should be a last resort, as it does not comply with RFC 2822."],["$additional_params","string","The <parameter>additional_params<\/parameter> parameter can be used to pass additional flags as command line options to the program configured to be used when sending mail, as defined by the <literal>sendmail_path<\/literal> configuration setting. For example, this can be used to set the envelope sender address when using sendmail with the <literal>-f<\/literal> sendmail option.\n\nThis parameter is escaped by <function>escapeshellcmd<\/function> internally to prevent command execution. <function>escapeshellcmd<\/function> prevents command execution, but allows to add additional parameters. For security reasons, it is recommended for the user to sanitize this parameter to avoid adding unwanted parameters to the shell command.\n\nSince <function>escapeshellcmd<\/function> is applied automatically, some characters that are allowed as email addresses by internet RFCs cannot be used. <function>mail<\/function> can not allow such characters, so in programs where the use of such characters is required, alternative means of sending emails (such as using a framework or a library) is recommended.\n\nThe user that the webserver runs as should be added as a trusted user to the sendmail configuration to prevent a 'X-Warning' header from being added to the message when the envelope sender (-f) is set using this method. For sendmail users, this file is \/etc\/mail\/trusted-users."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the mail was successfully accepted for delivery, <type>false<\/type> otherwise.\n\nIt is important to note that just because the mail was accepted for delivery, it does NOT mean the mail will actually reach the intended destination."],["<function>mb_send_mail<\/function>","<function>imap_mail<\/function>","PEAR::Mail","PEAR::Mail_Mime"]]
["function","Gets the best way of encoding\n\nFigures out the best way of encoding the content read from the given file pointer.",[["$fp","resource","A valid file pointer, which must be seek-able."]],["string","Returns one of the character encodings supported by the mbstring module."]]
["function","Create a mime mail resource\n\nCreate a <literal>MIME<\/literal> mail resource.",null,["resource","Returns a handle that can be used to parse a message."],["<function>mailparse_msg_free<\/function>","<function>mailparse_msg_parse_file<\/function>"]]
["function","Extracts\/decodes a message section\n\nThis function is currently not documented; only its argument list is available.",[["$mimemail","resource","A valid <literal>MIME<\/literal> resource."],["$msgbody","string",""],["$callbackfunc","callable",""]],["void","No value is returned."],["<function>mailparse_msg_extract_part_file<\/function>","<function>mailparse_msg_extract_whole_part_file<\/function>"]]
["function","Extracts\/decodes a message section\n\nExtracts\/decodes a message section from the supplied filename.\n\nThe contents of the section will be decoded according to their transfer encoding - base64, quoted-printable and uuencoded text are supported.",[["$mimemail","resource","A valid <literal>MIME<\/literal> resource, created with <function>mailparse_msg_create<\/function>."],["$filename","mixed","Can be a file name or a valid stream resource."],["$callbackfunc","callable","If set, this must be either a valid callback that will be passed the extracted section, or <type>null<\/type> to make this function return the extracted section.\n\nIf not specified, the contents will be sent to \"stdout\"."]],["string","If <parameter>callbackfunc<\/parameter> is not <type>null<\/type> returns <type>true<\/type> on success.\n\nIf <parameter>callbackfunc<\/parameter> is set to <type>null<\/type>, returns the extracted section as a string.\n\nReturns <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>mailparse_msg_extract_part<\/function>","<function>mailparse_msg_extract_whole_part_file<\/function>"]]
