["function","Octal to decimal\n\nReturns the decimal equivalent of the octal number represented by the <parameter>octal_string<\/parameter> argument.",[["$octal_string","string","The octal string to convert. Any invalid characters in <parameter>octal_string<\/parameter> are silently ignored. As of PHP 7.4.0 supplying any invalid characters is deprecated."]],["int|float","The decimal representation of <parameter>octal_string<\/parameter>"],["<function>decoct<\/function>","<function>bindec<\/function>","<function>hexdec<\/function>","<function>base_convert<\/function>"]]
["function","Toggle autocommit behaviour\n\nToggles autocommit behaviour.\n\nBy default, auto-commit is on for a connection. Disabling auto-commit is equivalent with starting a transaction.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$enable","bool|null","If <parameter>enable<\/parameter> is <type>true<\/type>, auto-commit is enabled, if it is <type>false<\/type> auto-commit is disabled. If <type>null<\/type> is passed, this function returns the auto-commit status for <parameter>odbc<\/parameter>."]],["int|bool","With a <type>null<\/type> <parameter>enable<\/parameter> parameter, this function returns auto-commit status for <parameter>odbc<\/parameter>. Non-zero is returned if auto-commit is on, 0 if it is off, or <type>false<\/type> if an error occurs.\n\nIf <parameter>enable<\/parameter> is non-null, this function returns <type>true<\/type> on success and <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>odbc_commit<\/function>","<function>odbc_rollback<\/function>"]]
["function",["Handling of binary column data","Controls handling of binary column data. ODBC SQL types affected are <literal>BINARY<\/literal>, <literal>VARBINARY<\/literal>, and <literal>LONGVARBINARY<\/literal>. The default mode can be set using the uodbc.defaultbinmode php.ini directive.","When binary SQL data is converted to character C data (<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_CONVERT<\/constant>), each byte (8 bits) of source data is represented as two ASCII characters. These characters are the ASCII character representation of the number in its hexadecimal form. For example, a binary <literal>00000001<\/literal> is converted to <literal>\"01\"<\/literal> and a binary <literal>11111111<\/literal> is converted to <literal>\"FF\"<\/literal>.","While the handling of <literal>BINARY<\/literal> and <literal>VARBINARY<\/literal> columns only depend on the binmode, the handling of <literal>LONGVARBINARY<\/literal> columns also depends on the longreadlen as well:",{"type":"table","title":"LONGVARBINARY handling","headers":["binmode","longreadlen","result"],"rows":[["<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_PASSTHRU<\/constant>","0","passthru"],["<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_RETURN<\/constant>","0","passthru"],["<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_CONVERT<\/constant>","0","passthru"],["<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_PASSTHRU<\/constant>",">0","passthru"],["<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_RETURN<\/constant>",">0","return as is"],["<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_CONVERT<\/constant>",">0","return as char"]]},"If <function>odbc_fetch_into<\/function> is used, passthru means that an empty string is returned for these columns. If <function>odbc_result<\/function> is used, passthru means that the data are sent directly to the client (i.e. printed)."],[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$mode","int","Possible values for <parameter>mode<\/parameter> are: <constant>ODBC_BINMODE_PASSTHRU<\/constant>: Passthru BINARY data <constant>ODBC_BINMODE_RETURN<\/constant>: Return as is <constant>ODBC_BINMODE_CONVERT<\/constant>: Convert to char and return   Handling of binary long columns is also affected by <function>odbc_longreadlen<\/function>. \n\n<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_PASSTHRU<\/constant>: Passthru BINARY data\n\n<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_RETURN<\/constant>: Return as is\n\n<constant>ODBC_BINMODE_CONVERT<\/constant>: Convert to char and return\n\nHandling of binary long columns is also affected by <function>odbc_longreadlen<\/function>."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Close an ODBC connection\n\nCloses down the connection to the database server.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."]],["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Close all ODBC connections\n\n<function>odbc_close_all<\/function> will close down all connections to database server(s).",null,["void","No value is returned."]]
["function","Lists columns and associated privileges for the given table\n\nLists columns and associated privileges for the given table.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$table","string","The table name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$column","string","The column name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure. This result object can be used to fetch a list of columns and associated privileges.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>GRANTOR<\/literal><literal>GRANTEE<\/literal><literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal><literal>IS_GRANTABLE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal>, <literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal>."]]
["function","Lists the column names in specified tables\n\nLists all columns in the requested range.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string|null","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$table","string|null","The table name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$column","string|null","The column name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>TYPE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_SIZE<\/literal><literal>BUFFER_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>DECIMAL_DIGITS<\/literal><literal>NUM_PREC_RADIX<\/literal><literal>NULLABLE<\/literal><literal>REMARKS<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_DEF<\/literal><literal>SQL_DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>SQL_DATETIME_SUB<\/literal><literal>CHAR_OCTET_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal><literal>IS_NULLABLE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_columnprivileges<\/function>","<function>odbc_procedurecolumns<\/function>"]]
["function","Commit an ODBC transaction\n\nCommits all pending transactions on the connection.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Connect to a datasource\n\nThe connection id returned by this functions is needed by other ODBC functions. You can have multiple connections open at once as long as they either use different db or different credentials.\n\nWith some ODBC drivers, executing a complex stored procedure may fail with an error similar to: \"Cannot open a cursor on a stored procedure that has anything other than a single select statement in it\". Using SQL_CUR_USE_ODBC may avoid that error. Also, some drivers don't support the optional row_number parameter in <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function>. SQL_CUR_USE_ODBC might help in that case, too.",[["$dsn","string","The database source name for the connection. Alternatively, a DSN-less connection string can be used."],["$user","string|null","The username. This parameter is ignored if <parameter>dsn<\/parameter> contains <literal>uid<\/literal>. To connect without specifying a <parameter>user<\/parameter>, use <type>null<\/type>."],["$password","string|null","The password. This parameter is ignored if <parameter>dsn<\/parameter> contains <literal>pwd<\/literal>. To connect without specifying a <parameter>password<\/parameter>, use <type>null<\/type>."],["$cursor_option","int","This sets the type of cursor to be used for this connection. This parameter is not normally needed, but can be useful for working around problems with some ODBC drivers.\n\nThe following constants are defined for cursortype:\n\n SQL_CUR_USE_IF_NEEDED  SQL_CUR_USE_ODBC  SQL_CUR_USE_DRIVER \n\nSQL_CUR_USE_IF_NEEDED\n\nSQL_CUR_USE_ODBC\n\nSQL_CUR_USE_DRIVER"]],["Odbc\\Connection|false","Returns an ODBC connection, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["For persistent connections: <function>odbc_pconnect<\/function>"]]
["function","Determines if an ODBC connection string value is quoted\n\nDetermines if a string is properly quoted for an ODBC connection string value. ODBC connection string quoting is performed using curly braces, and ending braces within a string must be escaped through repeating them twice, similar to SQL quoting.",[["$str","string","The string to check for quoting."]],["bool","<type>true<\/type> if quoted properly, <type>false<\/type> if not."],["<function>odbc_connection_string_quote<\/function>","<function>odbc_connection_string_should_quote<\/function>"]]
["function","Quotes an ODBC connection string value\n\nQuotes a value for a connection string, according to ODBC rules. That is, it will be surrounded by quotes, and any ending curly braces will be escaped. This should be done for any connection string values that come from user input. Not doing so can lead to issues with parsing the connection string, or values being injected into the connection string.\n\nNote that this function does not check if the string is already quoted, nor if the string needs quoting. For that, call <function>odbc_connection_string_is_quoted<\/function> and <function>odbc_connection_string_should_quote<\/function>.",[["$str","string","The unquoted string."]],["string","A quoted string, surrounded by curly braces, and properly escaped."],["<function>odbc_connection_string_is_quoted<\/function>","<function>odbc_connection_string_should_quote<\/function>"]]
["function","Determines if an ODBC connection string value should be quoted\n\nDetermines if a string needs to be quoted for an ODBC connection string value; that is, if it contains special characters.\n\nNote that this does not check if the string is already quoted; an already quoted string will contain characters that will make this function return true. You should call <function>odbc_connection_string_is_quoted<\/function> to check.",[["$str","string","The string to check for."]],["bool","<type>true<\/type> if the string should be quoted; <type>false<\/type> otherwise."],["<function>odbc_connection_string_quote<\/function>","<function>odbc_connection_string_is_quoted<\/function>"]]
["function","Get cursorname\n\nGets the cursorname for the given result_id.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."]],["string|false","Returns the cursor name, as a string, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Returns information about available DSNs\n\nThis function will return the list of available DSN (after calling it several times).",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$fetch_type","int","The <parameter>fetch_type<\/parameter> can be one of two constant types: <constant>SQL_FETCH_FIRST<\/constant>, <constant>SQL_FETCH_NEXT<\/constant>. Use <constant>SQL_FETCH_FIRST<\/constant> the first time this function is called, thereafter use the <constant>SQL_FETCH_NEXT<\/constant>."]],["array|null|false","Returns <type>false<\/type> on error, an <type>array<\/type> upon success, and <type>null<\/type> after fetching the last available DSN."]]
["function","Alias of odbc_exec\n\nThis function is an alias of: <function>odbc_exec<\/function>."]
["function","Get the last error code\n\nReturns a six-digit ODBC state, or an empty string if there has been no errors.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection|null","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."]],["string","If <parameter>odbc<\/parameter> is specified, the last state of that connection is returned, else the last state of any connection is returned.\n\nThis function returns meaningful value only if last odbc query failed (i.e. <function>odbc_exec<\/function> returned <type>false<\/type>)."],["<function>odbc_errormsg<\/function>","<function>odbc_exec<\/function>"]]
["function","Get the last error message\n\nReturns a string containing the last ODBC error message, or an empty string if there has been no errors.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection|null","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."]],["string","If <parameter>odbc<\/parameter> is specified, the last state of that connection is returned, else the last state of any connection is returned.\n\nThis function returns meaningful value only if last odbc query failed (i.e. <function>odbc_exec<\/function> returned <type>false<\/type>)."],["<function>odbc_error<\/function>","<function>odbc_exec<\/function>"]]
["function","Directly execute an SQL statement\n\nSends an SQL statement to the database server.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$query","string","The SQL statement."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object if the SQL command was executed successfully, or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>odbc_prepare<\/function>","<function>odbc_execute<\/function>"]]
["function","Execute a prepared statement\n\nExecutes a statement prepared with <function>odbc_prepare<\/function>.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object from <function>odbc_prepare<\/function>."],["$params","array","Parameters in <parameter>params<\/parameter> will be substituted for placeholders in the prepared statement in order. Elements of this array will be converted to strings by calling this function.\n\nAny parameters in <parameter>params<\/parameter> which start and end with single quotes will be taken as the name of a file to read and send to the database server as the data for the appropriate placeholder.\n\nIf you wish to store a string which actually begins and ends with single quotes, you must add a space or other non-single-quote character to the beginning or end of the parameter, which will prevent the parameter from being taken as a file name. If this is not an option, then you must use another mechanism to store the string, such as executing the query directly with <function>odbc_exec<\/function>)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>odbc_prepare<\/function>"]]
["function","Fetch a result row as an associative array\n\nFetch an associative <type>array<\/type> from an ODBC query.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object from <function>odbc_exec<\/function>."],["$row","int|null","The 1-based number of the row to retrieve. If omitted or <type>null<\/type>, the next row of the result set is fetched, as <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> does. If the driver does not support fetching rows by number, this parameter is ignored."]],["array|false","Returns an array that corresponds to the fetched row, or <type>false<\/type> if there are no more rows."],["<function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function>","<function>odbc_fetch_object<\/function>","<function>odbc_num_rows<\/function>"]]
["function","Fetch one result row into array\n\nFetch one result row into <type>array<\/type>.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$array","array","The result <type>array<\/type> that can be of any type since it will be converted to type array. The array will contain the column values starting at array index 0."],["$row","int|null","The 1-based number of the row to fetch. If omitted or <type>null<\/type>, the next row of the result set is fetched, as <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> does. If the driver does not support fetching rows by number, this parameter is ignored."]],["int|false","Returns the number of columns in the result; <type>false<\/type> on error."]]
["function","Fetch a result row as an object\n\nFetch an <type>object<\/type> from an ODBC query.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object from <function>odbc_exec<\/function>."],["$row","int|null","The 1-based number of the row to retrieve. If omitted or <type>null<\/type>, the next row of the result set is fetched, as <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> does. If the driver does not support fetching rows by number, this parameter is ignored."]],["stdClass|false","Returns an object that corresponds to the fetched row, or <type>false<\/type> if there are no more rows."],["<function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function>","<function>odbc_fetch_array<\/function>","<function>odbc_num_rows<\/function>"]]
["function","Fetch a row\n\nFetches a row of the data that was returned by <function>odbc_do<\/function> or <function>odbc_exec<\/function>. After <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> is called, the fields of that row can be accessed with <function>odbc_result<\/function>.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$row","int|null","If <parameter>row<\/parameter> is not specified, <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> will try to fetch the next row in the result set. Calls to <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> with and without <parameter>row<\/parameter> can be mixed.\n\nTo step through the result more than once, you can call <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> with <parameter>row<\/parameter> 1, and then continue doing <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function> without <parameter>row<\/parameter> to review the result. If a driver doesn't support fetching rows by number, the <parameter>row<\/parameter> parameter is ignored."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if there was a row, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Get the length (precision) of a field\n\nGets the length of the field referenced by number in the given result identifier.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$field","int","The field number. Field numbering starts at 1."]],["int|false","Returns the field length, or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>odbc_field_scale<\/function> to get the scale of a\n    floating point number"]]
["function","Get the columnname\n\nGets the name of the field occupying the given column number in the given result object.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$field","int","The field number. Field numbering starts at 1."]],["string|false","Returns the field name as a string, or <type>false<\/type> on error."]]
["function","Return column number\n\nGets the number of the column slot that corresponds to the named field in the given result object.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$field","string","The field name."]],["int|false","Returns the field number as an integer, or <type>false<\/type> on error. Field numbering starts at 1."]]
["function","Alias of odbc_field_len\n\nThis function is an alias of: <function>odbc_field_len<\/function>.",null,null,["<function>odbc_field_scale<\/function> to get the scale of a\n    floating point number."]]
["function","Get the scale of a field\n\nGets the scale of the field referenced by number in the given result identifier.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$field","int","The field number. Field numbering starts at 1."]],["int|false","Returns the field scale as an integer, or <type>false<\/type> on error."]]
["function","Datatype of a field\n\nGets the SQL type of the field referenced by number in the given result identifier.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$field","int","The field number. Field numbering starts at 1."]],["string|false","Returns the field type as a string, or <type>false<\/type> on error."]]
["function","Retrieves a list of foreign keys\n\nRetrieves a list of foreign keys in the specified table or a list of foreign keys in other tables that refer to the primary key in the specified table",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$pk_catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance) of the primary key table."],["$pk_schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance) of the primary key table."],["$pk_table","string","The primary key table."],["$fk_catalog","string","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance) of the foreign key table."],["$fk_schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance) of the foreign key table."],["$fk_table","string","The foreign key table."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>PKTABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>PKTABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>PKTABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>PKCOLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>FKTABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>FKTABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>FKTABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>FKCOLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>KEY_SEQ<\/literal><literal>UPDATE_RULE<\/literal><literal>DELETE_RULE<\/literal><literal>FK_NAME<\/literal><literal>PK_NAME<\/literal><literal>DEFERRABILITY<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nIf the foreign keys associated with a primary key are requested, the result set is ordered by <literal>FKTABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>FKTABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>FKTABLE_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>KEY_SEQ<\/literal>. If the primary keys associated with a foreign key are requested, the result set is ordered by <literal>PKTABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>PKTABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>PKTABLE_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>KEY_SEQ<\/literal>.\n\nIf <parameter>pk_table<\/parameter> contains a table name, <function>odbc_foreignkeys<\/function> returns a result set containing the primary key of the specified table and all of the foreign keys that refer to it.\n\nIf <parameter>fk_table<\/parameter> contains a table name, <function>odbc_foreignkeys<\/function> returns a result set containing all of the foreign keys in the specified table and the primary keys (in other tables) to which they refer.\n\nIf both <parameter>pk_table<\/parameter> and <parameter>fk_table<\/parameter> contain table names, <function>odbc_foreignkeys<\/function> returns the foreign keys in the table specified in <parameter>fk_table<\/parameter> that refer to the primary key of the table specified in <parameter>pk_table<\/parameter>. This should be one key at most."],["<function>odbc_tables<\/function>","<function>odbc_primarykeys<\/function>"]]
["function","Free objects associated with a result\n\nFree objects associated with a result.\n\n<function>odbc_free_result<\/function> only needs to be called if you are worried about using too much memory while your script is running. All result memory will automatically be freed when the script is finished.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Retrieves information about data types supported by the data source\n\nRetrieves information about data types supported by the data source.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$data_type","int","The data type, which can be used to restrict the information to a single data type."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: TYPE_NAMEDATA_TYPEPRECISIONLITERAL_PREFIXLITERAL_SUFFIXCREATE_PARAMSNULLABLECASE_SENSITIVESEARCHABLEUNSIGNED_ATTRIBUTEMONEYAUTO_INCREMENTLOCAL_TYPE_NAMEMINIMUM_SCALEMAXIMUM_SCALE\n\nThe result set is ordered by DATA_TYPE and TYPE_NAME."]]
["function","Handling of LONG columns\n\nControls handling of <literal>LONG<\/literal>, <literal>LONGVARCHAR<\/literal> and <literal>LONGVARBINARY<\/literal> columns. The default length can be set using the uodbc.defaultlrl php.ini directive.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$length","int","The number of bytes returned to PHP is controlled by the parameter length. If it is set to <literal>0<\/literal>, long column data is passed through to the client (i.e. printed) when retrieved with <function>odbc_result<\/function>."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Checks if multiple results are available\n\nChecks if there are more result sets available as well as allowing access to the next result set via <function>odbc_fetch_array<\/function>, <function>odbc_fetch_row<\/function>, <function>odbc_result<\/function>, etc.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if there are more result sets, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."]]
["function","Number of columns in a result\n\nGets the number of fields (columns) in an ODBC result.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object returned by <function>odbc_exec<\/function>."]],["int","Returns the number of fields, or -1 on error."]]
["function","Number of rows in a result\n\nGets the number of rows in a result. For INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE statements <function>odbc_num_rows<\/function> returns the number of rows affected. For a SELECT clause this can be the number of rows available.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object returned by <function>odbc_exec<\/function>."]],["int","Returns the number of rows in an ODBC result. This function will return -1 on error."]]
["function","Open a persistent database connection\n\nOpens a persistent database connection.\n\nThis function is much like <function>odbc_connect<\/function>, except that the connection is not really closed when the script has finished. Future requests for a connection with the same <parameter>dsn<\/parameter>, <parameter>user<\/parameter>, <parameter>password<\/parameter> combination (via <function>odbc_connect<\/function> and <function>odbc_pconnect<\/function>) can reuse the persistent connection.",null,["Odbc\\Connection|false","Returns an ODBC connection, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>odbc_connect<\/function>","Persistent Database Connections"]]
["function","Prepares a statement for execution\n\nPrepares a statement for execution. The ODBC result object can be used later to execute the statement with <function>odbc_execute<\/function>.\n\nSome databases (such as IBM DB2, MS SQL Server, and Oracle) support stored procedures that accept parameters of type IN, INOUT, and OUT as defined by the ODBC specification. However, the Unified ODBC driver currently only supports parameters of type IN to stored procedures.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$query","string","The query string statement being prepared."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object if the SQL command was prepared successfully. Returns <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>odbc_execute<\/function>"]]
["function","Gets the primary keys for a table\n\nReturns a result object that can be used to fetch the column names that comprise the primary key for a table.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$table","string",""]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>KEY_SEQ<\/literal><literal>PK_NAME<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>KEY_SEQ<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_tables<\/function>","<function>odbc_foreignkeys<\/function>"]]
["function","Retrieve information about parameters to procedures\n\nRetrieve information about parameters to procedures.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string|null","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$procedure","string|null","The proc. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$column","string|null","The column. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns the list of input and output parameters, as well as the columns that make up the result set for the specified procedures. Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_TYPE<\/literal><literal>DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>TYPE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_SIZE<\/literal><literal>BUFFER_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>DECIMAL_DIGITS<\/literal><literal>NUM_PREC_RADIX<\/literal><literal>NULLABLE<\/literal><literal>REMARKS<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_DEF<\/literal><literal>SQL_DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>SQL_DATETIME_SUB<\/literal><literal>CHAR_OCTET_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal><literal>IS_NULLABLE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>COLUMN_TYPE<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_columns<\/function>"]]
["function","Get the list of procedures stored in a specific data source\n\nLists all procedures in the requested range.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string|null","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$procedure","string|null","The name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object containing the information or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal><literal>NUM_INPUT_PARAMS<\/literal><literal>NUM_OUTPUT_PARAMS<\/literal><literal>NUM_RESULT_SETS<\/literal><literal>REMARKS<\/literal><literal>PROCEDURE_TYPE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>PROCEDURE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>PROCEDURE_SCHEMA<\/literal> and <literal>PROCEDURE_NAME<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_procedurecolumns<\/function>","<function>odbc_tables<\/function>"]]
["function","Get result data\n\nGet result data",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$field","string|int","The field name being retrieved. It can either be an integer containing the column number of the field you want; or it can be a string containing the name of the field."]],["string|bool|null","Returns the string contents of the field, <type>false<\/type> on error, <type>null<\/type> for NULL data, or <type>true<\/type> for binary data."]]
["function","Print result as HTML table\n\nPrints all rows from a result object produced by <function>odbc_exec<\/function>. The result is printed in HTML table format. The data is not escaped.\n\nThis function is not supposed to be used in production environments; it is merely meant for development purposes, to get a result set quickly rendered.",[["$statement","Odbc\\Result","The ODBC result object."],["$format","string","Additional overall table formatting."]],["int|false","Returns the number of rows in the result or <type>false<\/type> on error."]]
["function","Rollback a transaction\n\nRolls back all pending statements on the connection.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Adjust ODBC settings\n\nThis function allows fiddling with the ODBC options for a particular connection or query result. It was written to help find work around to problems in quirky ODBC drivers. You should probably only use this function if you are an ODBC programmer and understand the effects the various options will have. You will certainly need a good ODBC reference to explain all the different options and values that can be used. Different driver versions support different options.\n\nBecause the effects may vary depending on the ODBC driver, use of this function in scripts to be made publicly available is strongly discouraged. Also, some ODBC options are not available to this function because they must be set before the connection is established or the query is prepared. However, if on a particular job it can make PHP work so your boss doesn't tell you to use a commercial product, that's all that really matters.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection|Odbc\\Result","Is a connection id or result id on which to change the settings. For SQLSetConnectOption(), this is a connection id. For SQLSetStmtOption(), this is a result id."],["$which","int","Is the ODBC function to use. The value should be 1 for SQLSetConnectOption() and 2 for SQLSetStmtOption()."],["$option","int","The option to set."],["$value","int","The value for the given <parameter>option<\/parameter>."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Retrieves special columns\n\nRetrieves either the optimal set of columns that uniquely identifies a row in the table, or columns that are automatically updated when any value in the row is updated by a transaction.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$type","int","When the type argument is <constant>SQL_BEST_ROWID<\/constant>, <function>odbc_specialcolumns<\/function> returns the column or columns that uniquely identify each row in the table.\n\nWhen the type argument is <constant>SQL_ROWVER<\/constant>, <function>odbc_specialcolumns<\/function> returns the column or columns in the specified table, if any, that are automatically updated by the data source when any value in the row is updated by any transaction."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$table","string","The table."],["$scope","int","The scope, which orders the result set. One of <constant>SQL_SCOPE_CURROW<\/constant>, <constant>SQL_SCOPE_TRANSACTION<\/constant> or <constant>SQL_SCOPE_SESSION<\/constant>."],["$nullable","int","Determines whether to return special columns that can have a NULL value. One of <constant>SQL_NO_NULLS<\/constant> or <constant>SQL_NULLABLE<\/constant>."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>SCOPE<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>DATA_TYPE<\/literal><literal>TYPE_NAME<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_SIZE<\/literal><literal>BUFFER_LENGTH<\/literal><literal>DECIMAL_DIGITS<\/literal><literal>PSEUDO_COLUMN<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>SCOPE<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_tables<\/function>"]]
["function","Retrieve statistics about a table\n\nGet statistics about a table and its indexes.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$table","string","The table name."],["$unique","int","The type of the index. One of <constant>SQL_INDEX_UNIQUE<\/constant> or <constant>SQL_INDEX_ALL<\/constant>."],["$accuracy","int","One of <constant>SQL_ENSURE<\/constant> or <constant>SQL_QUICK<\/constant>. The latter requests that the driver retrieve the <literal>CARDINALITY<\/literal> and <literal>PAGES<\/literal> only if they are readily available from the server."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>NON_UNIQUE<\/literal><literal>INDEX_QUALIFIER<\/literal><literal>INDEX_NAME<\/literal><literal>TYPE<\/literal><literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal><literal>COLUMN_NAME<\/literal><literal>ASC_OR_DESC<\/literal><literal>CARDINALITY<\/literal><literal>PAGES<\/literal><literal>FILTER_CONDITION<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>NON_UNIQUE<\/literal>, <literal>TYPE<\/literal>, <literal>INDEX_QUALIFIER<\/literal>, <literal>INDEX_NAME<\/literal> and <literal>ORDINAL_POSITION<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_tables<\/function>"]]
["function","Lists tables and the privileges associated with each table\n\nLists tables in the requested range and the privileges associated with each table.",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$table","string","The name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>GRANTOR<\/literal><literal>GRANTEE<\/literal><literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal><literal>IS_GRANTABLE<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal>, <literal>PRIVILEGE<\/literal> and <literal>GRANTEE<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_tables<\/function>"]]
["function","Get the list of table names stored in a specific data source\n\nLists all tables in the requested range.\n\nTo support enumeration of qualifiers, owners, and table types, the following special semantics for the <parameter>catalog<\/parameter>, <parameter>schema<\/parameter>, <parameter>table<\/parameter>, and <parameter>table_type<\/parameter> are available:  If <parameter>catalog<\/parameter> is a single percent character (%) and <parameter>schema<\/parameter> and <parameter>table<\/parameter> are empty strings, then the result set contains a list of valid qualifiers for the data source. (All columns except the TABLE_QUALIFIER column contain NULLs.)  If <parameter>schema<\/parameter> is a single percent character (%) and <parameter>catalog<\/parameter> and <parameter>table<\/parameter> are empty strings, then the result set contains a list of valid owners for the data source. (All columns except the TABLE_OWNER column contain NULLs.)  If <parameter>table_type<\/parameter> is a single percent character (%) and <parameter>catalog<\/parameter>, <parameter>schema<\/parameter> and <parameter>table<\/parameter> are empty strings, then the result set contains a list of valid table types for the data source. (All columns except the TABLE_TYPE column contain NULLs.) \n\nIf <parameter>catalog<\/parameter> is a single percent character (%) and <parameter>schema<\/parameter> and <parameter>table<\/parameter> are empty strings, then the result set contains a list of valid qualifiers for the data source. (All columns except the TABLE_QUALIFIER column contain NULLs.)\n\nIf <parameter>schema<\/parameter> is a single percent character (%) and <parameter>catalog<\/parameter> and <parameter>table<\/parameter> are empty strings, then the result set contains a list of valid owners for the data source. (All columns except the TABLE_OWNER column contain NULLs.)\n\nIf <parameter>table_type<\/parameter> is a single percent character (%) and <parameter>catalog<\/parameter>, <parameter>schema<\/parameter> and <parameter>table<\/parameter> are empty strings, then the result set contains a list of valid table types for the data source. (All columns except the TABLE_TYPE column contain NULLs.)",[["$odbc","Odbc\\Connection","The ODBC connection object, see <function>odbc_connect<\/function> for details."],["$catalog","string|null","The catalog ('qualifier' in ODBC 2 parlance)."],["$schema","string|null","The schema ('owner' in ODBC 2 parlance). This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$table","string|null","The name. This parameter accepts the following search patterns: <literal>%<\/literal> to match zero or more characters, and <literal>_<\/literal> to match a single character."],["$types","string|null","If <parameter>table_type<\/parameter> is not an empty string, it must contain a list of comma-separated values for the types of interest; each value may be enclosed in single quotes (<literal>'<\/literal>) or unquoted. For example, <literal>'TABLE','VIEW'<\/literal> or <literal>TABLE, VIEW<\/literal>. If the data source does not support a specified table type, <function>odbc_tables<\/function> does not return any results for that type."]],["Odbc\\Result|false","Returns an ODBC result object containing the information or <type>false<\/type> on failure.\n\nThe result set has the following columns: <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal><literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal><literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal><literal>TABLE_TYPE<\/literal><literal>REMARKS<\/literal> Drivers can report additional columns.\n\nThe result set is ordered by <literal>TABLE_TYPE<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_CAT<\/literal>, <literal>TABLE_SCHEM<\/literal> and <literal>TABLE_NAME<\/literal>."],["<function>odbc_tableprivileges<\/function>","<function>odbc_columns<\/function>","<function>odbc_specialcolumns<\/function>","<function>odbc_statistics<\/function>","<function>odbc_procedures<\/function>"]]
["function","Compiles and caches a PHP script without executing it\n\nThis function compiles a PHP script and adds it to the opcode cache without executing it. This can be used to prime the cache after a Web server restart by pre-caching files that will be included in later requests.",[["$filename","string","The path to the PHP script to be compiled."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if <parameter>filename<\/parameter> was compiled successfully or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>opcache_invalidate<\/function>"]]
["function","Get configuration information about the cache\n\nThis function returns configuration information about the cache instance",null,["array|false","Returns an array of information, including ini, blacklist and version"],["<function>opcache_get_status<\/function>"]]
["function","Get status information about the cache\n\nThis function returns state information about the in-memory cache instance. It will not return any information about the file cache.",[["$include_scripts","bool","Include script specific state information"]],["array|false","Returns an array of information, optionally containing script specific state information, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>opcache_get_configuration<\/function>"]]
["function","Invalidates a cached script\n\nThis function invalidates a particular script from the opcode cache. If <parameter>force<\/parameter> is unset or <type>false<\/type>, the script will only be invalidated if the modification time of the script is newer than the cached opcodes. If the opcache.file_cache directive is enabled, this function also invalidates the corresponding file cache entry.",[["$filename","string","The path to the script being invalidated."],["$force","bool","If set to <type>true<\/type>, the script will be invalidated regardless of whether invalidation is necessary."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the opcode cache for <parameter>filename<\/parameter> was invalidated or if there was nothing to invalidate, or <type>false<\/type> if the opcode cache is disabled."],["<function>opcache_compile_file<\/function>","<function>opcache_reset<\/function>"]]
["function","Tells whether a script is cached in OPCache\n\nThis function checks if a PHP script has been cached in OPCache. This can be used to more easily detect the \"warming\" of the cache for a particular script. This function only checks in-memory cache, not file cache. In order to check file cache, use <function>opcache_is_script_cached_in_file_cache<\/function>.",[["$filename","string","The path to the PHP script to be checked."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if <parameter>filename<\/parameter> is cached in OPCache in-memory cache, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."],["<function>opcache_compile_file<\/function>","<function>opcache_is_script_cached_in_file_cache<\/function>"]]
["function","Tells whether a script is cached in OPCache file cache\n\nThis function checks if a PHP script has been cached in OPCache. This can be used to more easily detect the \"warming\" of the cache for a particular script. This function only checks file cache, not in-memory cache. In order to check in-memory cache, use <function>opcache_is_script_cached<\/function>.",[["$filename","string","The path to the PHP script to be checked."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if <parameter>filename<\/parameter> is cached in OPCache, <type>false<\/type> otherwise."],["<function>opcache_compile_file<\/function>","<function>opcache_is_script_cached<\/function>"]]
["function","Blacklists a function from being JIT compiled\n\nThis function blacklists a particular function from being JIT compiled when Tracing JIT is in use. The function is specified using a <classname>Closure<\/classname>.\n\nAny parts of the function that were already JIT compiled remain unaffected and will still be JIT compiled.",[["$closure","Closure","The function to blacklist, represented as a first class callable. It is also possible to pass an anonymous function, in which case the anonymous function itself is blacklisted."]],["void","No value is returned."],["<function>opcache_invalidate<\/function>","<function>opcache_reset<\/function>"]]
["function","Resets the contents of the opcode cache\n\nThis function resets the entire opcode cache. After calling <function>opcache_reset<\/function>, all scripts will be reloaded and reparsed the next time they are hit. This function only resets in-memory cache, not the file cache.",null,["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> if the opcode cache was reset, or <type>false<\/type> if the opcode cache is disabled or the restart is pending or in progress (see <function>opcache_get_status<\/function>)."],["<function>opcache_invalidate<\/function>","<function>opcache_get_status<\/function>"]]
["function","Generate OpenAL buffer",null,["resource","Returns an Open AL(Buffer) resource on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_buffer_loadwav<\/function>","<function>openal_buffer_data<\/function>"]]
["function","Load a buffer with data",[["$buffer","resource","An Open AL(Buffer) resource (previously created by <function>openal_buffer_create<\/function>)."],["$format","int","Format of <parameter>data<\/parameter>, one of: <constant>AL_FORMAT_MONO8<\/constant>, <constant>AL_FORMAT_MONO16<\/constant>, <constant>AL_FORMAT_STEREO8<\/constant> and <constant>AL_FORMAT_STEREO16<\/constant>"],["$data","string","Block of binary audio data in the <parameter>format<\/parameter> and <parameter>freq<\/parameter> specified."],["$freq","int","Frequency of <parameter>data<\/parameter> given in Hz."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_buffer_loadwav<\/function>","<function>openal_stream<\/function>"]]
["function","Destroys an OpenAL buffer",[["$buffer","resource","An Open AL(Buffer) resource (previously created by <function>openal_buffer_create<\/function>)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_buffer_create<\/function>"]]
["function","Retrieve an OpenAL buffer property",[["$buffer","resource","An Open AL(Buffer) resource (previously created by <function>openal_buffer_create<\/function>)."],["$property","int","Specific property, one of: <constant>AL_FREQUENCY<\/constant>, <constant>AL_BITS<\/constant>, <constant>AL_CHANNELS<\/constant> and <constant>AL_SIZE<\/constant>."]],["int|false","Returns an integer value appropriate to the <parameter>property<\/parameter> requested or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_buffer_create<\/function>"]]
["function","Load a .wav file into a buffer",[["$buffer","resource","An Open AL(Buffer) resource (previously created by <function>openal_buffer_create<\/function>)."],["$wavfile","string","Path to .wav file on local file system."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_buffer_data<\/function>","<function>openal_stream<\/function>"]]
["function","Create an audio processing context",[["$device","resource","An Open AL(Device) resource (previously created by <function>openal_device_open<\/function>)."]],["resource","Returns an Open AL(Context) resource on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_device_open<\/function>","<function>openal_context_destroy<\/function>"]]
["function","Make the specified context current",[["$context","resource","An Open AL(Context) resource (previously created by <function>openal_context_create<\/function>)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_context_create<\/function>"]]
["function","Destroys a context",[["$context","resource","An Open AL(Context) resource (previously created by <function>openal_context_create<\/function>)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_context_create<\/function>"]]
["function","Process the specified context",[["$context","resource","An Open AL(Context) resource (previously created by <function>openal_context_create<\/function>)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_context_create<\/function>","<function>openal_context_current<\/function>","<function>openal_context_suspend<\/function>"]]
["function","Suspend the specified context",[["$context","resource","An Open AL(Context) resource (previously created by <function>openal_context_create<\/function>)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_context_create<\/function>","<function>openal_context_current<\/function>","<function>openal_context_process<\/function>"]]
["function","Close an OpenAL device",[["$device","resource","An Open AL(Device) resource (previously created by <function>openal_device_open<\/function>) to be closed."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>openal_device_open<\/function>"]]
