["function","Set password provider callback function\n\nSets password provider function. This function can ask for the password on a standard input (if PHP script is executed in a command line environment), display GUI dialog or provide password in any other possible ways. Requested passwords are used to encrypt or decrypt secret keys or perform symmetric encryption\/decryption operations.",[["$ffi","RnpFFI","The FFI object returned by <function>rnp_ffi_create<\/function>."],["$password_callback","callable",["The function that is to be called for every password request. It has the following signature: password_callback(<type>string<\/type> <parameter>key_fp<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>pgp_context<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>password<\/parameter>): <type>bool<\/type> <literal>$key_fp<\/literal> - The key fingerprint, if any. Can be empty.<literal>$pgp_context<\/literal> - String describing why the key is being requested.<literal>$password<\/literal> - Password string reference where provided password should be stored to. Callback function should return <type>true<\/type> if password was successfully set or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
