["function","(Preferred) Verify then decrypt with XChaCha20-Poly1305\n\nVerify then decrypt with ChaCha20-Poly1305 (eXtended-nonce variant).\n\nGenerally, XChaCha20-Poly1305 is the best of the provided AEAD modes to use.",[["$ciphertext","string","Must be in the format provided by <function>sodium_crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt<\/function> (ciphertext and tag, concatenated)."],["$additional_data","string","Additional, authenticated data. This is used in the verification of the authentication tag appended to the ciphertext, but it is not encrypted or stored in the ciphertext."],["$nonce","string","A number that must be only used once, per message. 24 bytes long. This is a large enough bound to generate randomly (i.e. <function>random_bytes<\/function>)."],["$key","string","Encryption key (256-bit)."]],["string|false","Returns the plaintext on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","(Preferred) Encrypt then authenticate with XChaCha20-Poly1305\n\nEncrypt then authenticate with XChaCha20-Poly1305 (eXtended-nonce variant).\n\nGenerally, XChaCha20-Poly1305 is the best of the provided AEAD modes to use.",[["$message","string","The plaintext message to encrypt."],["$additional_data","string","Additional, authenticated data. This is used in the verification of the authentication tag appended to the ciphertext, but it is not encrypted or stored in the ciphertext."],["$nonce","string","A number that must be only used once, per message. 24 bytes long. This is a large enough bound to generate randomly (i.e. <function>random_bytes<\/function>)."],["$key","string","Encryption key (256-bit)."]],["string","Returns the ciphertext and authentication tag as a string of raw binary bytes."]]
