["function","Compute a tag for the message\n\nSymmetric message authentication via <function>sodium_crypto_auth<\/function> provides integrity, but not confidentiality.\n\nUnlike with digital signatures (e.g. <function>sodium_crypto_sign_detached<\/function>), any party capable of verifying a message is also capable of authenticating their own messages. (Hence, symmetric authentication.)",[["$message","string","The message you intend to authenticate"],["$key","string","Authentication key"]],["string","Authentication tag"]]
["function","Generate a random key for sodium_crypto_auth\n\nGenerate a key for use with <function>sodium_crypto_auth<\/function> and <function>sodium_crypto_auth_verify<\/function>.",null,["string","Returns a 256-bit random key."]]
["function","Verifies that the tag is valid for the message\n\nVerify the authentication tag is valid for a given message and key.\n\nUnlike with digital signatures (e.g. <function>sodium_crypto_sign_verify_detached<\/function>), any party capable of verifying a message is also capable of authenticating their own messages. (Hence, symmetric authentication.)",[["$mac","string","Authentication tag produced by <function>sodium_crypto_auth<\/function>"],["$message","string","Message"],["$key","string","Authentication key"]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Authenticated public-key encryption\n\nEncrypt a message using asymmetric (public key) cryptography.\n\nThe algorithm used by functions prefixed with <function>sodium_crypto_box<\/function> are Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman over the Montgomery curve, Curve25519; usually abbreviated as X25519.",[["$message","string","The message to be encrypted."],["$nonce","string","A number that must be only used once, per message. 24 bytes long. This is a large enough bound to generate randomly (i.e. <function>random_bytes<\/function>)."],["$key_pair","string","See <function>sodium_crypto_box_keypair_from_secretkey_and_publickey<\/function>. This should include the sender's X25519 secret key and the recipient's X25519 public key."]],["string","Returns the encrypted message (ciphertext plus authentication tag). The ciphertext will be 16 bytes longer than the plaintext, and a raw binary string. See <function>sodium_bin2base64<\/function> for safe encoding for storage."]]
["function","Randomly generate a secret key and a corresponding public key\n\nGenerates a secret key and a public key as one string.\n\nTo get the secret key out of this unified keypair string, see <function>sodium_crypto_box_secretkey<\/function>. To get the public key out of this unified keypair string, see <function>sodium_crypto_box_publickey<\/function>.",null,["string","One string containing both the X25519 secret key and corresponding X25519 public key."]]
["function","Create a unified keypair string from a secret key and public key\n\nThis function exists to satisfy the API requirements of e.g. <function>crypto_box<\/function>. Pass in one party's secret key and the other's public key, and you will obtain a \"keypair\" for your conversation.",[["$secret_key","string","Secret key."],["$public_key","string","Public key."]],["string","X25519 Keypair."]]
["function","Authenticated public-key decryption\n\nDecrypt a message using asymmetric (public key) cryptography.",[["$ciphertext","string","The encrypted message to attempt to decrypt."],["$nonce","string","A number that must be only used once, per message. 24 bytes long. This is a large enough bound to generate randomly (i.e. <function>random_bytes<\/function>)."],["$key_pair","string","See <function>sodium_crypto_box_keypair_from_secretkey_and_publickey<\/function>. This should include the sender's public key and the recipient's secret key."]],["string|false","Returns the plaintext message on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Extract the public key from a crypto_box keypair\n\nGiven a keypair, fetch only the public key.",[["$key_pair","string","A keypair, such as one generated by <function>sodium_crypto_box_keypair<\/function> or <function>sodium_crypto_box_seed_keypair<\/function>"]],["string","X25519 public key."]]
["function","Calculate the public key from a secret key\n\nGiven a secret key, calculate the corresponding public key.\n\nThis only works with the type of keys intended for use with <function>crypto_box<\/function> (which uses Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman over the Montgomery curve, Curve25519; abbreviated as X25519), not <function>crypto_sign<\/function> (which uses Edwards Digital Signature Algorithm over the Edwards Curve with the corresponding parameters; abbreviated Ed25519).",[["$secret_key","string","X25519 secret key"]],["string","X25519 public key."]]
["function","Anonymous public-key encryption\n\nEncrypt a message such that only the recipient can decrypt it.\n\nUnlike with <function>sodium_crypto_box<\/function>, you only need to know the recipient's public key to use <function>sodium_crypto_box_seal<\/function>. One consequence of this convenience, however, is that the ciphertext isn't bound to a static public key, and is therefore not authenticated. Hence, anonymous public-key encryption.\n\n<function>sodium_crypto_box_seal<\/function> still provides ciphertext integrity. Just not sender identity authentication.\n\nIf you also need sender authentication, the <function>sodium_crypto_sign<\/function> functions are likely the best place to start.",[["$message","string","The message to encrypt."],["$public_key","string","The public key that corresponds to the only key that can decrypt the message."]],["string","A ciphertext string in the format of (one-time public key, encrypted message, authentication tag)."]]
["function","Anonymous public-key decryption\n\nDecrypt a message that was encrypted with <function>sodium_crypto_box_seal<\/function>",[["$ciphertext","string","The encrypted message"],["$key_pair","string","The keypair of the recipient. Must include the secret key."]],["string|false","The plaintext on success, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Extracts the secret key from a crypto_box keypair\n\nGiven a keypair, fetch only the secret key.",[["$key_pair","string","A keypair, such as one generated by <function>sodium_crypto_box_keypair<\/function> or <function>sodium_crypto_box_seed_keypair<\/function>"]],["string","X25519 secret key."]]
["function","Deterministically derive the key pair from a single key\n\nClamps the seed to form a secret key, derives the public key, and returns the two as a keypair.\n\nThe <literal>*_seed_keypair<\/literal> functions are ideal for generating a keypair from a password and salt. Use the result as a <parameter>seed<\/parameter> to generate the desired keys.",[["$seed","string","Some cryptographic input. Must be 32 bytes."]],["string","X25519 Keypair (secret key and public key)."]]
["function","Adds an element\n\nAdds an element <parameter>q<\/parameter> to <parameter>p<\/parameter>. Available as of libsodium 1.0.18.\n\nThis function is currently not documented; only its argument list is available.",[["$p","string","An element."],["$q","string","An element."]],["string","Returns a 32-byte random <type>string<\/type>."],["<function>sodium_crypto_core_ristretto255_random<\/function>","<function>sodium_crypto_core_ristretto255_sub<\/function>"]]
