["function","Return current Unix timestamp\n\nReturns the current time measured in the number of seconds since the Unix Epoch (January 1 1970 00:00:00 GMT).\n\nUnix timestamps do not contain any information with regards to any local timezone. It is recommended to use the <classname>DateTimeImmutable<\/classname> class for handling date and time information in order to avoid the pitfalls that come with just Unix timestamps.",null,["int","Returns the current timestamp."],["<classname>DateTimeImmutable<\/classname>","<function>date<\/function>","<function>microtime<\/function>"]]
