["function","Wraps a string to a given number of characters\n\nWraps a string to a given number of characters using a string break character. Strings wrap after a space (U+0020) character unless <parameter>cut_long_words<\/parameter> is set to <type>true<\/type>.",[["$string","string","The input string."],["$width","int","The number of characters at which the string will be wrapped."],["$break","string","The line is broken using the optional <parameter>break<\/parameter> parameter. It must not be an empty string."],["$cut_long_words","bool","If the <parameter>cut_long_words<\/parameter> is set to <type>true<\/type>, the string is always wrapped at or before the specified <parameter>width<\/parameter>. So if you have a word that is larger than the given width, it is broken apart. (See second example). When <type>false<\/type> the function does not split the word even if the <parameter>width<\/parameter> is smaller than the word width."]],["string","Returns the given string wrapped at the specified length."],["<function>nl2br<\/function>","<function>chunk_split<\/function>"]]
["function","Get an extended attribute\n\nThis function gets the value of an extended attribute of a file.\n\nExtended attributes have two different namespaces: user and root. The user namespace is available to all users, while the root namespace is available only to users with root privileges. xattr operates on the user namespace by default, but this can be changed with the <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter.",[["$filename","string","The file from which we get the attribute."],["$name","string","The name of the attribute."],["$flags","int",[{"type":"table","title":"Supported xattr flags","headers":[],"rows":[["<constant>XATTR_DONTFOLLOW<\/constant>","Do not follow the symbolic link but operate on symbolic link itself."],["<constant>XATTR_ROOT<\/constant>","Set attribute in root (trusted) namespace. Requires root privileges."]]}]]],["string|false","Returns a string containing the value or <type>false<\/type> if the attribute doesn't exist."],["<function>xattr_list<\/function>","<function>xattr_set<\/function>","<function>xattr_remove<\/function>"]]
["function","Get a list of extended attributes\n\nThis functions gets a list of names of extended attributes of a file.\n\nExtended attributes have two different namespaces: user and root. The user namespace is available to all users, while the root namespace is available only to users with root privileges. xattr operates on the user namespace by default, but this can be changed with the <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter.",[["$filename","string","The path of the file."],["$flags","int",[{"type":"table","title":"Supported xattr flags","headers":[],"rows":[["<constant>XATTR_DONTFOLLOW<\/constant>","Do not follow the symbolic link but operate on symbolic link itself."],["<constant>XATTR_ROOT<\/constant>","Set attribute in root (trusted) namespace. Requires root privileges."]]}]]],["array","This function returns an array with names of extended attributes."],["<function>xattr_get<\/function>"]]
["function","Remove an extended attribute\n\nThis function removes an extended attribute of a file.\n\nExtended attributes have two different namespaces: user and root. The user namespace is available to all users, while the root namespace is available only to users with root privileges. xattr operates on the user namespace by default, but this can be changed with the <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter.",[["$filename","string","The file from which we remove the attribute."],["$name","string","The name of the attribute to remove."],["$flags","int",[{"type":"table","title":"Supported xattr flags","headers":[],"rows":[["<constant>XATTR_DONTFOLLOW<\/constant>","Do not follow the symbolic link but operate on symbolic link itself."],["<constant>XATTR_ROOT<\/constant>","Set attribute in root (trusted) namespace. Requires root privileges."]]}]]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xattr_list<\/function>","<function>xattr_set<\/function>","<function>xattr_get<\/function>"]]
["function","Set an extended attribute\n\nThis function sets the value of an extended attribute of a file.\n\nExtended attributes have two different namespaces: user and root. The user namespace is available to all users, while the root namespace is available only to users with root privileges. xattr operates on the user namespace by default, but this can be changed with the <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter.",[["$filename","string","The file in which we set the attribute."],["$name","string","The name of the extended attribute. This attribute will be created if it doesn't exist or replaced otherwise. You can change this behaviour by using the <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter."],["$value","string","The value of the attribute."],["$flags","int",[{"type":"table","title":"Supported xattr flags","headers":[],"rows":[["<constant>XATTR_CREATE<\/constant>","Function will fail if extended attribute already exists."],["<constant>XATTR_REPLACE<\/constant>","Function will fail if extended attribute doesn't exist."],["<constant>XATTR_DONTFOLLOW<\/constant>","Do not follow the symbolic link but operate on symbolic link itself."],["<constant>XATTR_ROOT<\/constant>","Set attribute in root (trusted) namespace. Requires root privileges."]]}]]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xattr_get<\/function>","<function>xattr_remove<\/function>"]]
["function","Check if filesystem supports extended attributes\n\nThis functions checks if the filesystem holding the given file supports extended attributes. Read access to the file is required.",[["$filename","string","The path of the tested file."],["$flags","int",[{"type":"table","title":"Supported xattr flags","headers":[],"rows":[["<constant>XATTR_DONTFOLLOW<\/constant>","Do not follow the symbolic link but operate on symbolic link itself."]]}]]],["bool","This function returns <type>true<\/type> if filesystem supports extended attributes, <type>false<\/type> if it doesn't and <type>null<\/type> if it can't be determined (for example wrong path or lack of permissions to file)."],["<function>xattr_get<\/function>","<function>xattr_list<\/function>"]]
["function","Make binary diff of two files\n\nMakes a binary diff of two files and stores the result in a patch file. This function works with both text and binary files. Resulting patch file can be later applied using <function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>\/<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>.",[["$old_file","string","Path to the first file. This file acts as \"old\" file."],["$new_file","string","Path to the second file. This file acts as \"new\" file."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting patch file. Resulting file contains differences between \"old\" and \"new\" files. It is in binary format and is human-unreadable."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Read a size of file created by applying a binary diff\n\nReturns a size of a result file that would be created after applying binary patch from file <parameter>file<\/parameter> to the original file.",[["$file","string","The path to the binary patch created by <function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function> or <function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function> function."]],["int","Returns the size of file that would be created."],["<function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_file_rabdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Patch a file with a binary diff\n\nPatches a <parameter>file<\/parameter> with a binary <parameter>patch<\/parameter> and stores the result in a file <parameter>dest<\/parameter>. This function accepts patches created both via <function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function> and <function>xdiff_file_rabdiff<\/function> functions or their string counterparts.",[["$file","string","The original file."],["$patch","string","The binary patch file."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting file."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_file_rabdiff<\/function>"]]
["function","Make unified diff of two files\n\nMakes an unified diff containing differences between <parameter>old_file<\/parameter> and <parameter>new_file<\/parameter> and stores it in <parameter>dest<\/parameter> file. The resulting file is human-readable. An optional <parameter>context<\/parameter> parameter specifies how many lines of context should be added around each change. Setting <parameter>minimal<\/parameter> parameter to true will result in outputting the shortest patch file possible (can take a long time).",[["$old_file","string","Path to the first file. This file acts as \"old\" file."],["$new_file","string","Path to the second file. This file acts as \"new\" file."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting patch file."],["$context","int","Indicates how many lines of context you want to include in diff result."],["$minimal","bool","Set this parameter to <type>true<\/type> if you want to minimalize size of the result (can take a long time)."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_file_patch<\/function>"]]
["function","Alias of xdiff_file_bdiff\n\nMakes a binary diff of two files and stores the result in a patch file. This function works with both text and binary files. Resulting patch file can be later applied using <function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>.\n\nStarting with version 1.5.0 this function is an alias of <function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function>.",[["$old_file","string","Path to the first file. This file acts as \"old\" file."],["$new_file","string","Path to the second file. This file acts as \"new\" file."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting patch file. Resulting file contains differences between \"old\" and \"new\" files. It is in binary format and is human-unreadable."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Merge 3 files into one\n\nMerges three files into one and stores the result in a file <parameter>dest<\/parameter>. The <parameter>old_file<\/parameter> is an original version while <parameter>new_file1<\/parameter> and <parameter>new_file2<\/parameter> are modified versions of an original.",[["$old_file","string","Path to the first file. It acts as \"old\" file."],["$new_file1","string","Path to the second file. It acts as modified version of <parameter>old_file<\/parameter>."],["$new_file2","string","Path to the third file. It acts as modified version of <parameter>old_file<\/parameter>."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting file, containing merged changed from both <parameter>new_file1<\/parameter> and <parameter>new_file2<\/parameter>."]],["mixed","Returns <type>true<\/type> if merge was successful, string with rejected chunks if it was not or <type>false<\/type> if an internal error happened."],["<function>xdiff_string_merge3<\/function>"]]
["function","Patch a file with an unified diff\n\nPatches a <parameter>file<\/parameter> with a <parameter>patch<\/parameter> and stores the result in a file. <parameter>patch<\/parameter> has to be an unified diff created by <function>xdiff_file_diff<\/function>\/<function>xdiff_string_diff<\/function> function. An optional <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter specifies mode of operation.",[["$file","string","The original file."],["$patch","string","The unified patch file. It has to be created using <function>xdiff_string_diff<\/function>, <function>xdiff_file_diff<\/function> functions or compatible tools."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting file."],["$flags","int","Can be either <constant>XDIFF_PATCH_NORMAL<\/constant> (default mode, normal patch) or <constant>XDIFF_PATCH_REVERSE<\/constant> (reversed patch).\n\nStarting from version 1.5.0, you can also use binary OR to enable <constant>XDIFF_PATCH_IGNORESPACE<\/constant> flag."]],["mixed","Returns <type>false<\/type> if an internal error happened, string with rejected chunks if patch couldn't be applied or <type>true<\/type> if patch has been successfully applied."],["<function>xdiff_file_diff<\/function>"]]
["function","Alias of xdiff_file_bpatch\n\nPatches a <parameter>file<\/parameter> with a binary <parameter>patch<\/parameter> and stores the result in a file <parameter>dest<\/parameter>. This function accepts patches created both via <function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function> or <function>xdiff_file_rabdiff<\/function> functions or their string counterparts.\n\nStarting with version 1.5.0 this function is an alias of <function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>.",[["$file","string","The original file."],["$patch","string","The binary patch file."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting file."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_string_patch_binary<\/function>"]]
["function","Make binary diff of two files using the Rabin's polynomial fingerprinting algorithm\n\nMakes a binary diff of two files and stores the result in a patch file. The difference between this function and <function>xdiff_file_bdiff<\/function> is different algorithm used which should result in faster execution and smaller diff produced. This function works with both text and binary files. Resulting patch file can be later applied using <function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>\/<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>.\n\nFor more details about differences between algorithm used please check libxdiff website.",[["$old_file","string","Path to the first file. This file acts as \"old\" file."],["$new_file","string","Path to the second file. This file acts as \"new\" file."],["$dest","string","Path of the resulting patch file. Resulting file contains differences between \"old\" and \"new\" files. It is in binary format and is human-unreadable."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Make binary diff of two strings\n\nMakes a binary diff of two strings and returns the result. This function works with both text and binary data. Resulting patch can be later applied using <function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>\/<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>.",[["$old_data","string","First string with binary data. It acts as \"old\" data."],["$new_data","string","Second string with binary data. It acts as \"new\" data."]],["string","Returns string with binary diff containing differences between \"old\" and \"new\" data or <type>false<\/type> if an internal error occurred."],["<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Read a size of file created by applying a binary diff\n\nReturns a size of a result file that would be created after applying binary <parameter>patch<\/parameter> to the original file.",[["$patch","string","The binary patch created by <function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function> or <function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function> function."]],["int","Returns the size of file that would be created."],["<function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Patch a string with a binary diff\n\nPatches a string <parameter>str<\/parameter> with a binary <parameter>patch<\/parameter>. This function accepts patches created both via <function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function> and <function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function> functions or their file counterparts.",[["$str","string","The original binary string."],["$patch","string","The binary patch string."]],["string","Returns the patched string, or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function>"]]
["function","Make unified diff of two strings\n\nMakes an unified diff containing differences between <parameter>old_data<\/parameter> string and <parameter>new_data<\/parameter> string and returns it. The resulting diff is human-readable. An optional <parameter>context<\/parameter> parameter specifies how many lines of context should be added around each change. Setting <parameter>minimal<\/parameter> parameter to true will result in outputting the shortest patch file possible (can take a long time).",[["$old_data","string","First string with data. It acts as \"old\" data."],["$new_data","string","Second string with data. It acts as \"new\" data."],["$context","int","Indicates how many lines of context you want to include in the diff result."],["$minimal","bool","Set this parameter to <type>true<\/type> if you want to minimalize the size of the result (can take a long time)."]],["string","Returns string with resulting diff or <type>false<\/type> if an internal error happened."],["<function>xdiff_string_patch<\/function>"]]
["function","Alias of xdiff_string_bdiff\n\nMakes a binary diff of two strings and returns the result. This function works with both text and binary data. Resulting patch can be later applied using <function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>\/<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>.\n\nStarting with version 1.5.0 this function is an alias of <function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>.",[["$old_data","string","First string with binary data. It acts as \"old\" data."],["$new_data","string","Second string with binary data. It acts as \"new\" data."]],["string","Returns string with result or <type>false<\/type> if an internal error happened."],["<function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Merge 3 strings into one\n\nMerges three strings into one and returns the result. The <parameter>old_data<\/parameter> is an original version of data while <parameter>new_data1<\/parameter> and <parameter>new_data2<\/parameter> are modified versions of an original. An optional <parameter>error<\/parameter> is used to pass any rejected parts during merging process.",[["$old_data","string","First string with data. It acts as \"old\" data."],["$new_data1","string","Second string with data. It acts as modified version of <parameter>old_data<\/parameter>."],["$new_data2","string","Third string with data. It acts as modified version of <parameter>old_data<\/parameter>."],["$error","string","If provided then rejected parts are stored inside this variable."]],["mixed","Returns the merged string, <type>false<\/type> if an internal error happened, or <type>true<\/type> if merged string is empty."],["<function>xdiff_file_merge3<\/function>"]]
["function","Patch a string with an unified diff\n\nPatches a <parameter>str<\/parameter> string with an unified patch in <parameter>patch<\/parameter> parameter and returns the result. <parameter>patch<\/parameter> has to be an unified diff created by <function>xdiff_file_diff<\/function>\/<function>xdiff_string_diff<\/function> function. An optional <parameter>flags<\/parameter> parameter specifies mode of operation. Any rejected parts of the patch will be stored inside <parameter>error<\/parameter> variable if it is provided.",[["$str","string","The original string."],["$patch","string","The unified patch string. It has to be created using <function>xdiff_string_diff<\/function>, <function>xdiff_file_diff<\/function> functions or compatible tools."],["$flags","int","<parameter>flags<\/parameter> can be either <constant>XDIFF_PATCH_NORMAL<\/constant> (default mode, normal patch) or <constant>XDIFF_PATCH_REVERSE<\/constant> (reversed patch).\n\nStarting from version 1.5.0, you can also use binary OR to enable <constant>XDIFF_PATCH_IGNORESPACE<\/constant> flag."],["$error","string","If provided then rejected parts are stored inside this variable."]],["string","Returns the patched string, or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>xdiff_string_diff<\/function>"]]
["function","Alias of xdiff_string_bpatch\n\nPatches a string <parameter>str<\/parameter> with a binary <parameter>patch<\/parameter>. This function accepts patches created both via <function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function> and <function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function> functions or their file counterparts.\n\nStarting with version 1.5.0 this function is an alias of <function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>.",[["$str","string","The original binary string."],["$patch","string","The binary patch string."]],["string","Returns the patched string, or <type>false<\/type> on error."],["<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_rabdiff<\/function>"]]
["function","Make a binary diff of two strings using the Rabin's polynomial fingerprinting algorithm\n\nMakes a binary diff of two strings using the Rabin's polynomial fingerprinting algorithm implemented by libxdiff. Compared to <function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>, this algorithm generally produces smaller diffs and operates faster, while remaining fully compatible with <function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function> and <function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function> for applying patches.\n\nThis function can be used with both text and binary data. The resulting diff data can later be applied to recreate the new version from the old one.\n\nFor further information about the algorithm, see the libxdiff documentation.",[["$old_data","string","The first string containing the \"old\" binary data."],["$new_data","string","The second string containing the \"new\" binary data."]],["string|false","Returns a binary diff string containing the differences between the old and new data, or <type>false<\/type> on failure."],["<function>xdiff_string_bdiff<\/function>","<function>xdiff_string_bpatch<\/function>","<function>xdiff_file_bpatch<\/function>"]]
["function","Stops xhprof profiler\n\nStops the profiler, and returns xhprof data from the run.",null,["array|null","An <type>array<\/type> of xhprof data, from the run. Returns <type>null<\/type> if profiling is not enabled."]]
["function","Start xhprof profiler\n\nStart xhprof profiling.",[["$flags","int","Optional flags to add additional information to the profiling. See the XHprof constants for further information about these flags, e.g., <constant>XHPROF_FLAGS_MEMORY<\/constant> to enable memory profiling."],["$options","array","An <type>array<\/type> of optional options, namely, the 'ignored_functions' option to pass in functions to be ignored during profiling."]],["void","<type>null<\/type>"],["<function>xhprof_disable<\/function>","<function>xhprof_sample_enable<\/function>","<function>memory_get_usage<\/function>","<function>getrusage<\/function>"]]
["function","Stops xhprof sample profiler\n\nStops the sample mode xhprof profiler, and returns the profile info.",null,["array|null","An <type>array<\/type> of xhprof sample data, from the run. Returns <type>null<\/type> if profiling is not enabled."]]
["function","Start XHProf profiling in sampling mode\n\nStarts profiling in sample mode, which is a lighter weight version of <function>xhprof_enable<\/function>. The sampling interval is 0.1 seconds, and samples record the full function call stack. The main use case is when lower overhead is required when doing performance monitoring and diagnostics.",null,["void","<type>null<\/type>"],["<function>xhprof_sample_disable<\/function>","<function>xhprof_enable<\/function>","<function>memory_get_usage<\/function>","<function>getrusage<\/function>"]]
["function","Get XML parser error string\n\nGets the XML parser error string associated with the given <parameter>error_code<\/parameter>.",[["$error_code","int","An error code from <function>xml_get_error_code<\/function>."]],["string|null","Returns a string with a textual description of the error <parameter>error_code<\/parameter>, or <type>null<\/type> or <literal>\"Unknown\"<\/literal> if no description was found."],["<function>xml_get_error_code<\/function>"]]
["function","Get current byte index for an XML parser\n\nGets the current byte index of the given XML parser.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to get byte index from."]],["int","Returns which byte index the parser is currently at in its data buffer (starting at 0)."],["<function>xml_get_current_column_number<\/function>","<function>xml_get_current_line_number<\/function>"]]
["function","Get current column number for an XML parser\n\nGets the current column number of the given XML parser.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to get column number from."]],["int","Returns which column on the current line (as given by <function>xml_get_current_line_number<\/function>) the parser is currently at."],["<function>xml_get_current_byte_index<\/function>","<function>xml_get_current_line_number<\/function>"]]
["function","Get current line number for an XML parser\n\nGets the current line number for the given XML parser.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to get line number from."]],["int","Returns which line the parser is currently at in its data buffer."],["<function>xml_get_current_column_number<\/function>","<function>xml_get_current_byte_index<\/function>"]]
["function","Get XML parser error code\n\nGets the XML parser error code.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to get error code from."]],["int","Returns one of the error codes listed in the error codes section."],["<function>xml_error_string<\/function>"]]
["function","Start parsing an XML document\n\n<function>xml_parse<\/function> parses an XML document. The handlers for the configured events are called as many times as necessary.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to use."],["$data","string","Chunk of data to parse. A document may be parsed piece-wise by calling <function>xml_parse<\/function> several times with new data, as long as the <parameter>is_final<\/parameter> parameter is set and <type>true<\/type> when the last data is parsed."],["$is_final","bool","If set and <type>true<\/type>, <parameter>data<\/parameter> is the last piece of data sent in this parse."]],["int","Returns 1 on success or 0 on failure.\n\nFor unsuccessful parses, error information can be retrieved with <function>xml_get_error_code<\/function>, <function>xml_error_string<\/function>, <function>xml_get_current_line_number<\/function>, <function>xml_get_current_column_number<\/function> and <function>xml_get_current_byte_index<\/function>.\n\nSome errors (such as entity errors) are reported at the end of the data, thus only if <parameter>is_final<\/parameter> is set and <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Parse XML data into an array structure\n\nThis function parses an XML string into 2 parallel array structures, one (<parameter>index<\/parameter>) containing pointers to the location of the appropriate values in the <parameter>values<\/parameter> array. These last two parameters must be passed by reference.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser."],["$data","string","A string containing the XML data."],["$values","array","An array containing the values of the XML data"],["$index","array","An array containing pointers to the location of the appropriate values in the $values."]],["int|false","<function>xml_parse_into_struct<\/function> returns 0 for failure and 1 for success. This is not the same as <type>false<\/type> and <type>true<\/type>, be careful with operators such as ===."]]
["function","Create an XML parser\n\n<function>xml_parser_create<\/function> creates a new XML parser and returns a <classname>XMLParser<\/classname> instance to be used by the other XML functions.",[["$encoding","string|null","The input encoding is automatically detected, so that the <parameter>encoding<\/parameter> parameter specifies only the output encoding. If empty string is passed, the parser attempts to identify which encoding the document is encoded in by looking at the heading 3 or 4 bytes. The default output charset is UTF-8. The supported encodings are <literal>ISO-8859-1<\/literal>, <literal>UTF-8<\/literal> and <literal>US-ASCII<\/literal>."]],["XMLParser","Returns a new <classname>XMLParser<\/classname> instance."],["<function>xml_parser_create_ns<\/function>"]]
["function","Create an XML parser with namespace support\n\n<function>xml_parser_create_ns<\/function> creates a new XML parser with XML namespace support and returns a <classname>XMLParser<\/classname> instance to be used by the other XML functions.",[["$encoding","string|null","The input encoding is automatically detected, so that the <parameter>encoding<\/parameter> parameter specifies only the output encoding. The default output charset is UTF-8. The supported encodings are <literal>ISO-8859-1<\/literal>, <literal>UTF-8<\/literal> and <literal>US-ASCII<\/literal>."],["$separator","string","With a namespace aware parser tag parameters passed to the various handler functions will consist of namespace and tag name separated by the string specified in <parameter>separator<\/parameter>."]],["XMLParser","Returns a new <classname>XMLParser<\/classname> instance."],["<function>xml_parser_create<\/function>"]]
["function","Free an XML parser\n\nThis function has no effect. Prior to PHP 8.0.0, this function was used to close the resource.\n\nFrees the given XML <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.\n\nIn addition to calling <function>xml_parser_free<\/function> when the parsing is finished, prior to PHP 8.0.0, it was necessary to also explicitly unset the reference to <parameter>parser<\/parameter> to avoid memory leaks, if the parser resource is referenced from an object, and this object references that parser resource.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to free."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Get options from an XML parser\n\nGets an option value from an XML parser.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to get an option from."],["$option","int","Which option to fetch. <constant>XML_OPTION_CASE_FOLDING<\/constant>, <constant>XML_OPTION_PARSE_HUGE<\/constant>, <constant>XML_OPTION_SKIP_TAGSTART<\/constant>, <constant>XML_OPTION_SKIP_WHITE<\/constant> and <constant>XML_OPTION_TARGET_ENCODING<\/constant> are available. See <function>xml_parser_set_option<\/function> for their description."]],["string|int|bool","Returns the option's value."]]
["function","Set options in an XML parser\n\nSets an option in an XML parser.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to set an option in."],["$option","int",["Which option to set. See below.","The following options are available:",{"type":"table","title":"XML parser options","headers":["Option constant","Data type","Description"],"rows":[["<constant>XML_OPTION_CASE_FOLDING<\/constant>","bool","Controls whether case-folding is enabled for this XML parser. Enabled by default."],["<constant>XML_OPTION_PARSE_HUGE<\/constant>","bool","Allows parsing documents larger than 10 MB. This option should only be enabled when the document size is bounded because this could otherwise lead to a DoS. This option is only available when using libxml2."],["<constant>XML_OPTION_SKIP_TAGSTART<\/constant>","integer","Specify how many characters should be skipped in the beginning of a tag name."],["<constant>XML_OPTION_SKIP_WHITE<\/constant>","bool","Whether to skip values consisting of whitespace characters."],["<constant>XML_OPTION_TARGET_ENCODING<\/constant>","string","Sets which target encoding to use in this XML parser.By default, it is set to the same as the source encoding used by <function>xml_parser_create<\/function>. Supported target encodings are <literal>ISO-8859-1<\/literal>, <literal>US-ASCII<\/literal> and <literal>UTF-8<\/literal>."]]}]],["$value","string|int|bool","The option's new value."]],["bool","Returns <type>true<\/type> on success or <type>false<\/type> on failure."]]
["function","Set up character data handler\n\nSets the character data handler function for the XML parser <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.",[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>data<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>data<\/parameter> — Character data as a string.","Character data handler is called for every piece of a text in the XML document. It can be called multiple times inside each fragment (e.g. for non-ASCII strings)."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Set up default handler\n\nSets the default handler function for the XML parser <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.",[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>data<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>data<\/parameter> — <parameter>data<\/parameter> contains the character data. This may be the XML declaration, document type declaration, entities or other data for which no other handler exists."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Set up start and end element handlers\n\nSets the element handler functions for the XML <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.\n\n<parameter>start_handler<\/parameter> is called when a new XML element is opened. <parameter>end_handler<\/parameter> is called when an XML element is closed.",[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$start_handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: start_element_handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>name<\/parameter>, <type>array<\/type> <parameter>attributes<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>name<\/parameter> — Contains the name of the element for which this handler is called. If case-folding is in effect for this parser, the element name will be in uppercase letters. <parameter>attributes<\/parameter> — An associative array with the element's attributes. The array is empty if the element has no attributes. The keys of this array are the attribute names, the values are the attribute values. Attribute names are case-folded on the same criteria as element names. Attribute values are not case-folded. The order in which <parameter>attributes<\/parameter> is traversed is identical to the order in which the attributes were declared."]],["$end_handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: end_element_handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>name<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>name<\/parameter> — Contains the name of the element for which this handler is called. If case-folding is in effect for this parser, the element name will be in uppercase letters."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Set up end namespace declaration handler\n\nSet a handler to be called when leaving the scope of a namespace declaration. This will be called, for each namespace declaration, after the handler for the end tag of the element in which the namespace was declared.\n\nThis event is not supported under libXML, so a registered handler wouldn't be called.",[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>prefix<\/parameter>): <type>mixed<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>prefix<\/parameter> — The prefix is a string used to reference the namespace within an XML object. <type>false<\/type> if no prefix exists."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."],["<function>xml_set_start_namespace_decl_handler<\/function>"]]
["function","Set up external entity reference handler\n\nSets the external entity reference handler function for the XML parser <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.",[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>open_entity_names<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>base<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>system_id<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>public_id<\/parameter>): <type>bool<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>open_entity_names<\/parameter> — A space-separated list of the names of the entities that are open for the parse of this entity (including the name of the referenced entity). <parameter>base<\/parameter> — This is the base for resolving the system identifier (<parameter>system_id<\/parameter>) of the external entity. <parameter>system_id<\/parameter> — The system identifier as specified in the entity declaration. <parameter>public_id<\/parameter> — The public identifier as specified in the entity declaration, or an empty string if none was specified; the whitespace in the public identifier will have been normalized as required by the XML spec.","The handler should return <type>true<\/type> if the entity was handled, <type>false<\/type> otherwise. When returning <type>false<\/type> the XML parser will stop parsing and <function>xml_get_error_code<\/function> will return <constant>XML_ERROR_EXTERNAL_ENTITY_HANDLING<\/constant>."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function",["Set up notation declaration handler","Sets the notation declaration handler function for the XML parser <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.","A notation declaration is part of the document's DTD and has the following format:",{"type":"code","text":"<!NOTATION <parameter>name<\/parameter>\n{ <parameter>systemId<\/parameter> | <parameter>publicId<\/parameter>?>","role":"xml"},"See section 4.7 of the XML 1.0 spec for the definition of notation declarations."],[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>notation_name<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>base<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>system_id<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>public_id<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>notation_name<\/parameter> — This is the notation's name, as per the notation format described above. <parameter>base<\/parameter> — This is the base for resolving the system identifier (<literal>system_id<\/literal>) of the notation declaration. <parameter>system_id<\/parameter> — System identifier of the external notation declaration. <parameter>public_id<\/parameter> — Public identifier of the external notation declaration."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Use XML Parser within an object\n\nThis function allows to use <parameter>parser<\/parameter> inside <parameter>object<\/parameter>. All callback functions could be set with <function>xml_set_element_handler<\/function> etc and assumed to be methods of <parameter>object<\/parameter>.",[["$parser","XMLParser","A reference to the XML parser to use inside the object."],["$object","object","The object where to use the XML parser."]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function",["Set up processing instruction (PI) handler","Sets the processing instruction (PI) handler function for the XML parser <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.","A processing instruction has the following format:",{"type":"code","text":"<?target\ndata\n?>","role":"xml"},"PHP code is delimited by the <literal><?php<\/literal> processing instruction. As such it is possible to have PHP code within an XML document. However, the PI end tag (<literal>?><\/literal>) must not be part of the data. If a PI end tag exists as part of the embedded PHP code, the rest of the PHP code and the \"real\" PI end tag, will be treated as character data."],[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>target<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>data<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>target<\/parameter> — The processing instruction target. <parameter>data<\/parameter> — The processing instruction data."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
["function","Set up start namespace declaration handler\n\nSet a handler to be called when a namespace is declared. Namespace declarations occur inside start tags. But the namespace declaration start handler is called before the start tag handler for each namespace declared in that start tag.",[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>prefix<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>uri<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>prefix<\/parameter> — The prefix is a string used to reference the namespace within an XML object. <type>false<\/type> if no prefix exists. <parameter>uri<\/parameter> — Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) of namespace."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."],["<function>xml_set_end_namespace_decl_handler<\/function>"]]
["function",["Set up unparsed entity declaration handler","Sets the unparsed entity declaration handler function for the XML parser <parameter>parser<\/parameter>.","The <parameter>handler<\/parameter> will be called if the XML parser encounters an external entity declaration with an NDATA declaration, like the following:",{"type":"code","text":"<!ENTITY <parameter>name<\/parameter> {<parameter>publicId<\/parameter> | <parameter>systemId<\/parameter>}\n        NDATA <parameter>notationName<\/parameter>","role":"xml"},"See section 4.2.2 of the XML 1.0 spec for the definition of notation declared external entities."],[["$parser","XMLParser","The XML parser."],["$handler","callable|string|null",["If <type>null<\/type> is passed, the handler is reset to its default state.  An empty string will also reset the handler, however this is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>callable<\/type>, the callable is set as the handler.","If <parameter>handler<\/parameter> is a <type>string<\/type>, it can be the name of a method of an object set with <function>xml_set_object<\/function>.  This is deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0. ","As of PHP 8.4.0, the callable is checked to be valid while setting the handler, not when it is called. This means that <function>xml_set_object<\/function> must be called prior to setting a method string as the callback. However, as this behaviour is also deprecated as of PHP 8.4.0, using a proper <type>callable<\/type> for the method is recommended instead.","The signature of the handler must be: handler(<type>XMLParser<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>entity_name<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>base<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type> <parameter>system_id<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>public_id<\/parameter>, <type>string<\/type>|<type>false<\/type> <parameter>notation_name<\/parameter>): <type>void<\/type> <parameter>parser<\/parameter> — The XML parser calling the handler. <parameter>entity_name<\/parameter> — The name of the entity that is about to be defined. <parameter>base<\/parameter> — This is the base for resolving the system identifier (<parameter>systemId<\/parameter>) of the external entity. <parameter>system_id<\/parameter> — System identifier for the external entity. <parameter>public_id<\/parameter> — Public identifier for the external entity. <parameter>notation_name<\/parameter> — Name of the notation of this entity (see <function>xml_set_notation_decl_handler<\/function>)."]]],["true","Always returns <type>true<\/type>."]]
