["function","Calls callbacks for pending operations\n\nThe <function>zookeeper_dispatch<\/function> function calls the callbacks passed by operations like Zookeeper::get or Zookeeper::exists.\n\nSince version 0.4.0, this function must be called manually to achieve asynchronous operations. If you want that to be done automatically, you also can declare ticks at the beginning of your program.\n\nAfter PHP 7.1, you can ignore this function. This extension uses EG(vm_interrupt) to implement async dispatch.",null,["void","No value is returned."],["Zookeeper::addAuth","Zookeeper::connect","Zookeeper::__construct","Zookeeper::exists","Zookeeper::get","Zookeeper::getChildren","Zookeeper::setWatcher"]]
